{"name":"Kinetic Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can make a ranged spell attack against a target within 120 feet of you. On a hit, you deal your kinetic shape die + CHA modifier damage of your chosen element's type.</p><p>The amount of the damage for both shapes increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Kinetic Shape column of the Kineticist table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":120,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"rsak","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.kineticist.kinetic-shape + @abilities.cha.mod",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/trail-streak-impact-blue.webp","_id":"s000479517ba616f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Treachery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emanate an aura of discord, which gives you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Cull the Herd.</strong> You have Advantage on melee Attack Rolls against any creature that has one or more of its allies within 5 feet of it.</p><p><strong>Treacherous Strike.</strong> If a creature within 5 feet of you misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to force the attacker to reroll that attack against a creature of your choice that is also within 5 feet of the attacker. The ability fails and is wasted if the attacker is Immune to being Charmed.</p><p>You can use this ability three times. You regain one expended use on a Short Rest and all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s00376f7e0347bb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystical Connection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You now have the ability to nudge which spirits of Spirits from Beyond you channel. Whenever you roll on the Spirits from Beyond table, you can roll the die twice and choose which of the two effects to bestow. If you roll the same number on both dice, you can ignore the number and choose any effect on the table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s00a602175247ae6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persistent Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can remain shifted for an indefinite amount of time and your Formshift does not end when you are asleep naturally. You can still end your Formshift as usual.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s00f2abee427e70f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel divine energy directly from the Outer Planes to fuel magical effects. You start with three such effects: Divine Spark, Turn Undead and Harness Divine Power, each of which is described below. Each time you use this class's Channel Divinity, choose which Channel Divinity effect from this class to create. You gain additional effect options at higher Cleric levels.</p><p>You can use this class's Channel Divinity twice. You regain one of its expended uses when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You gain additional uses when you reach certain Cleric levels, as shown in the Channel Divinity column of the Cleric Features table.</p><p>If a Channel Divinity effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals the spell save DC from this class's Spellcasting feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-smoke-yellow.webp","_id":"s01927a5b2b8476a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alert Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-teal.webp","_id":"s01ea25559aa7d03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limited Wish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You entreat your patron to grant you a small wish. As an Action, you can speak your desire to your Genie's Vessel, requesting the effect of one spell that is 7th level or lower and has a casting time of 1 action. The spell can be from any class's spell list, and you don't need to meet the requirements in that spell, including costly components; the spell simply takes effect as part of this action.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s020da4c5f20f0d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamagic (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional metamagic options.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-colllecting-energy-green.webp","_id":"s0227f8a89668bc2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contagious Curse","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If the target of Bestow Curse drops to 0 hit points before the end of their duration, you can take a Bonus Action to move the curse to a new creature you can see within range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s022a39f0774363f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a special kind of Blindsight with a radius of 120 feet. This Blindsight only functions against creatures with blood.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s02c014b27c67eea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fiendish Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to fire damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s031f75d239ba6ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Esoteric Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one feat of your choice. You ignore all race, class, and level prerequisites the feat normally has. You do not, however, gain any features that the feat might depend on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s04410ee8d161204","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can communicate with other beasts as if you were sharing the same language.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rodent-rat-green.webp","_id":"s04816d63157d3a0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Hate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The paladin, as well any fiends and undead within 10 feet of the paladin, gains a bonus to melee weapon damage rolls equal to the paladin's Charisma modifier (minimum of +1). A creature can benefit from this feature from only one paladin at a time.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s04d3197bfdc1aec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trance of Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to align your consciousness to the endless calculations of Mechanus. As a Bonus Action, you can enter this state for 1 minute. For the duration, Attack Rolls against you can't benefit from Advantage, and whenever you make an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can treat a roll of 9 or lower on the d20 as a 10.</p><p>Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s050271db2c6a87f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mask of the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attempt to hide even when you're only lightly obscured by foliage, heavy rain, falling snow, mist, and other natural phenomena.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-beast-eyes-green.webp","_id":"s05176d3f734b39b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Cannon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to create a magical cannon. Using woodcarver's tools or weaponsmith's tools, you can take an Action to magically create a Small or Tiny eldritch cannon in an unoccupied space on a horizontal surface within 5 feet of you. A Small eldritch cannon occupies its space, and a Tiny one can be held in one hand.</p><p>Once you create a cannon, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or until you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. You can have only one cannon at a time and can't create one while your cannon is present.</p><p>The cannon is a magical object. Regardless of size, the cannon has an AC of 18 and a number of hit points equal to five times your artificer level. It is Immune to poison damage and psychic damage, and all conditions. If it is forced to make an Ability Check or a Saving Throw, treat all its ability scores as 10 (+0). If the Mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. It disappears if it is reduced to 0 hit points or after 1 hour. You can dismiss it early as an Action.</p><p>When you create the cannon, you determine its appearance and whether it has legs. You also decide which type it is, choosing from the options on the Eldritch Cannons table. On each of your turns, when you take your Action, you can cause the cannon to activate if you are within 60 feet of it and fire at the closest hostile creature. Alternatively, you can use your Bonus Action to designate the target creature manually. As part of the same Bonus Action, you can direct the cannon to walk or climb up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space, provided it has legs.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Eldritch Cannons</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Cannon</th><th scope=\"col\">Activation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Flamethrower</td><td>The cannon exhales fire in an adjacent 15-foot cone that you designate. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d8 fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.</td></tr><tr><td>Force Ballista</td><td>Make a ranged spell attack, originating from the cannon, at one creature or object within 120 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 force damage, and if the target is a creature, it is pushed up to 5 feet away from the cannon.</td></tr><tr><td>Protector</td><td>The cannon emits a burst of positive energy that grants itself and each creature of your choice within 10 feet of it a number of temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/artillery/cannon-engraved.webp","_id":"s0518e598d87fbfc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Overcharge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast a spell gained through an elemental discipline as a 9th level spell, without expending any additional ki points.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s053f60e46b055dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Misty Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can slip in and out of the Feywild to move in a blink of an eye: you can cast Misty Step without expending a spell slot. You can do so a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, whenever you cast Misty Step, you can bring along one willing creature you can see within 5 feet of you. That creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice within 5 feet of your destination space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s054cb80103d9e38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Survival Instincts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>2nd-level barbarian feature (replaces Danger Sense)</p><p>You become proficient in your choice of two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, Perception, or Survival.</p><p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses either of those skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-green.webp","_id":"s057dff95df6049f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contact Patron","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>In the past, you usually contacted your patron through intermediaries. Now you can communicate directly; you always have the Contact Other Plane spell prepared. With this feature, you can cast the spell without expending a spell slot to contact your patron, and you automatically succeed on the spell's saving throw.</p><p>Once you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so in this way again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-light-fire-blue.webp","_id":"s05861cbf09e5922","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic in the Blood","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Arcana check, you can use your Charisma in place of your Intelligence for it.</p><p>Additionally, you learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the Sorcerer or Wizard spell list. A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Sorcerer Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s05a2ae1480e2291","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Restoration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose to recover sorcery points equal to half your sorcerer level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a short rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/orb-water-ice-pink.webp","_id":"s05eb11a32e89a4f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Zephyr Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are hit by an attack, you can use your Reaction to make a Dexterity (Acrobatics) check and subtract the result of the roll from the damage taken.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Dexterity modifier and you can regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s060a0ec76ef7650","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legendary Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can choose one ally within 60 feet of you that can see or hear you. That ally gains an additional action on their next turn. Alternatively, the target can take its Reaction to use this action immediately.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-quintuple-orange.webp","_id":"s060ffff573b777c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Secrets","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two spells of your choice from any class. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Wizard table, or a cantrip. The chosen spells count as wizard spells for you and don't count against the number of wizard spells you can prepare.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s062dadd5d87444d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with alchemist's supplies. If you already have this Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"s065645ec4080237","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Exceptional Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Bonus Action to give magically allow your companion to act more swiftly. On its next turn, it can use its Bonus Action to use the Dash, Disengage, Dodge, or Help action (your choice).</p><p>Additionally, your companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0677e522440aa53","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Silent Flight.</strong> While flying, you can hide as a Bonus Action and your wings cause no sound when you move while flying. If you attack while hidden, the benefits of being hidden persist against the target of your attack until the end of your turn.</li><li><strong>On Swift Wings.</strong> When you move, you can choose a creature that is within 5 ft and at least one size smaller than you and move the creature with you until the end of the current turn. The creature's movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Deadly Talons.</strong> The critical range with your natural weapons increases by 1. When you critically hit with your natural weapons, you roll your weapon damage dice two additional times and add them to the damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0681b7c68d81b49","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Item Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attune to up to six magic items at once.</p><p>Additionally, you ignore all class, race, spell, and level requirements on attuning to or using a magic item.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s068ef35a37d80b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Arcane Jolt and steel defender become more powerful:</p><ul><li>The extra damage and the healing of your Arcane Jolt both increase to 4d6.</li><li>Your steel defender gains a +2 bonus to Armor Class.</li><li>Whenever your steel defender uses its Deflect Attack, the attacker takes force damage equal to 1d4 + your Intelligence modifier.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-stone-earth-gray.webp","_id":"s06cb478285be37a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Studied Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You masterfully study your opponents and learn from each attack you make. If you make an Attack Roll against a creature and miss, you have Advantage on your next Attack Roll against that creature before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strikes-sword-triple-gray.webp","_id":"s070811f45d6cef6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fathomless Plunge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically open temporary conduits to watery destinations. As an Action, you can teleport yourself and up to five other willing creatures that you can see within 30 feet of you. Amid a whirl of tentacles, you all vanish and then reappear in a body of water (pond size or larger) you've seen in the same plane of existence as you or within 30 feet of it, each of you appearing in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of the others.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0718704ccf7f426","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel the souls of your ancestors into your physical form. When you start casting a sorcerer spell on your turn and expend a spell slot, you can increase your size by one category—from Medium to Large, for example.</p><p>This increase lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you die or are Incapacitated. Until it ends, you enjoy the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your current hit points and your hit point maximum both increase by 1 per sorcerer level.</li><li>Your reach increases by 5 feet.</li><li>Your Speed increases by 5 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</li><li>If you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can shove or grapple that creature as part of the same attack.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you spend 4 sorcery points to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s071b60fa6b0fcc9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mushroom Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following additional options for your Magic Mushrooms:</p><p><strong>Boom Shroom.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. They take force damage equal to 1d6 x your Proficiency on a failure, and half as much on a success.</p><p><strong>Madcap.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make an Intelligence Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Confused until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p><strong>Waxy Webber.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make an Strength Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Restrained until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p>Additionally, you regain one use of Magic Mushrooms when you roll Initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s072ac0d25d35d20","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hurl Through Hell","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll, you can try to instantly transport the target through the Lower Planes. The target must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or the target disappears and hurtles through a nightmare landscape. The target takes 10d10 Psychic damage if it isn't a Fiend, and it has the Incapacitated condition until the end of your next turn, when it returns to the space it previously occupied or the nearest unoccupied space.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-fire-orange.webp","_id":"s074545e72a450c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage or it fails its Saving Throw against such a spell, it also suffers the Lacerated condition for 1 minute. If the spell natively causes them to become Lacerated, the damage they take from the condition increases by an amount equal to your Proficiency.</p><p>At the end of their turns, they can make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC to end the condition.</p><p>They do not make this Saving Throw if the spell triggering this effect is still affecting them and allows for repeat Saving Throws on subsequent turns. In such a case, the Lacerated condition instead ends when they succeed on the repeat Saving Throw for that spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0822964e3cb499c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fanatical Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine power that fuels your rage can protect you. If you fail a Saving Throw while you're raging, you can reroll it and take the highest. You can use this ability only once per rage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s099008b0a3da981","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Turn Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you present your Holy Symbol and censure Undead creatures. Each Undead of your choice within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. If the creature fails its save, it has the Frightened and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute. For that duration, it tries to move as far from you as it can on its turns. This effect ends early on the creature if it takes any damage, if you have the Incapacitated condition, or if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":30,"width":null,"units":"ft","type":"sphere"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"self"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"wis","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-creature-skeleton.webp","_id":"s0a228ebff50d571","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Transmuter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to consume the reserve of transmutation magic stored within your transmuter's stone in a single burst. Once per Long Rest when you do so, choose one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>Major Transformation.</strong> You can transmute one nonmagical object—no larger than a 5-foot cube—into another nonmagical object of similar size and mass and of equal or lesser value. You must spend 10 minutes handling the object to transform it.</p><p><strong>Panacea.</strong> You remove all curses, diseases, and poisons affecting a creature that you touch with the transmuter's stone. The creature also regains all its hit points.</p><p><strong>Restore Life.</strong> You cast the Raise Dead spell on a creature you touch with the transmuter's stone, without expending a spell slot and without providing any components.</p><p><strong>Restore Youth.</strong> You touch the transmuter's stone to a willing creature, and that creature's apparent age is reduced by 3d10 years, to a minimum of 13 years. This effect doesn't extend the creature's lifespan and can be used no more than once on the same creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a292020644b1e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unfailing Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your inspiring words are so persuasive that others feel driven to succeed. When a creature adds one of your Bardic Inspiration dice to its Ability Check, Attack Roll, or Saving Throw and the roll fails, the creature can keep the Bardic Inspiration die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a36878a8c67451","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Discerning Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against Illusions and skill checks to identify illusions.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-red.webp","_id":"s0a62dd0c5af108f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hidden Paths","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the hidden, magical pathways that some fey use to traverse space in the blink of an eye. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, you can use your action to teleport one willing creature you touch up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0a7172b99471511","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Juggernaut","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation. As a result, the extra damage you deal with the Giant's Might feature increases to 1d10. Moreover, when you use that feature, your size can increase to Huge, and while you are that size, your reach increases by 5 feet.</p><p>Additionally, you now regain the use of your Giant's Might feature on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0aad9312264fbc8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Born Predator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a +2 bonus to initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp","_id":"s0abad6bac75976a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blackguard's Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to slip away from your foes. Immediately after you are hit by an attack, you can use your Reaction to turn Invisible and teleport up to 60 feet to a spot you can see. You remain Invisible until the end of your next turn or until you attack, deal damage, or force a creature to make a Saving Throw. Once you use this feature, you must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b127c0b2bed5ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage caused by your Gathered Swarm counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b1ba56e6ddf4dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Knight Conclave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0b333d0c5069564","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hearth of Moonlight and Shadow","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Home can be wherever you are. During a Short or a Long Rest, you can invoke the shadowy power of the Gloaming Court to help guard your respite. At the start of the rest, you touch a point in space, and an invisible, 30-foot-radius sphere of magic appears, centered on that point. Total cover blocks the sphere.</p><p>While within the sphere, you and your allies gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) and Wisdom (Perception) checks, and any light from open flames in the sphere (a campfire, torches, or the like) isn't visible outside it.</p><p>The sphere vanishes at the end of the rest or when you leave the sphere.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0be7c0f3d82c600","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Eldritch Invocation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0bf0f67500d8ac3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Accursed Magicks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to blend hemocraft and profane magic together, using one pool of dark power to feed the other. You gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p><p>Additionally, you can expend uses of your Blood Maledict to cast Warlock spells and Pact Magic spell slots to use Blood Curses as per the table below. This feature allows you to cast Pact Magic spells at a lower level than you currently have access to, but not higher. If you use a Blood Curse by expending a Pact Magic spell slot, any excess uses generated are regained instead. If you amplify a Blood Curse used in this manner, you do not roll separately for the hit point cost and gain, they nullify each other at a 1:1 ratio.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Accursed Magick Conversion</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Pact Magic Spell Slot</th><th scope=\"col\">Blood Maledict Cost/Regain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>1 use</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>1 use + hit point cost for amplifying 1 blood curse</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>2 uses</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>2 uses + hit point cost for amplifying 2 blood curses</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0c02ed5f498581f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Diamond Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ki grants you Proficiency in all Saving Throws.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you make a Saving Throw and fail, you can spend 1 ki point to reroll it and take the second result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make a Saving Throw and fail"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-icecicle.webp","_id":"s0c3b2a713ad67f9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unleash the Kraken","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call upon your patron for aid. As an Action, you open a portal at a point you can see within 30 ft. of you and choose one of the following effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0c9ffa915bd5251","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Warding Flare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You regain all expended uses of your Warding Flare when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, whenever you use Warding Flare, you can give the target of the triggering attack a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to 2d6 plus your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0cd2043d29f1d7d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Searing Vengeance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or an ally within 60 feet of you is about to make a Death Saving Throw, you can unleash radiant energy to save the creature. The creature regains Hit Points equal to half its Hit Point maximum and can end the Prone condition on itself. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of the creature takes Radiant damage equal to 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier, and each has the Blinded condition until the end of the current turn.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0cdb6d2c11c7dfd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Event Horizon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically emit a powerful field of gravitational energy that tugs at other creatures for up to 1 minute or until your Concentration ends (as if you were concentrating on a spell). For the duration, whenever a creature hostile to you starts its turn within 60 feet of you, it must make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, it takes 4d10 + Intelligence modifier force damage, and its Speed is reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage, and every foot it moves this turn costs 2 extra feet of movement.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest or until you expend a spell slot of 5th level or higher to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0d0b96757d9f8c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two of your elemental disciplines and reduce their ki cost by 1 (minimum of 1). You change your choices whenever you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0d3f435f9a9cb2c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Favored by the Gods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Divine power guards your destiny. If you fail a Saving Throw or miss with an Attack Roll, you can roll 2d4 and add it to the total, possibly changing the outcome. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you use 2 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0db509dcb1bf81c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cantrip","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know one cantrip of your choice from the cleric, wizard, or sorcerer spell list. Your spellcasting ability for it is INT, WIS, or CHA (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cross-circle-blue.webp","_id":"s0db7d30ec741370","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Misty Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast Misty Step as a Reaction in response to taking damage.</p><p>In addition, the following effects are now among your Steps of the Fey options.</p><p><strong>Disappearing Step.</strong> You have the Invisible condition until the start of your next turn or until immediately after you make an Attack Roll, deal damage, or cast a spell.</p><p><strong>Dreadful Step.</strong> Creatures within 5 feet of the space you left or the space you appear in (your choice) must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take 2d10 Psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0ddbebedea1e9bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0df69ec9052bbb3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a style of fighting as your specialty. Choose one of the following options. You can't take a Fighting Style option more than once, even if you later get to choose again.</p><h5>Archery</h5><p>You gain a +2 bonus to Attack Rolls you make with ranged weapons.</p><h5>Close Quarters Shooter</h5><p>When making a ranged weapon attack while you are within 5 feet of a hostile creature, you do not have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. Your ranged weapon attacks ignore half cover and three-quarters cover against targets within 30 feet of you. You have a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls on ranged weapon attacks.</p><h5>Defense</h5><p>While you are wearing armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Dueling</h5><p>When you are wielding a melee weapon in one hand and no other weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with that weapon.</p><h5>Great Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.</p><h5>Mariner</h5><p>As long as you are not wearing heavy armor or using a shield, you have a Swim Speed and a Climb Speed equal to your normal Speed, and you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</p><h5>Protection</h5><p>When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. You must be wielding a shield.</p><h5>Two-Weapon Fighting</h5><p>When you engage in two-weapon fighting, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of the second attack.</p><h5>Superior Technique</h5><p>You learn one maneuver of your choice from among those available to the fighter archetype. If a maneuver you use requires your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects, the Saving Throw DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice).</p><p>You gain one superiority die, which is a d6 (this die is added to any superiority dice you have from another source). This die is used to fuel your maneuvers. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Blind Fighting</h5><p>You have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</p><h5>Interception</h5><p>When a creature you can see hits a target, other than you, within 5 feet of you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to reduce the damage the target takes by 1d10 + your Proficiency bonus (to a minimum of 0 damage). You must be wielding a shield or a simple or martial weapon to use this Reaction.</p><h5>Thrown Weapon Fighting</h5><p>You can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.</p><p>In addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll.</p><h5>Unarmed Fighting</h5><p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-daggers-orange.webp","_id":"s0e8d1361f0f0a78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clairvoyant Combatant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you form a telepathic bond with a creature using your Awakened Mind, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you, and you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against that creature for the duration of the bond.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s0f13f709f5e86fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Halfling Nimbleness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move through the space of any creature that is of a size larger than yours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s0fa81d9b68e5f07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Manipulation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have discovered ways to manipulate elemental energy in dynamic ways, including adapting more nuanced kinetic shapes, either temporary or persistent.</p><p><strong>Elemental Infusions.</strong> You gain two elemental infusions of your choice. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page. When you gain certain kineticist levels, you gain additional infusions of your choice.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the infusions you know and replace it with another infusion that you could learn at that level.</p><p>If an elemental infusion has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the infusion at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.</p><p>Some infusions modify your kinetic shape. There are modifications for your kinetic blast and kinetic blade, and kinetic shape effects. You can only apply one one shape modification and one shape effect to the same use of a kinetic shape.</p><p><strong>Kinesis Points.</strong> You have 2 kinesis points, which are used to power some of your elemental infusions. You gain one additional point every time you level up, to a maximum of 20 at level 20.</p><p>You can never have more kinesis points than shown on the table for your level. You regain all spent kinesis points when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Kinetic Reserves.</strong> You gain the following ways to spend your kinesis points.</p><ul><li><strong>Kinetic Enhancement.</strong> When you make an Ability Check, you can spend 1 kinesis point to gain Advantage on the check.</li><li><strong>Kinetic Shield.</strong> When you take acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, you can spend 1 kinesis point and use your Reaction to grant yourself Resistance against that instance of the damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.kineticist.kinesis-points","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/abstract-ribbons-red-orange.webp","_id":"s0fd6902f16322d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bountiful Harvest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two tools from among alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit. Your Proficiency Bonus for checks with the chosen tools is doubled.</p><p>Additionally, when you forage for food or ingredients, you can roll the die on the result column twice and take the higher result.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1018dad6844153c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unsleeping","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Shadowborn require neither food nor sleep. To sustain themselves they instead harness energy from the Shadowplane, for which they need to enter a state similar to deep meditation for 4 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/moon-crescent.webp","_id":"s1040602e3f6b896","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite Improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Crimson Rite.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s104bf2ffbac07c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elegant Courtier","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your discipline and attention to detail allow you to excel in social situations. Whenever you make a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p>Your self-control also causes you to gain Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws. If you already have this Proficiency, you instead gain Proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma Saving Throws (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s10799f8f8a50dcc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the nature skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/leaf-juggle-humanoid-green.webp","_id":"s1131813d0d8c6ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Exalted Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your presence on the field of battle is an inspiration to those dedicated to your cause. You can use your Bonus Action to gain the following benefits for 1 hour:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>You gain a Heroic Inspiration at the start of every one of your turns if you do not currently have one. Alternatively, you can give a Heroic Inspiration to one ally you can see within 30 ft of you and who does not already have one. You can do so even if you already have a Heroic Inspiration yourself.</li><li>All allies within 30 ft of you have Advantage on Wisdom Saving Throws.</li></ul><p>This effect ends early if you are Incapacitated or die. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1159bcbad7704ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Self-Restoration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sheer force of will, you can remove one of the following conditions from yourself at the end of each of your turns: Charmed, Frightened, or Poisoned.</p><p>In addition, forgoing food and drink doesn't give you levels of Exhaustion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-flared-green.webp","_id":"s11a1e633a497c96","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insightful","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the insight skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s11c26fd09f7c17c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Whirling Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Bonus Action on your turn, which you can use to make a melee weapon attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s125151a1bf5930d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Geokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Mold Earth cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s125bb4245909e97","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of the Voracious","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on the Saving Throw for your bloodlust while in hybrid form. Additionally, your Brand of Castigation can now bind a foe to your hunter's ferocity. While in your hybrid form, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against a creature branded by you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s128a63d54aa884a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Calm before the Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s129cae62f75272a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Ambition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Deception, Intimidation, and Persuasion checks. Additionally, you do not expend a use of your Channel Divinity on Reject Failure if the D20 test does not succeed after the reroll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s12cadac17393a7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Expertise in two of your skill proficiencies of your choice. Performance and Persuasion are recommended if you have Proficiency in them.</p><p>At Bard level 9, you gain Expertise in two more of your skill proficiencies of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"s12d1b9531fe395d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Iron Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed your ability to resist the mind-altering powers of your prey. You gain Proficiency in Wisdom Saving Throws. If you already have this Proficiency, you instead gain Proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma Saving Throws (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s12ee5be9247955d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Second-Story Work","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've trained to get into especially hard-to-reach places, granting you these benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Climber.</strong> You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</li><li><strong>Jumper.</strong> You can determine your jump distance using your Dexterity rather than your Strength.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/settlement/stone-stairs.webp","_id":"s132bcd19f811413","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flexible Casting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your sorcery points to gain additional spell slots, or sacrifice spell slots to gain additional sorcery points. You learn other ways to use your sorcery points as you reach higher levels.</p><p><strong>Creating Spell Slots.</strong> You can transform unexpended sorcery points into one spell slot on your turn (no Action required). The created spell slots vanish at the end of a Long Rest. The Creating Spell Slots table shows the cost of creating a spell slot of a given level. You can create spell slots no higher in level than 5th.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Creating Spell Slots</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Spell Slot Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Sorcery Point Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1st</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>7</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Converting a Spell Slot to Sorcery Points.</strong> You can expend one spell slot and gain a number of sorcery points equal to the slot's level (no Action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-shock-wave-teal.webp","_id":"s13696402dc79974","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clockwork Cavalcade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You summon spirits of order to expunge disorder around you. As an Action, you summon the spirits in a 30-foot cube originating from you. The spirits look like modrons or other constructs of your choice. The spirits are intangible and invulnerable, and they create the following effects within the cube before vanishing:</p><ul><li>The spirits restore up to 100 hit points, divided as you choose among any number of creatures of your choice in the cube.</li><li>Any damaged objects entirely in the cube are repaired instantly.</li><li>Every spell of 6th level or lower ends on creatures and objects of your choice in the cube.</li></ul><p>Once you use this action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s138b2971779524b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knowledge of the Ages","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the history and arcana skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-book-study-purple.webp","_id":"s13bd3878d4c233f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Shadowborn do not breathe, cannot benefit from regular healing except for class features that can target only themselves, are Immune to Poison and Disease, and vulnerable to Radiant Damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/death/skull-energy-light-white.webp","_id":"s13d4999fc7ffb19","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swift Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your add your Intelligence modifier to Initiative rolls.</p><p>Additionally, you can use your Cunning Action and Master of Tactics as part of the same Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s13db9fa56da6ef6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Hex","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your alien patron grants you a powerful curse. You always have the Hex spell prepared. When you cast Hex and choose an ability, the target also has Disadvantage on Saving Throws of the chosen ability for the duration of the spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s145c99eebbc1544","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically transform yourself into a shadowy form as a Bonus Action. In this form, you have Resistance to all damage except force and radiant damage, and you can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3. You take 5 force damage if you end your turn inside an object.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can change your hit points to three times your Sorcerer level instead. This feature does not work if the triggering damage was radiant or a critical hit. You can use this effect only once per use of Umbral form.</p><p>Once you have used this feature, you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1488d1496e857fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ghost Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can phase partially into the realm of the dead, becoming like a ghost. As a Bonus Action, you assume a spectral form. While in this form, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed, you can hover, and Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you. You can also move through creatures and objects as if they were 3, but you take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.</p><p>You stay in this form for 10 minutes or until you end it as a Bonus Action. To use this feature again, you must finish a Long Rest or destroy one of your soul trinkets as part of the Bonus Action you use to activate Ghost Walk.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s14fe060dfc25a50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cleansing Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you lose Lay on Hands on a creature, you can also remove one or more of the following conditions: Blinded, Charmed, Confused, Dazed, Deafened, Dominated, Frightened, Paralyzed, or Stunned by spending 5 points per condition from your pool of healing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-teal.webp","_id":"s15c1d45bd6ef3ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sear Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use Turn Undead, you can roll a number of d8s equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1d8) and add the rolls together. Each Undead that fails its Saving Throw against that use of Turn Undead takes Radiant damage equal to the roll's total. This damage doesn't end the turn effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-impact-shock-wave.webp","_id":"s15d471ee04dc9c1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to read the barriers between the planes, making it easier for you to draw forth more powerful creatures. When you expend a spell slot to cast a conjuration or necromancy spell that summons creatures, the spell counts as a number of spell levels lower for you for the purposes of which level of spell slot it requires. This reduction is equal to half your proficiency (rounded down). Further, it determines when you can learn these spells and also affects spells cast at a higher level. This feature cannot reduce the level of a spell below 1st.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s15ea3b1cad92b01","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Host Caller's Link","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use the Summoner's Call or Transposition class feature, you can target another creature you have summoned instead of your Eidolon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1635b1c2f514b64","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Confound (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you until the start of your next turn while any of your allies are within reach of its attacks.</li><li><strong>Instigate (Cost: 3d6).</strong> An ally of your choice within 60 feet of you can use its Reaction to make a weapon attack against the same target, provided it is within reach.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s16766d81f6e6ce9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack Action on your turn, you can replace one of the attacks with a casting of one of your Sorcerer cantrips that has a casting time of an Action.</p><p>Any feature that increases the damage die size of your Unarmed Attack also increases the size of one of your damaging cantrips' dice by the same number of steps. For the purposes of this feature, the initial effect of your Martial Arts feature counts as one step, as do any further increments acquired through Monk levels. This feature has no effect when you are wielding a weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1680faf77148e89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your familiar gains 1 additional hit point for each of your Witch levels and its AC increases by 2. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus in place of its own attack bonus and your spellcasting save DC in place of any DC for its features.</p><p>Your familiar's weapon attacks deal an additional 1d4 damage of a type determined by your chosen Wild Domain, as seen in the table below. This additional damage increases at 5th level (1d6), 11th level (1d8), and 17th level (1d10) in this class.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Familiar Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>Radiant</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s16e155e1f547260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortifying Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>15th-level ranger Beast Conclave feature (replaces Share Spells)</p><p>While your companion can see you, it has Advantage on all Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s172ee1defa1220d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scion of the Depths","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron accepts you into his inner court of servitors. You gain the ability to breathe water, and a Swim Speed equal to your normal Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>You gain Immunity to lightning damage. When your Immunity reduces damage from an effect to 0, as a Reaction you can cause creatures of your choice that you can see within 30 ft. of you to take lightning damage equal to your Charisma modifier + your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1730e18de8fe298","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earth Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1754b8a5d07ef8c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lucky","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll a 1 on the d20 for an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/gaming/dice-runed-brown.webp","_id":"s1754f5d0f738120","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Throw Wide the Gates","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Gate spell without expending a spell slot and without a material component. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s17ea76ae04f2a1a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Chemical Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:</p><ul><li>You gain Resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are Immune to the Poisoned condition.</li><li>You can cast Greater Restoration and Heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you have alchemist's supplies on your person. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a Long Rest.</li><li>Potent Healing: When you cast an Artificer spell that restores hit points, you treat the spell as two spell levels higher for the purpose of determining the amount of hit points restored.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/vials-blue-pink.webp","_id":"s185c328acccd75a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You regain all uses of Fighting Spirit when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s185ced54839406f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speak with Small Beasts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas with Small or smaller beasts. Forest gnomes love animals and often keep squirrels, badgers, rabbits, moles, woodpeckers, and other creatures as beloved pets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rodent-rat-green.webp","_id":"s1889be4dc9d66a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Dreadful Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you focus your negative emotion into a lance of magical menace. Choose one creature you can see within 60 ft of you that can also you. The creature has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls and contested Ability Checks against you for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s18d31e67aef92da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of the Raven","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to merge with your raven spirit. As a Bonus Action when your raven is perched on your shoulder, your body merges with your raven's form. While merged, you become Tiny, you replace your Speed with the raven's, and you can use your action only to Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, or Search. During this time, you gain the benefits of your raven being perched on your shoulder. As an Action, you and the raven return to normal.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s18d506a145a3e81","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Devious Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed yourself in new ways to use your Sneak Attack. The following effects are now among your Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Daze (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or become Dazed until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Knock Out (Cost: 6d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or drop Unconscious for 1d4 hours or until it takes damage.</li><li><strong>Obscure (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or become Blinded until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/sword-stuck-glowing-pink.webp","_id":"s1997c37e921a8ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two spells in your spellbook as your signature spells. Choose one benefit for each signature spell from the list below. Whenever you cast one of your signature spells, it gains the chosen benefit. You cannot choose the same benefit for both of your signature spells.</p><p><strong>Intensified.</strong> The spell counts as 2 spell levels higher for the purpose of dealing damage.</p><p><strong>Labyrinthine.</strong> The spell cannot be counterspelled or dispelled.</p><p><strong>Focus.</strong> The spell no longer requires Concentration.</p><p><strong>Magnified.</strong> The spell's area of effect is doubled and you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your INT modifier from the effect.</p><p><strong>Overhelming.</strong> The Spell Save DC for this spell receives a +3 bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/beam-impact-purple.webp","_id":"s19f8de73e05f223","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the dread presence of your dragon ancestor, causing those around you to become awestruck or frightened. As a Bonus Action, you draw on this power and exude an aura of awe or fear (your choice) to a distance of 60 feet. For 1 minute, each hostile creature that starts its turn in this aura or enters it for the first time on a turn must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be Charmed (if you chose awe) or Frightened (if you chose fear) until the aura ends. A creature that succeeds on this Saving Throw is Immune to your aura for 24 hours.</p><p>Additionally, any spell that deals the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry is treated as 1 spell level higher for the purposes of its damage.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/projectile-smoke-glowing.webp","_id":"s1a51710ea916cd2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcery Incarnate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you have no uses of Innate Sorcery left, you can use it if you spend 2 Sorcery Points when you take the Bonus Action to activate it.</p><p>In addition, while your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use up to two of your Metamagic options on each spell you cast.</p><p>Additionally, you add your Charisma modifier to the damage you deal with any Sorcerer cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-teal.webp","_id":"s1acbf781235584f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine energy coursing through you can empower healing spells. Whenever you or an ally within 5 feet of you rolls dice to determine the number of hit points a spell restores, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll any number of those dice once, provided you aren't Incapacitated. You can use this feature only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1b0e1a8c348a81e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Signature Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have achieved such mastery over certain spells that you can cast them at will. Choose a 1st-level wizard spell and a 2nd-level wizard spell that are in your spellbook. You can cast those spells at their lowest level without expending a spell slot when you have them prepared. If you want to cast either spell at a higher level, you must expend a spell slot as normal.</p><p>By spending 8 hours in study, you can exchange one or both of the spells you chose for different spells of the same levels.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/projectile-wave-arrow.webp","_id":"s1b26330f2ee775a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you are not wearing armor or wielding a shield. This bonus increases when you reach certain monk levels, as shown in the Monk table.</p><p>At 9th level, you gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling during the move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/root-vine-entangle-foot-green.webp","_id":"s1b9bfaa752fc683","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite Improvement (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional Crimson Rite.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s1bc79e0f2500f14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scornful Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Those who dare to strike you are psychically punished for their audacity. Whenever a creature hits you with an attack, that creature takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1) if you're not Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1bcd5110df43ecb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1bd22f300348e8a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Coordinated Takedown.</strong> When a creature within reach of your natural weapons is hit by a melee attack from one of your allies, you can use your Reaction to immediately force that creature to make a Strength Saving Throw as per your Fanged Aspect feature.</li><li><strong>Bolstering Barks.</strong> Whenever you use the Help action on one of your allies, they gain temporary hit points equal to half your Shifter level.</li><li><strong>Fierce Protector.</strong> When you hit a creature with your natural weapons, it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against creatures other than you until the end of your next turn while it is within your reach. If it makes an attack against a target other than you during that time, you have Advantage on your next Attack Roll against it and add half your Shifter level to the damage roll (rounded down).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c037ef1a3ac68c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rooted Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to twist and turn the ground beneath you. While you are in your guardian form, the ground within 30 feet of you is 3 for your enemies.</p><p>Additionally, you cannot be moved forcibly or knocked Prone while in your guardian form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c281e69e8a4e3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twinkling Constellations","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The constellations of your Starry Form improve. The 1d8 of the Archer and the Chalice becomes 2d8, and while the Dragon is active, you have a Fly Speed of 20 feet and can hover.</p><p>Moreover, at the start of each of your turns while in your Starry Form, you can change which constellation glimmers on your body.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1c854dfd61fca6a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Archer Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn magical theory or some of the secrets of nature—typical for practitioners of this elven martial tradition. You choose to gain Proficiency in either the Arcana or the Nature skill, and you choose to learn either the Prestidigitation or the Druidcraft cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1d92f2029b92474","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Intervention","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on your deity or pantheon to intervene on your behalf. As a Magic action, choose any Cleric spell of level 5 or lower that requires an Action or a Bonus Action to cast. As part of the same action, you cast that spell without expending a spell slot or needing Material components. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue-purple.webp","_id":"s1dc04f83c7c8ab3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warding Maneuver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to fend off strikes directed at you, your mount, or other creatures nearby. If you or a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack, you can roll 1d8 as a Reaction if you're wielding a melee weapon or a shield. Roll the die, and add the number rolled to the target's AC against that attack. If the attack still hits, the target has Resistance against the attack's damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1dec0f9b97df1c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the mastery benefits for two weapons of your choice as well as an armor type (see Armor Mastery and Weapon Mastery variant rules). You must be proficient in the chosen weapons and armor. If you possess the Unarmored Defense feature, you may choose it in place of an armor type.</p><p>You can change your choices when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/maneuver-sword-katana-yellow.webp","_id":"s1e10999e1cfebf0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Doom Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, your or your bonded familiar can touch a creature you can see and weave a protective charm that wards against ill luck for 1 hour. The target cannot have Disadvantage on any D20 Tests. You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e1a66c72a8c8e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Coil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Tentacle of the Deeps can defend you and others, interposing itself between them and harm. When you or a creature you can see takes damage while within 10 feet of the tentacle, you can use your Reaction to choose one of those creatures and reduce the damage to that creature by 1d8 + your Charisma modifier. When you reach 10th level in this class, the damage reduced by the tentacle increases to 2d8 + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e2e8e5e4ca218c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Embodiment of the Law","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become remarkably adept at channeling magical energy to compel others.</p><p>If you cast a spell of the enchantment school using a spell slot of 1st level or higher, you can change the spell's casting time to 1 Bonus Action for this casting, provided the spell's casting time is normally 1 action.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e48e16148c25f2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Charger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can run down your foes, whether you're mounted or not. If you move at least 10 feet in a straight line right before attacking a creature no more than 1 size larger than you (or your mount if you're mounted) and you hit it with the attack, that target takes additional damage equal to half your fighter level and must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be knocked Prone. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1e8130ffe8b8a86","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action: Umbral Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use your Cunning Action to shape the shadows around you into a 30-feet radius sphere around your position. The area inside the sphere counts as dim light and persists for 10 minutes. It disappears early if you become Incapacitated or if its area overlaps with light created by a spell of 3rd level or higher.</p><p>You can only have one Umbral Shroud active at a time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1eca522f9bdbc74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Duplicity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The illusion of your Invoke Duplicity has grown more powerful in the following ways.</p><ul><li><strong>Shared Distraction.</strong> When you and your allies make Attack Rolls against a creature within 5 feet of the illusion, the Attack Rolls have Advantage.</li><li><strong>Healing Illusion.</strong> When the illusion ends, you or a creature of your choice within 5 feet of it regains a number of Hit Points equal to your Cleric level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1f0f61949d45a50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Your Psionic Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every member of the Psionics tradition has a story about how their psionic focus came into their life. Consider how you found yours and what form it takes.</p><p>The event that brought your psionic focus to you probably holds personal significance. Did your master give it to you upon the completion of your apprenticeship? Was it awarded to you when you graduated from your academy of wizardry? Did it call to you in a jeweler's shop? Was it associated with the moment when your psionic powers first manifested? One morning, did you wake up with it humming under your pillow?</p><p>The form your psionic focus takes is also yours to define, likely being a reflection of how your magic came into being, a symbol of your own psyche, or an item you use to focus your thoughts. It is a handheld object that has special meaning to you, but that can't be a weapon or magic item. Perhaps it's a childhood memento, the skull of an alien creature, a crystal that makes you feel a certain way, a coin that only lands on its edge, a firescarred planchette, or any other enigmatic personal relic.</p><p>However the object arrived and whatever form it takes, your psionic focus is now yours, and you decide how to handle it. Will you mount it on a wand or staff? Would you prefer to wear it on a necklace or circlet? Have you embedded it into the cover of your spellbook? Wherever you put it, you can now channel your magic through it, and it is a sign of your membership in the revered tradition of psionic wizardry.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s1f3295193bb5424","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Plane Charter Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach an Artificer level specified in the Plane Charter Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Plane Charter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>Faerie Fire, Guiding Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Locate Object, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Blink, Clairvoyance</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Dimension Door, Locate Creature</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Scrying, Teleportation Circle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s1f9e1a69e071314","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Instinct","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your instincts are so honed that you have Advantage on initiative rolls.</p><p>Additionally, if you are Surprised at the beginning of combat and aren't Incapacitated, you can act normally on your first turn, but only if you enter your rage before doing anything else on that turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/wolf-howl-moon-forest-blue.webp","_id":"s1fa63c9e1ee3391","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Hexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spread your Hexblade's Curse from a slain creature to another creature. When the creature cursed by your Hexblade's Curse dies, you can apply the curse to a different creature you can see within 30 feet of you, provided you aren't Incapacitated. When you apply the curse in this way, you don't regain hit points from the death of the previously cursed creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s200b35404f758e0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Chivy (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw or use its Reaction to move as far from you as it can, taking the safest route.</li><li><strong>Stupefy (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target must make an Intelligence Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes before the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s21345d9cfb7fa7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Archdruid","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The vitality of nature constantly blooms within you, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Evergreen Wild Shape.</strong> Whenever you roll Initiative and have no uses of Wild Shape left, you regain one expended use of it.</li><li><strong>Nature Magician.</strong> You can convert uses of Wild Shape into a spell slot (no action required). Choose a number of your unexpended uses of Wild Shape and convert them into a single spell slot, with each use contributing 2 spell levels. For example, if you convert two uses of Wild Shape, you produce a level 4 spell slot. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</li><li><strong>Longevity.</strong> The primal magic that you wield causes you to age more slowly. For every ten years that pass, your body ages only one year.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/beam-hand-leaves-green.webp","_id":"s214d9d45799f6e1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wyvern Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have undergone specialized training that allows you to bond with and ride a wyvern.</p><p>With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 50 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth a wyvern from the wilderness to serve as your faithful companion. See its game statistics in the accompanying Wyvern Companion stat block. You choose the damage type for its Draconic Blood feature.</p><p>At the end of the 8 hours, your Wyvern Companion appears and gains all the benefits of your Rider's Bond ability. You can have only one Wyvern Companion at a time.</p><p>If your Wyvern Companion is ever slain, the life bond you share allows you to return it to life. To do so you have to spend 1 hour, 25 gp worth of ingredients, and a use of your Second Wind or 2 of your Hit Dice to return it to life with a special ritual.</p><p>You can return your Wyvern Companion to life in this manner even if you do not possess any part of its body, but to do so you have spend double the required resources and the ritual instead requires 8 hours.</p><p>If you use this ability to return a former Wyvern Companion to life while you have a current Wyvern Companion, your current companion leaves you and is replaced by the restored companion.</p><p>You can mount your companion even if you are the same size. If you ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can use any of its actions during your turn or immediately after. While you ride it, your companion's flying speed is halved and it has to end its flying movement on the ground.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s217721b894258a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Durability","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your toughness allows you to shrug off assaults that would devastate others.</p><p>Whenever you make a Saving Throw, roll 1d6 and add the die to your Saving Throw total. If applying this bonus to a death Saving Throw increases the total to 20 or higher, you gain the benefits of rolling a 20 on the d20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s218be2432a75ae0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mindless Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can't be Charmed or Frightened while raging. If you are Charmed or Frightened when you enter your rage, the effect ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/toxins/cup-goblet-poisoned-spilled.webp","_id":"s21c321ded0c07c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Protector of the Prime Material","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar are always under the effects of a Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast Banishment on a creature that has the Magic Resistance trait and is not native to the Prime Material Plane, you ignore the effects of that trait.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s22208880ffbcbe3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your quick thinking and agility allow you to move and act quickly. You can take a Bonus Action on each of your turns in combat. This action can be used only to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-watch.webp","_id":"s225d35fb16edbea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Ready","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your combat training and your experiments with magic have paid off in two ways:</p><ul><li>You gain Proficiency with martial weapons.</li><li>When you attack with a magic weapon, you can use your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity modifier, for the attack and damage rolls.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/sword-engraved-glow-purple.webp","_id":"s22b8ec994150d90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Advanced Transformation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to unleash and control more of the beast within. Your hybrid form also gains the following additional benefit.</p><p><strong>Lycan Regeneration.</strong> At the start of each of your turns in your hybrid form when you have at least 1 hit point, you regain hit points equal to your hemocraft die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s232c474baee0096","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Druidic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know Druidic, the secret language of druids. While learning this ancient tongue, you also unlocked the magic of communicating with animals; you always have the Speak with Animals spell prepared.</p><p>You can use Druidic to leave hidden messages. You and others who know Druidic automatically spot such a message. Others spot the message's presence with a successful DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check but can't decipher it without magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"s233c5dfa1867643","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (7th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 7th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-symbol-skull-grey.webp","_id":"s2399d0ff8279722","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Cunning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can perform an esoteric rite for 1 minute. At the end of it, you regain expended Pact Magic spell slots but no more than a number equal to half your maximum (round up). Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hand-green.webp","_id":"s240826511f0c2bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 4 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s24f41783e603962","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Training in War and Song (Bladesinging)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with light armor, and you gain Proficiency with one type of one-handed melee weapon of your choice.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Performance skill if you don't already have it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s25f9a8e513eb84d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 16)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2673ce2b0039737","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can imbue yourself with a primal power called Rage, a force that grants you extraordinary might and resilience. You can enter it as a Bonus Action if you aren't wearing Heavy armor.</p><p>You can enter your Rage the number of times shown for your Barbarian level in the Rages column of the Barbarian Features table. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>While active, your Rage follows the rules below.</p><p><strong>Damage Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage.</p><p><strong>Rage Damage.</strong> When you make an attack using Strength—with either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike—and deal damage to the target, you gain a bonus to the damage that increases as you gain levels as a Barbarian, as shown in the Rage Damage column of the Barbarian Features table.</p><p><strong>Strength Advantage.</strong> You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</p><p><strong>No Concentration or Spells.</strong> You can't maintain Concentration, and you can't cast spells.</p><p><strong>Duration.</strong> The Rage lasts until the end of your next turn, and it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition. If your Rage is still active on your next turn, you can extend the Rage for another round by doing one of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Duration.</strong> Make an Attack Roll against an enemy.</li><li>Force an enemy to make a Saving Throw.</li><li>Take a Bonus Action to extend your Rage.</li></ul><p>Each time the Rage is extended, it lasts until the end of your next turn. You can maintain a Rage for up to 10 minutes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":10,"units":"minute"},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":"self"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"self"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.barbarian.rages","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/mouth-teeth-human.webp","_id":"s268aea0605b7eb5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deft Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Thanks to your travels, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Expertise.</strong> Choose one of your skill proficiencies with which you lack Expertise. You gain Expertise in that skill.</li><li><strong>Languages.</strong> You know two languages of your choice.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/settlement/bridge-stone.webp","_id":"s272e435a5e9f7b1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of hemocraft suffuses your body to permanently reinforce your resilience. Your Speed increases by 5 feet, and you have a bonus to Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution Saving Throws equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-body-explode-disintegrate.webp","_id":"s2798305fdbc3909","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tokens of the Departed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a life ends in your presence, you're able to snatch a token from the departing soul, a sliver of its life essence that takes physical form: when a creature you can see dies within 30 feet of you, you can open your free hand and cause a Tiny trinket to appear there, a soul trinket. The DM determines the trinket's form or has you roll on the Trinkets table in the Player's Handbook to generate it. You can have a maximum number of soul trinkets equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you can't create one while at your maximum.</p><p>You can use soul trinkets in the following ways:</p><ul><li>While a soul trinket is on your person, you have Advantage on death Saving Throws and Constitution Saving Throws, for your vitality is enhanced by the life essence within the object.</li><li>When you deal Sneak Attack damage on your turn, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets that's on your person and then immediately use Wails from the Grave, without expending a use of that feature.</li><li>As an Action, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets, no matter where it's located. When you do so, you can ask the spirit associated with the trinket one question. The spirit appears to you and answers in a language it knew in life. It's under no obligation to be truthful, and it answers as concisely as possible, eager to be free. The spirit knows only what it knew in life, as determined by the DM.</li></ul><p>You gain two soul trinkets when you gain this feature. You regain all soul trinkets whenever you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s280eeb22c3f5aef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slippery Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you may use your Reaction to immediately teleport 30 feet to a place that you can see and attempt to hide.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2846d9b0aecabae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deep Freeze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Speed reduction from your Clinging Frost feature increases to 20 feet and subsequent failed Saving Throws against it have additional effects as per below:</p><ul><li><strong>One failed save:</strong> The affected creature has Disadvantage on its next Attack Roll.</li><li><strong>Two failed save:</strong> The affected creature's Speed is reduced to 0.</li><li><strong>Three failed save:</strong> The affected creature has vulnerability against the damage of the next spell you cast that deals cold damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s285eb5171708bec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nimble Beast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>11th-level ranger Beast Conclave feature (replaces Beast's Fury)</p><p>Whenever an attacker that your companion can see hits it with an attack, it can use its Reaction to halve the attack's damage against it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2877882c40786e3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Ambusher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master the art of the ambush. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p>At the start of your first turn of each combat, your Speed increases by 10 feet, which lasts until the end of that turn. If you take the Attack action on that turn, you can make one additional weapon attack as part of that action. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's damage type.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s28861a697cfd240","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nimble Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage against DEX Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/figure-running-gray.webp","_id":"s29727dee0808f83","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unyielding Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Wisdom Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s29cf614fed1dfa3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"s29ed1bd04285cbe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Icon of Deceit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become of an avatar of deceit and emit an aura of treacherous magic in a 30-ft emanation. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>When a creature targets you with an attack, but any of your allies are within the aura and within range of the attack, it makes the roll with Disadvantage.</li><li>As part of the Bonus Action to activate this feature and as a Bonus Action on every subsequent turn, you can give yourself Advantage on one Attack Roll.</li><li>When you use your Treacherous Strikes feature, the new target of the attack can be anywhere in the aura. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2a17746de03b43e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Student of the Divine","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Religion skill. If you are already proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2a3e57607696197","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tough as Nails","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in Constitution Saving Throws and your hit point maximum increases by 1 for every level in this class and increases by 1 again when you gain a level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2a76294e7c5d6e1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swarming Dispersal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can discorporate into your swarm, avoiding danger. When you take damage, you can use your Reaction to give yourself Resistance to that damage. You vanish into your swarm and then teleport to an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you, where you reappear with the swarm.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2aac2c7c22e76b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Counter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to counterattack when your prey tries to sabotage you. If the target of your Slayer's Prey forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to make one weapon attack against the quarry. You make this attack immediately before making the Saving Throw. If your attack hits, your save automatically succeeds, in addition to the attack's normal effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ac7a691358810c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empower Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to spend your own magical reserves to empower your Eidolon's attacks. As a Bonus Action, you can spend a spell slot if you can see your Eidolon within 60 feet of you. For 1 hour, you add 1d8 times the level of the spell slot expended to your Eidolon's damage rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ad5c06368ef4be","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heroic Warrior","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>10th-level fighter Champion feature (replaces Champion's Reflexes)</p><p>The thrill of battle drives you toward victory. During combat, you can give yourself Heroic Inspiration whenever you start your turn without it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2aee1698949012e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Ultimate Mercy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of life energy opens the door to the ultimate mercy. As an Action, you can touch the corpse of a creature that died within the past 24 hours and expend 5 ki points. The creature then returns to life, regaining a number of hit points equal to 4d10 + your Wisdom modifier. If the creature died while subject to any of the following conditions, it revives with them removed: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, and Stunned.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b18a0c4e5dfd75","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Seasonal Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain the following benefits based on your chosen season:</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> You are Immune to poison and disease.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> You are Resistance to fire and radiant damage, and you are acclimatized to extreme heat.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> You are Resistance to necrotic and lightning damage, and your maximum hit points cannot be reduced.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> You are Resistance to cold damage and you are acclimatized to extreme cold. Any temporary hit points that you gain are increased by an amount equal to your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b55c096b104a5a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stalker's Flurry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to attack with such unexpected speed that you can turn a miss into another strike. Once on each of your turns when you miss with a weapon attack, you can make another weapon attack as part of the same action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2b7a02926a0e9dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swift Memorize","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically extract knowledge from your spellbook and replace one of the level 1+ Wizard spells you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell from the book.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-eye-brown.webp","_id":"s2b8735c0b43259f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Concerted Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose up to two allies for your Concerted Attack. Alternatively, you can choose to make two weapon attacks instead of one with your attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/crosshair-triple-strike-orange.webp","_id":"s2bc9c602affe145","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Season","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you or your bonded familiar awaken the power of your chosen season in a 30-feet radius sphere around a point you can see within 60 feet, affecting creatures of your choice in the area in the following ways for 1 minute.</p><p>Either of you can dismiss this effect as a Bonus Action and only one instance of the effect can be active at a time.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> An affected creature regains additional hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier when healed.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> An affected creature that starts its turn in the area or enters it for the first time on turn, its Speed is increased by 10 feet. Additionally, the area is brightly lit. This light counts as sunlight.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Healing on affected creatures is halved.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> The area is 3 for affected creatures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2c0e314388d3104","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Maneuver Options","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you have access to maneuvers, the following maneuvers are added to the list of options available to you. Maneuvers are available to Battle Masters but also to characters who have a special feature like the Superior Technique fighting style or the Martial Adept feat.</p><h5>Ambush</h5><p>When you make a Dexterity (Stealth) check or an initiative roll, you can expend one superiority die and add the die to the roll, provided you aren't Incapacitated.</p><h5>Bait and Switch</h5><p>When you're within 5 feet of a creature on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and switch places with that creature, provided you spend at least 5 feet of movement and the creature is willing and isn't Incapacitated. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p><p>Roll the superiority die. Until the start of your next turn, you or the other creature (your choice) gains a bonus to AC equal to the number rolled.</p><h5>Brace</h5><p>When a creature you can see moves into the reach you have with the melee weapon you're wielding, you can use your Reaction to expend one superiority die and make one attack against the creature, using that weapon. If the attack hits, add the superiority die to the weapon's damage roll.</p><h5>Commanding Presence</h5><p>When you make a Charisma (Intimidation), a Charisma (Performance), or a Charisma (Persuasion) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the Ability Check.</p><h5>Grappling Strike</h5><p>Immediately after you hit a creature with a melee attack on your turn, you can expend one superiority die and then try to grapple the target as a Bonus Action (see the Player's Handbook for rules on grappling). Add the superiority die to your Strength (Athletics) check.</p><h5>Quick Toss</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one superiority die and make a ranged attack with a weapon that has the thrown property. You can draw the weapon as part of making this attack. If you hit, add the superiority die to the weapon's damage roll.</p><h5>Tactical Assessment</h5><p>When you make an Intelligence (Investigation), an Intelligence (History), or a Wisdom (Insight) check, you can expend one superiority die and add the superiority die to the Ability Check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2c360f274355b4b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ascendant Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your draconic spirit reaches its peak. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Augment Breath.</strong> When you use your Breath of the Dragon, you can spend 1 ki point to augment its shape and power. The exhalation of draconic energy becomes either a 60-foot cone or a 120-foot line that is 5 feet wide (your choice), and each creature in that area takes damage equal to four rolls of your Martial Arts die on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</li><li><strong>Blindsight.</strong> You gain blindsight out to 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind total cover, even if you're Blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an Invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you.</li><li><strong>Explosive Fury.</strong> When you activate your Aspect of the Wyrm, draconic fury explodes from you. Choose any number of creatures you can see in your aura. Each of those creatures must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw against your ki save DC or take 3d10 acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2c55e0dd073c770","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"There and Back Again","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to speak, read, and write Sylvan. You make Pathfinding checks in the Feywild with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ca790d94ce5053","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision from your race, its range increases by 60 feet.</p><p>You are also adept at evading creatures that rely on darkvision. While in darkness, you are Invisible to any creature that relies on darkvision to see you in that darkness.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2d0af23d1a881ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Branches of the Tree","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever a creature you can see starts its turn within 30 feet of you while your Rage is active, you can take a Reaction to summon spectral branches of the World Tree around it. The target must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC 8 plus your Strength modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or be teleported to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of yourself or in the nearest unoccupied space you can see. After the target teleports, you can reduce its Speed to 0 until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2d1e20c39ddcb7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Diamond Skin","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to harden specific areas of your body in response to physical trauma. When an effect makes you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, you can use your Reaction to halve the effect's damage against you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2d26846194a4a28","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes of Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your eyes begin to glow with your inner fire, giving you a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, your darkvision instead increases by 60 feet.</p><p>In addition, fire and smoke caused by fire cannot obscure your vision.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2da3f373cd1099a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Peerless Skill","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Ability Check or Attack Roll and fail, you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration; roll the Bardic Inspiration die, and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning a failure into a success. On a failure, the Bardic Inspiration isn't expended.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s2db5ff562ca94eb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Companion's Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your animal companion gains a variety of benefits while it is linked to you.</p><p>The animal companion loses its Multiattack action, if it has one.</p><p>The companion obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own.</p><p>When using your Natural Explorer feature, you and your animal companion can both move stealthily at a normal pace.</p><p>Your animal companion has abilities and game statistics determined in part by your level. Your companion uses your Proficiency bonus rather than its own. In addition to the areas where it normally uses its Proficiency bonus, an animal companion also adds its Proficiency bonus to its AC and to its damage rolls.</p><p>Your animal companion gains Proficiency in two skills of your choice. It also becomes proficient with all Saving Throws.</p><p>For each level you gain after 3rd, your animal companion gains an additional hit die and increases its hit points accordingly.</p><p>Whenever you gain the Ability Score Improvement class feature, your companion's abilities also improve. Your companion can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or it can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, your companion can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature unless its description specifies otherwise.</p><p>Your companion shares your alignment, and has a personality trait and a flaw that you can roll for or select from the tables below. Your companion shares your ideal, and its bond is always, \"The ranger who travels with me is a beloved companion for whom I would gladly give my life.\"</p><p>Your animal companion gains the benefits of your Favored Enemy feature, and of your Improved Favored Enemy feature when you gain that feature at 6th level. It uses the favored enemies you selected for those features.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Companion Trait</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Trait</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>I'm dauntless in the face of adversity.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Threaten my friends, threaten me.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>I stay on alert so others can rest.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>People see an animal and underestimate me.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>I have a knack for showing up in the nick of time.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>I put my friends' needs before my own in all things.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Companion Flaw</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Flaw</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>If there's food left unattended, I'll eat it.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>I growl at strangers, and all people except my ranger are strangers to me.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Any time is a good time for a belly rub.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>I'm deathly afraid of water.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>My idea of hello is a flurry of licks to the face.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>I jump on creatures to tell them how much I love them.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2e3012823dd4edd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bend Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have the ability to twist fate using your wild magic. When another creature you can see makes an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction and spend 1 sorcery points to roll 1d4 and apply the number rolled as a bonus or penalty (your choice) to the creature's roll. You can do so after the creature rolls but before any effects of the roll occur.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2e4663684151008","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Revelation in Flesh","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unleash the aberrant truth hidden within yourself. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 or more sorcery points to magically transform your body for 10 minutes. For each sorcery point you spend, you can gain one of the following benefits of your choice, the effects of which last until the transformation ends:</p><ul><li>You can see any Invisible creature within 60 feet of you, provided it isn't behind total cover. Your eyes also turn black or become writhing sensory tendrils.</li><li>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed, and you can hover. As you fly, your skin glistens with mucus or shines with an otherworldly light.</li><li>You gain a Swim Speed equal to twice your Speed, and you can breathe underwater. Moreover, gills grow from your neck or fan out from behind your ears, your fingers become webbed, or you grow writhing cilia that extend through your clothing.</li><li>Your body, along with any equipment you are wearing or carrying, becomes slimy and pliable. You can move through any space as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing, and you can spend 5 feet of movement to escape from nonmagical restraints or being Grappled.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2e4b6e450ae6db1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ingenious Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Flash of Genius, you or a willing creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of yourself can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see as part of that same Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"s2e8c9518f933870","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Epitome of Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a Sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage, you add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of the spell. If the level of the spell is higher than your Charisma modifier, you add it to the damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hand-green.webp","_id":"s2ea837c309c7880","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Smith Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Battle Smith Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Battle Smith Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Shield</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Branding Smite, Warding Bond</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Aura of Vitality, Conjure Barrage</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Aura of Purity, Fire Shield</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Banishing Smite, Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s2eb93530a07dc90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eternal Spellguard","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can empower your Aura of Protection, granting the benefits below for 1 minute or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can restore your use of this ability by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Improved Spell-Breaking Blade.</strong> You add your Charisma modifier to the Ability Check of Counterspell and Dispel Magic when using Spell-Breaking Blade.</li><li><strong>Protection from Magic.</strong> You and your allies in the aura have Advantage on Saving Throws against spells.</li><li><strong>Spell Ward.</strong> Spell attack rolls against you and your allies in the aura have Disadvantage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ec13f2eeb3582c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Divine Intervention","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are able to call on even more powerful divine intervention. When you use your Divine Intervention feature, you can select cleric spells up to 8th level. Additionally, you can select Wish when you select a spell. If you do so, you can't use Divine Intervention again until you finish 2d4 Long Rests. When you cast Wish with this feature, you are Immune to the stress caused by using Wish to do something other than casting a spell, other than the chance to lose the ability to cast the spell again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue.webp","_id":"s2ec644f0fa49238","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supernatural Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain extra resilience against your prey's assaults on your mind and body. Whenever the target of your Slayer's Prey forces you to make a Saving Throw or Ability Check, add 1d6 to your roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2eea257395ac1b5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blazing Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically transform into a creature of living flame. In this form, you have Resistance to piercing, bludgeoning, and slashing damage as well as Immunity to fire damage and poison.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature hits you with a melee attack from within 10 ft or touches you, it takes fire damage equal to half your sorcerer level. Additionally, you add your Charisma modifier to the damage of all the other features gained from this subclass that deal fire damage.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you have used this feature, you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2f283e06f22f7bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Corona of Light","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you cause yourself to emit an aura of sunlight that lasts for 1 minute or until you dismiss it (no action required). You emit Bright Light in a 60-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. Your enemies in the Bright Light have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your Radiance of the Dawn and any spell that deals Fire or Radiant damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2f4efade2959163","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Protective Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you forge between people helps them protect each other. When a creature affected by your Bonds of Solidarity feature is about to take damage, a second bonded creature within 30 feet of the first can use its Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the first creature. The second creature then takes all the damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s2ffa220286dc5c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Transmutation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are concentrating on a transmutation spell, your Concentration can't be broken as a result of taking damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s300ba0ba037fa55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you gain a level of Exhaustion, you can use a Bonus Action to remove it. You can't use this ability again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage.webp","_id":"s30952ed492124e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Swarmkeeper Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Mage Hand cantrip if you don't already know it. When you cast it, the hand takes the form of your swarming nature spirits.</p><p>You also learn an additional spell of 1st level or higher when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Swarmkeeper Spells table. Each spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Swarmkeeper Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Faerie Fire</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Web</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Gaseous Form</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Arcane Eye</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s30bd7435fc2f716","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ki-Empowered Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Unarmed Strikes count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"s31009589f6f6043","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Allegiance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature within 5 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to magically substitute your own health for that of the target creature, causing that creature not to take the damage. Instead, you take the damage. This damage to you can't be reduced or prevented in any way.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3124b182c191c94","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Evolution Feat (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional evolution feat for which you meet the prequisites.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s317bad13f3311df","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one eldritch invocation available to the warlock class. You cannot select an invocation for which you do not meet all prerequisites, including certain class features available only to the warlock class. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can replace the invocation you know with another invocation that you could learn at that level. You use your levels in this class in place of warlock levels to determine whether you meet the prerequisites.</p><p>If an invocation allows you to cast a spell, you must have access to the appropriate spell level, even if the invocation does not require you to expend a spell slot to cast it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s318aab310b491a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Old Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two cantrips and three spells of your choice from the Druid spell list. A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3223950b2aae21a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Incarnate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Battle Tyrant.</strong> You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against any creature with the Frightened condition.</li><li><strong>Murderous Intent.</strong> When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for your Sneak Attack, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s323eeeb1418cb9f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fearless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"s32a92a796189fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Banishment Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Banishment, you can treat it as one spell level higher than the Spell Slot you expended for the purpose of determining its effects and it does not count against your Concentration limit, though the initial instance of the spell ends if you cast it again.</p><p>If you fail a Concentration Saving Throw and you are currently Concentration on more than one spell, you lose Concentration on both spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s32cdd1fa943f99d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire Lord","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of fire allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of flame.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You shed bright light in a 60 feet radius and dim light in a radius of 30 feet beyond that.</li><li>You gain Immunity to fire damage.</li><li>Creatures in the bright light have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against infusions that include the fire element.</li><li>You radiate intense heat in a 10 feet radius around you. Any creature of your choice that enters that radius for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, takes half your kinetic shape damage.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s32f53968a5592a9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roving","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you aren't wearing Heavy armor. You also have a Climb Speed and a Swim Speed equal to your Speed.</p><p>Additionally, you can use your Dexterity modifier in place of your Strength modifier when you make an Ability Check to swim or climb.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s337ee1b730fc242","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oathbreaker Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain oathbreaker spells at the paladin levels listed.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Oathbreaker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Paladin Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Hellish Rebuke, Inflict Wounds</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Crown of Madness, Darkness</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Animate Dead, Bestow Curse</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Blight, Confusion</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Contagion, Dominate Person</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s338ad46588d820f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unstable Backlash","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are imperiled during your rage, the magic within you can lash out; immediately after you take damage or fail a Saving Throw while raging, you can use your Reaction to roll on the Wild Magic table and immediately produce the effect rolled. This effect replaces your current Wild Magic effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s33b841e295896b2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aegis of Rime","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to cold damage.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that deals cold damage, you form a protective layer of magical ice on yourself.</p><p>While under this effect, the first time you take damage, that damage is reduced by an amount equal to your sorcerer level + your Charisma modifier. The effect then ends on you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s33beca676a91444","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dedicated Crafter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with one tool of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/hammer-sledge-steel-grey.webp","_id":"s33f7d2c96a38e13","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gathered Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A swarm of intangible nature spirits has bonded itself to you and can assist you in battle. While you're alive, the swarm remains in your space, crawling on you or flying and skittering around you within your space. You determine its appearance, or you generate its appearance by rolling on the Swarm Appearance table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Swarm Appearance</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d4</th><th scope=\"col\">Appearance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Swarming insects</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Miniature twig blights</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fluttering birds</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Playful pixies</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Once on each of your turns, you can cause the swarm to assist you in one of the following ways, immediately after you hit a creature with an attack:</p><ul><li>The attack's target takes 1d6 piercing damage from the swarm.</li><li>The attack's target must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC or be moved by the swarm up to 15 feet horizontally in a direction of your choice.</li><li>You are moved by the swarm 15 feet horizontally in a direction of your choice.</li></ul><div><strong>It's Your Swarm</strong><p>A Swarmkeeper's swarm and spells are reflections of the character's bond with nature spirits. Take the opportunity to describe the swarm and the ranger's magic in play. For example, when your ranger casts gaseous form, they might appear to melt into the swarm, instead of a cloud of mist, or the Arcane Eye spell could create an extension of your swarm that spies for you. Such descriptions don't change the effects of spells, but they are an exciting opportunity to explore your character's narrative through their class abilities. For more guidance on customizing spells, see the \"Personalizing Spells\" section in chapter 3.</p><p>Also, remember that the swarm's appearance is yours to customize, and don't feel confined to a single appearance. Perhaps the spirits' look changes with the ranger's mood or with the seasons. You decide!</p></div","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s340250d2e329e66","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sigils of Warding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add Glyph of Warding to your spellbook and it doesn't count against the number of prepared spells for you. You can replace the material component of the spell with a use of one of your runes.</p><p>Additionally, you can also choose objects you or someone else is wearing as valid targets for the spell. If you do so, you cannot choose the Spell Glyph option of the spell.</p><p>You can place only one glyph in this manner and if you place a new one in this manner, the first one disappears.</p><p>Additionally, when you cast Glyph of Warding, you can choose a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier. The chosen creatures are exempt from the Glyph's effect when it is triggered.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s34406b31e4c8d1e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rune Maven","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke each rune twice. When you finish a Short Rest, you now can regain two uses of one rune or one use of two different runes of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s344e3e6e26f5712","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bond of Fang and Scale","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you share with your drake intensifies, protecting you and stoking the drake's fury. When you summon your drake, it grows wings on its back and gains a Fly Speed equal to its Speed.</p><p>In addition, while your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Drake Mount.</strong> The drake grows to Large size. Its Hit Points increase by 1 for each of your levels in this class.</li><li><strong>Elemental Infusion.</strong> The drake's Bite and Elemental Bolt attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence and counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> You gain Resistance to the damage type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s349ed4f3101639a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ceaseless Pursuit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature within your Unnerving Aura moves away from you, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed towards it without provoking Attacks of Opportunity, then make an Attack of Opportunity against that creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s34b17d15847f184","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can interfere with the flow of ki in an opponent's body. When you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack, you can spend 1 ki point to attempt a stunning strike. The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or be Stunned until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-blue.webp","_id":"s34e0b3d0f61ad60","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weapon Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn a ritual that creates a magical bond between yourself and one weapon. You perform the ritual over the course of 1 hour, which can be done during a Short Rest. The weapon must be within your reach throughout the ritual, at the conclusion of which you touch the weapon and forge the bond.</p><p>Once you have bonded a weapon to yourself, you can't be Disarmed of that weapon unless you are Incapacitated. If it is on the same plane of existence, you can summon that weapon as a Bonus Action on your turn, causing it to teleport instantly to your hand.</p><p>You can have up to two bonded weapons, but can summon only one at a time with your Bonus Action. If you attempt to bond with a third weapon, you must break the bond with one of the other two.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3514f4b359dfa0f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack (2)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack three times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s35422960a346916","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Viper's Venom","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you damage a creature with a weapon affected by your Rite of the Viper, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Hemocraft save DC. You can force a creature to make this Saving Throw only once per turn.</p><p>On a failure, a target is Poisoned for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turn, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s35cbadf0b73de38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Spirit Claw.</strong> When you are hidden, you ignore Immunity to the Lacerated condition and healing does not remove the Lacerated condition if it was applied by you unless the target was healed back to its hitpoint maximum. Additionally, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that are Lacerated.</li><li><strong>Feline Grace.</strong> No Attack Roll has Advantage against you and you cannot have Disadvantage on Dexterity Saving Throws and Ability Checks. You lose these benefits when you are Incapacitated or your Speed is 0.</li><li><strong>Killing Bite.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can immediately make another attack with them as a Bonus Action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s361a651a1b6bfc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Boons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Lunar phases influence your metamagic. Each lunar phase is associated with spells of the following schools of magic:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon.</strong> Abjuration and conjuration spells</li><li><strong>New Moon.</strong> Evocation and necromancy spells</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon.</strong> Divination and transmutation spells</li></ul><p>Whenever you use Metamagic on a spell from the Lunar Spells table or a spell of a school of magic associated with the lunar phase you are in, you can reduce the sorcery points spent by 1 (minimum 0). You can reduce the sorcery points spent for your Metamagic a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s37097aa4de77cfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Forbidden Studies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficient in the Medicine skill. If you are already Proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p><p>Additionally, you can target a friendly dying creature with Shocking Grasp to resuscitate it. If you hit, the attack does not count as a critical hit, but the target still suffers one Death Saving Throw failure. It then regains hit points equal to half the lightning damage done. This feature cannot target creatures that have already incurred two Death Saving Throw failures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s37237360468ebf4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Jolt","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn new ways to channel arcane energy to harm or heal. When either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:</p><ul><li>The target takes an extra 2d6 force damage.</li><li>Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 hit points to it.</li></ul><p>You can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once on a turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"2d6","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/explosion-impact-shock-wave.webp","_id":"s37407b6e4b2bbf3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Divine power infuses you in battle. You gain one of the following options of your choice (if you get either option from a Cleric subclass in an older book, use only the option you choose for this feature).</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Strike.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll using a weapon, you can cause the target to take an extra 1d8 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice). At your DM's discretion, you can replace one of these options with a different damage type appropriate for your cleric subclass.</li><li><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> Add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Cleric cantrip.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/projectiles-blades-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s3776b6ddbda5236","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rider's Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Wyvern Companion gains a variety of benefits while it is bonded to you.</p><p>The companion obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own.</p><p>Your Wyvern Companion has abilities and game statistics determined in part by your level. Your companion uses your Proficiency bonus rather than its own. In addition to the areas where it normally uses its Proficiency bonus, a Wyvern Companion also adds its Proficiency bonus to its AC and to its damage rolls.</p><p>For each level you gain after 3rd, your Wyvern Companion gains an additional hit die and increases its hit points accordingly.</p><p>Whenever you gain the Ability Score Improvement class feature, your companion's abilities also improve. Your companion can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or it can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, your companion can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature unless its description specifies otherwise.</p><p>Whenever you use your Second Wind, your Wyvern Companion also regains hit points equal to 5 + your Fighter level.</p><p>Whenver you use Action Surge, your Wyvern Companion can also immediately make one bite attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s37c667a694c53b5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutal Beating","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action and use your Sneak Attack, you can immediately make another attack. If the target is suffering from a condition, you can add half your Sneak Attack dice (rounded down) to that attack.</p><p>You also learn the following new way to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Stun (Cost: 6d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or become Stunned until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s37d8ab170f341ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to peer at a creature and magically discern how best to hurt it. As an Action, choose one creature you can see within 60 feet of you. You immediately learn whether the creature has any damage Immunities, Resistances, or vulnerabilities and what they are. If the creature is hidden from divination magic, you sense that it has no damage Immunities, Resistances, or vulnerabilities.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s38302e6422e1b5b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warping Implosion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unleash your aberrant power as a space-warping anomaly. As a Bonus Action, you can teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 120 feet of you. Immediately after you disappear, each creature within 30 feet of the space you left must make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 4d10 force damage and is pulled straight toward the space you left, ending in an unoccupied space as close to your former space as possible. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pulled.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s383793cf319ed39","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Call to Arms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you are not incapacitated or Surprised at the start of combat, you can add your Leadership modifier to the initiative roll of all allies of your choice within 60 feet that can see or you and aren't incapacitated or Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/flags/banner-sword-blue.webp","_id":"s3878a2fac7f828b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark One's Own Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on your patron to alter fate in your favor. When you make an Ability Check or a Saving Throw, you can use this feature to add a d10 to your roll. You can do so after seeing the initial roll but before any of the roll's effects occur.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/unholy/demon-fanged-horned-yellow.webp","_id":"s3892d6737a5704a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Pack Tactics.</strong> You have Advantage on Attack Rolls with your natural weapons against a creature if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't Incapacitated.</li><li><strong>A Friend in Deed.</strong> You can take the Help action as a Bonus Action and with a range of 30 feet. You can always use the Help action to give someone Advantage on a skill check, even if you are not proficient in the relevant skill yourself.</li><li><strong>Thick Hide.</strong> The temporary hit points gained through your Martial Mastery (Unarmored Defense) increase by half (rounded down). Additionally, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against becoming Poisoned or Lacerated.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s38b4e5ef228bf67","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Patron","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have struck a bargain with an otherworldly being chosen from the list of available patrons. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p><p>Additionally, spells from the expanded spell list are now learned automatically and do not count against the number of warlock spells known.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/lights/candles-lit-red-evil.webp","_id":"s38be1c50c4a9c63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiosis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to meld with your Eidolon's essence, two creatures merged as one, fighting in perfect unison.</p><p>As an Action, when you are within 5 feet of your Eidolon, you can merge forms with it, entering Symbiosis. The resulting form can be that of your Eidolon, your own, or something in-between.</p><p>In this form, you gain all your Eidolon's features and evolution feats, and you choose whether to use your own or your Eidolon's stats for each ability score and armor class. You gain your Eidolon's hitpoints as temporary hitpoints. All features and effects that normally affect your Eidolon's hitpoints affect these temporary hitpoints as well. If these temporary hitpoints reach 0, your Eidolon disappears and you lose the benefits of Symbiosis and revert to your normal form. You can also relinquish the Symbiosis and split up into a summoner and Eidolon as an Action.</p><p>You also retain all of your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the Eidolon.</p><p>You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them. And you can use any special senses available to your Eidolon and you.</p><p>When you transform, you choose whether your equipment merges into the new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal. The DM determines whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the form's shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change shape or size to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must merge into your new form. Equipment that merges has no effect in that state.</p><p>While in this form, you can cast all summoner spells as a Bonus Action. Summoner class features that normally require you to be separate entities to work, allow you to target a different beneficiary instead, treating it as the summoner. In the case of Twin Eidolon, you instead completely duplicate your merged form for the duration and it receives all benefits from equipment that you are wearing and currently using in that form as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39273ed3f247726","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Artifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You develop a mystical connection to your magic items, which you can draw on for protection:</p><ul><li>You gain a +1 bonus to all Saving Throws per magic item you are currently attuned to.</li><li>If you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your Reaction to expend a use of Flash of Genius and change your hit points to 20 instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"20","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-beam-blue.webp","_id":"s39448dc50dc7661","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Blessed Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The option you chose for Blessed Strikes grows more powerful.</p><ul><li><strong>Divine Strike.</strong> The extra damage of your Divine Strike increases to 2d8.</li><li><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> When you cast a spell that deals damage, you can add your Wisdom modifier to one damage roll of that spell.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/projectile-beams-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s394fbd3e4bf2b29","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Mushrooms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you or your bonded familiar can cause enchanted mushrooms to spring up from the ground in a 10-feet circle around a point you can see within 60 feet.</p><p>The effect of the mushrooms depends on the type you choose from the options below, which you can activate as a Reaction when a creature steps into the area. Immediately afterwards, the mushrooms disappear.</p><p><strong>Fortifying Fungus.</strong> The triggering creature and all other creatures in the area gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch level.</p><p><strong>Nightcap.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, they fall asleep until the start of the triggering creature's next turn. An affected creature wakes up early if it takes damage or another creature uses an Action to shake it awake.</p><p><strong>Venomgill.</strong> The triggering creature and all creatures in the area have to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failure, they are Poisoned until the start of the triggering creature's next turn.</p><p>You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39a7b537b2c3221","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Poisoned Beauty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use a shard of the Spider Queen's alien beauty, causing other creatures to become enraptured by your appearance. As a Bonus Action, pick a creature you can see. That creature must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw or become Charmed by you. While Charmed, it also gains vulnerability to poison damage. This benefit lasts for one minute or until you or your allies damages the creature. Once you use this ability, you cannot use it again until you complete a Short or a Long Rest, unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39d4e12f089109d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You harbor a wellspring of psionic energy within yourself. It is represented by your Psionic Energy Dice, which fuel powers you have from this subclass. The Psi Warrior Energy Dice table shows the die size and number of these dice you have when you reach certain Fighter levels.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Psi Warrior Energy Dice</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Die Size</th><th scope=\"col\">Number</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>D6</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>D8</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>D8</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>D10</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>D10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>D12</td><td>12</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Any features in this subclass that use a Psionic Energy Die use only the dice from this subclass. Some of your powers expend the Psionic Energy Die, as specified in a power's description, and you can't use a power if it requires you to use a die when all your Psionic Energy Dice are expended.</p><p>You regain one of your expended Psionic Energy Dice when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all of them when you finish a Long Rest.</p><ul><li><strong>Protective Field.</strong> When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can take a Reaction to expend one Psionic Energy Die, roll the die, and reduce the damage taken by the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum reduction of 1), as you create a momentary shield of telekinetic force.</li><li><strong>Psionic Strike.</strong> You can propel your weapons with psionic force. Once on each of your turns, immediately after you hit a target within 30 feet of yourself with an attack and deal damage to it with a weapon, you can expend one Psionic Energy Die, rolling it and dealing Force damage to the target equal to the number rolled plus your Intelligence modifier.</li><li><strong>Telekinetic Movement.</strong> You can move an object or a creature with your mind. As a Magic action, choose one target you can see within 30 feet of yourself; the target must be a loose object that is Large or smaller or one willing creature other than you. You transport the target up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Alternatively, if the target is a Tiny object, you can transport it to or from your hand.</li><li>Once you take this action, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest unless you expend a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) to restore your use of it.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39eb74812f31d72","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summoner's Call","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to call your Eidolon to your side. It appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you that you can see.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s39ff5dcc4940fff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword Sage's Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Arcane Aegis to protect an ally, you can choose up to three creatures to gain its benefits. (You are a valid target as well).</p><p>Additionally, when you have no Reaction remaining and a creature triggers the Reaction attack from your Arcane Aegis feature, you can spend 2 sorcery points to use the attack without a Reaction. You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3a3e423abedbf0f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reckless Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can throw aside all concern for defense to attack with increased ferocity. When you make your first Attack Roll on your turn, you can decide to attack recklessly. Doing so gives you Advantage on Attack Rolls using Strength until the start of your next turn, but Attack Rolls against you have Advantage during that time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blade-tips-triple-bent-white.webp","_id":"s3a7eb1cd4584162","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heightened Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Flurry of Blows.</strong> You can expend 1 Ki Point to use Flurry of Blows and make three Unarmed Strikes with it instead of two.</li><li><strong>Patient Defense.</strong> When you expend a Ki Point to use Patient Defense, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die.</li><li><strong>Step of the Wind.</strong> When you expend a Ki Point to use Step of the Wind, you can choose a willing creature within 5 feet of yourself that is Large or smaller. You move the creature with you until the end of your turn. The creature's movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s3aa5701e436bb2f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kensai Kai","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to infuse your monk weapons with some of your Ki, making them even more deadly. Your critical range with your monk weapons increases by 1.</p><p>Additionally, when you deal damage with a monk weapon, you can spend 1 Ki Point to deal additional damage equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3b6e105f135adf3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Prey","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/dissolve-bone-skull.webp","_id":"s3b8816482bb2a3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Know Your Enemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your keen sense of observation allows you to spot weaknesses in your foe's defense. As a Bonus Action, you can make a Wisdom (Insight) check against a creature you can see within 60 feet. The DC is equal to 10 + half the creature's challenge rating (rounded down) or the creature's passive deception, whichever is higher. On a success, the creature has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw against one of your maneuvers before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3bad60190386eeb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aether Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can magically step into the veil between the planes as long as you aren't Incapacitated. Your movement doesn't provoke Attacks of Opportunity and you can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3, as well as see and affect creatures and objects on the Ethereal Plane. You take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside an object.</p><p>This feature lasts for one minute. If you are inside an object when it ends, you are immediately shunted to the nearest unoccupied space and you take force damage equal to twice the number of feet you moved.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest - or until you spend a use of your Blood Maledict to regain it. You can use Aether Walk twice between rests starting at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3bb65f8bc503edd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stormborn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Fly Speed equal to your current Speed whenever you are not underground or indoors, and gain Resistance to lighting and thunder damage.</p><p>Additionally, you regain all expended uses of your Wrath of the Storm subclass feature when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3bbcde66687f7d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heroic Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Reaction to recover hitpoints equal to half your hitpoint maximum. Once you use this feature, you cannot use it again until you complete a Long Rest. You can spend three uses of your Indomitable feature to regain a use of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3bdcd22a0fea152","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Vitality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can expend a use of your Formshift to immediately regain hit points equal to twice your Shifter level. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["2 * @classes.shifter.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/bear-roar-bite-brown-green.webp","_id":"s3c186bc530ade0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Elemental Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The option you chose for Elemental Fury grows more powerful:</p><p><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> When you cast a Druid spell of 1st level or higher that deals damage, you add your Wisdom modifier to one damage roll of the spell.</p><p><strong>Primal Strike.</strong> The extra damage of your Primal Strike increases to 2d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-large-teal.webp","_id":"s3c45a8e29e25c55","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved War Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can cast a spell in place of two of your melee weapon attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3c4605fdc4d2a2a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfect Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have developed your body and mind to new heights. Your Strength or Dexterity score (your choice) and Wisdom scores increase by 4, to a maximum of 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp","_id":"s3c547bf4bc37a31","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dragon Wings","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to sprout a pair of dragon wings from your back, gaining a Fly Speed equal to your current Speed. You can create these wings as a Bonus Action on your turn. They last until you dismiss them as a Bonus Action on your turn.</p><p>You can't manifest your wings while wearing armor unless the armor is made to accommodate them, and clothing not made to accommodate your wings might be destroyed when you manifest them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/wing-batlike-white-blue.webp","_id":"s3c58b0acff30ef5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Awakened Season","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The effect of your Awakened Season improves in the following ways:</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Affected creatures that start their turn in the area or enter it for the first time on a turn, regain hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. This effect does not receive the bonus healing from Awakened Season.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any radiant or fire damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any lightning or necrotic damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> You add your spellcasting ability modifier to any cold damage you deal to affected creatures in the area.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3c5fdab0e1e50a8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slippery Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have acquired greater mental strength. You gain Proficiency in two out of the following Saving Throws: Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/illusion-evasion-echo-purple.webp","_id":"s3c79b0ebd19a7e3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aegis of Faith","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any creature that currently has temporary hitpoints from your Armor of Faith, is also considered to be under the effect of the Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3c801be623fbfb6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bulwark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally within 60 feet of you fails a Saving Throw, you can expend a use of your Indomitable class feature as a Reaction to grant its benefit to that ally.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3caeeb09d52f42b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Disciplined","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use heavy weapons despite being small.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-guard-steel-green.webp","_id":"s3cc788b16c2872f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lay on Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blessed touch can heal wounds. You have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you take a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of hit points equal to your paladin level × 5.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can touch a creature and draw power from the pool to restore a number of hit points to that creature, up to the maximum amount remaining in your pool.</p><p>Alternatively, you can expend 5 hit points from your pool of healing to cure the target of one disease or neutralize one poison affecting it. You can cure multiple diseases and neutralize multiple poisons with a single use of Lay on Hands, expending hit points separately for each one.</p><p>This feature has no effect on undead and constructs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"5 * @classes.paladin.levels","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"s3cc9b74ee453a2a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slow Fall","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Reaction when you fall to reduce any falling damage you take by an amount equal to five times your monk level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you fall"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"5 * @classes.monk.levels","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/pseudopod-teal.webp","_id":"s3d0f3f5775593c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of the Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to lightning and thunder damage.</p><p>In addition, whenever you start casting a spell of 1st level or higher that deals lightning or thunder damage, stormy magic erupts from you. This eruption causes creatures of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of you to take lightning or thunder damage (choose each time this ability activates) equal to half your sorcerer level. You can deal this damage before, during, or after the movement granted by your Tempestuous Magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3d2c682e95fbb7b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Evocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of any wizard evocation spell you cast.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/explosion-mushroom-nuke-orange.webp","_id":"s3d616069a5af1d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Victory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1) to the damage of your melee weapon attacks while your Bladesong is active.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3da013e546c8caf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells from the Wizard spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3dbe8610aec9c13","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tranquil Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As long as you have at least 1 hit point, you regain hit points equal to half your paladin level + your Charisma modifier at the start of every one of your turns.</p><p>If you deal damage to a creature, force it to make a Saving Throw, or otherwise target it with a harmful effect, this feature stops working until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3e0e0693b098cf7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Preparation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in initiative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3e222e69f59ca89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can expend 3 Ki Points to bolster yourself against harm for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition. During that time, you have Resistance to all damage except Force damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"at the start of your turn"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s3e3628faf73515a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fast Movement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet while you aren't wearing heavy armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"s3e5eb6e2b9e7df9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura Improvements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The range of your Aura of Protection increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/barrier-wall-explosion-orange.webp","_id":"s3e75fda6c70977d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bewitching Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron grants you the ability to weave your magic with teleportation. Immediately after you cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell using an action and a spell slot or as part of a Mystic Arcanum use, you can cast Misty Step as part of the same action and without expending a spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3eb3002eedfc045","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grasping Tentacles","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the spell Evard's Black Tentacles. It counts as a warlock spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of spells you know. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Whenever you cast this spell, your patron's magic bolsters you, granting you a number of temporary hit points equal to your warlock level. Moreover, damage can't break your Concentration on this spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3ebf0dfb1d24e9f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inner Sun","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 1 to 10 Ki Points as an Action and bathe the area in a 30-foot Emanation in a blinding light. Each creature of your choice in the area has to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, a target takes 1d10 radiant damage per Ki Point spent and is Blinded until the end of your next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't Blinded.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3ef6f97321d0522","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Elves don't need to sleep. Instead, they meditate deeply, remaining semiconscious, for 4 hours a day. While meditating, you can dream after a fashion; such dreams are actually mental excercises that have become reflexive through years of practice. After resting in this way, you gain the same benefit that a human does from 8 hours of sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp","_id":"s3f0d495d5acfd63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dispelling Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to lace your shots with disruptive magic. Once per turn, when you hit with a ranged weapon attack, you can end any spells of 3rd level or lower on the target.</p><p>For each spell of 4th level or higher on the target, make an Ability Check using the ability score for your Arcane Shot save DC. The DC equals 10 + the caster's spellcasting ability modifier + the spell slot level of the target spell - 3. On a successful check, the spell ends.</p><p>You can use this features a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. You can also expend a use of your Arcane Shot to use this feature again (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f0df4c714638df","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Minor Arcana","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can expend one pact magic spell slot to gain a number of free castings for lesser spells until you finish your next Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>You can choose only warlock spells that you know and each chosen spell must not have a clause that grants it additional or enhanced effects when it is cast at a higher level. The total spell level of the chosen spells must be equal to or lower than the level of the expended pact magic slot. You can choose the same spell multiple times.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a Short or a Long Rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-eye-purple.webp","_id":"s3f21066df704f6e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artificer's Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make an INT-check related to magic items, alchemical objects, or technological devices, you have Advantage on the check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-worn-blue.webp","_id":"s3f26aa65663b951","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hold the Line","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are not incapacitated, Attack Rolls against allies that benefit from your Formation Fighting cannot have Advantage. Additionally, you and all allies under the effect of your Formation Fighting add your Leadership ability modifier to Saving Throws and Ability Checks against being knocked prone, pushed, or otherwise forced to move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f2f6e963b7b9ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spectral Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to move between planes enables you to slip through the planar boundaries to lessen the harm done to you during battle. When you take damage from an attack or an effect that requires you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to give yourself Resistance to all of that attack's damage on this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f420c6d4417180","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Trickster's Transposition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you take the Bonus Action to create or move the illusion of your Invoke Duplicity, you can teleport, swapping places with the illusion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3f80a30ab6a16f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transport","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and up to 5 creatures of your choosing that you can see are grasped by tentacles that emerge from the portal. A second portal opens at a point of your choice within 100 miles that you have visited in the past 24 hours, depositing you and your chosen allies there.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3fa4279605e4b75","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Shot Options","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Arcane Shot feature lets you choose options for it at certain levels. The options are presented here in alphabetical order. They are all magical effects, and each one is associated with one of the schools of magic.</p><p>If an option requires a Saving Throw, your Arcane Shot save DC is calculated as follows:</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Arcane Shot save DC</strong> = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Intelligence modifier + your Wisdom modifier</p><h5>Banishing Shot</h5><p>You use abjuration magic to try to temporarily banish your target to a harmless demiplane. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x Proficiency extra force damage and must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw or be banished. While banished in this way, the target is Incapacitated. At the end of its next turn, the target reappears in the space it vacated or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied.</p><h5>Beguiling Shot</h5><p>Your enchantment magic causes this projectile to temporarily beguile its target. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x Proficiency extra psychic damage, and choose one of your allies within 30 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it is Charmed by the chosen ally for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><h5>Bursting Shot</h5><p>You imbue your projectile with force energy drawn from the school of evocation. The energy detonates after your attack. Immediately after the projectile hits the creature, The target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take D6 x your Proficiency force damage.</p><h5>Dimensional Shot</h5><p>You target an unoccupied space within 20 x your Proficiency ft that you can see instead of a creature. You shoot the projectile at the location and then teleport towards it. Any effect that prevents the projectile from reaching its destination also cuts short your teleport. In such a case you instead teleport to where the projectile was stopped or to the nearest unoccupied space of your choice.</p><h5>Enfeebling Shot</h5><p>You weave necromantic magic into your projectile. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra necrotic damage. The target must also succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw, or the damage dealt by its weapon attacks is halved for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><h5>Grasping Shot</h5><p>When this projectile strikes its target, transmutation magic turns it into grasping, poisonous brambles, which wrap around the target. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra poison damage, its Speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it takes D6 x your Proficiency slashing damage the first time on each turn it moves 1 foot or more without teleporting. The target or any creature that can reach it can use its action to remove the brambles with a successful Strength (Athletics) check against your Arcane Shot save DC. Otherwise, the brambles last for 1 minute or until you use this option again.</p><h5>Seeking Shot</h5><p>Using divination magic, you grant your projectile the ability to seek out a target. When you use this option, you don't make an Attack Roll for the attack. Instead, choose one creature you have seen in the past minute. The projectile flies toward that creature, moving around corners if necessary and ignoring three-quarters cover and half cover. If the target is within the weapon's range and there is a path large enough for the projectile to travel to the target, the target must make a Dexterity Saving Throw. Otherwise, the projectile disappears after traveling as far as it can. On a failed save, the target takes damage as if it were hit by the projectile, plus an extra D6 x your Proficiency force damage, and you learn the target's current location. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and you don't learn its location.</p><h5>Shadow Shot</h5><p>You weave illusion magic into your projectile, causing it to occlude your foe's vision with shadows. The creature hit by the projectile takes D6 x your Proficiency extra psychic damage, and it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be unable to see anything farther than 5 feet away for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3fc663be2af8f35","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to psychic damage, and you have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed or Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s3fd530b07b2e65b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Illusionist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Minor Illusion cantrip. Your spellcasting ability for it is INT, WIS, or CHA (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-firefly-hand-yellow.webp","_id":"s3fdfd3b4179f435","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Distant Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make a ranged weapon attack, you can spend 1 ki point to prevent attacking at long range from imposing Disadvantage on your Attack Rolls until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make a ranged weapon attack at long range"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/projectile-spiral-gray.webp","_id":"s40045b9d3cea955","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Drain Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now use Drain Magic as a Bonus Action. In addition, when you use Drain Magic, you can end one ongoing level 1, level 2, or level 3 spell on the target, and the target recovers one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower (the target's choice). Alternatively, you regain a number of Empower Sneak Attack uses equal to the spell's level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4077cd03978ecbc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bloodthirst","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If your Sneak Attack hits a Bloodied or Lacerated creature, the target takes extra damage of the weapon's type equal to half your Rogue level (round up). In addition, when an enemy you can see is reduced to 0 Hit Points, you can take a Reaction and move up to your Speed. You can then make one melee attack. You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice, minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s40c01f5c667920a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beguiling Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron teaches you how to guard your mind and body. You are immune to the Charmed condition.</p><p>In addition, immediately after a creature you can see hits you with an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage you take by half (round down), and you can force the attacker to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker takes Psychic damage equal to the damage you take. Once you use this Reaction, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s40c26fd6d82c3b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Crimson Rite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to invoke a rite of hemocraft that infuses your weapon strikes with elemental energy. As a Bonus Action, you can activate any rite you know on one weapon you're holding. The effect of the rite lasts until you finish a Short or a Long Rest. When you activate a rite, you take necrotic damage equal to one roll of your hemocraft die. This damage can't be reduced in any way.</p><p>While the rite is in effect, attacks you make with this weapon are magical, and deal extra damage equal to your hemocraft die of the type determined by the chosen rite. A weapon can hold only one active rite at a time. Other creatures can't gain the benefit of your rite.</p><p>If you have a Crimson Rite active on a weapon you're holding and a creature within 30 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points by an effect that includes the chosen damage type, you regain one Hit Die, which you can spend immediately as if you had taken a Rest. This effect cannot be triggered again until the start of your next turn.</p><p>You choose one rite from the crimson rites below when you first gain this feature. You learn an additional crimson rite at 7th level, and again at 14th level.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Flame.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is fire damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Frozen.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is cold damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Storm.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is lightning damage.</p><p><strong>Rite of the Dead.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is necrotic damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p><p><strong>Rite of the Oracle.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is psychic damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p><p><strong>Rite of the Roar.</strong> The extra damage dealt by your rite is thunder damage. (Prerequisite: 14th level)</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.bloodhunter.hemocraft","necrotic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-sword-dagger-runes-red.webp","_id":"s40ffa3cbe889123","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battle Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered the art of weaving spellcasting and weapon use into a single harmonious act. When you use your action to cast a bard spell, you can make one weapon attack as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4119306a339c8bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unbreakable Majesty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can assume a magically majestic presence for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition. For the duration, whenever any creature hits you with an Attack Roll for the first time on a turn, the attacker must succeed on a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or the attack misses instead, as the creature recoils from your majesty.</p><p>Once you assume this majestic presence, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4120aced537eae3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond you share with your drake creates a connection to dragonkind, granting you understanding and empowering your presence. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Thaumaturgy.</strong> You learn the Thaumaturgy cantrip, which is a ranger spell for you.</li><li><strong>Tongue of Dragons.</strong> You learn to speak, read, and write Draconic or one other language of your choice.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s418994bd26bed94","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Strength and Constitution scores increase by 2, up to a maximum of 22.</p><p>In addition, you can now use Jotun Rage twice between rests, but no more than once on a turn. If you use that feature while under its effects, its increases to your size, hit points, reach, and Speed are cumulative.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s41be8efae438dd2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spiked Retribution","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are wearing spiked armor and a creature touches you (e.g. by grappling you or hitting you with a natural weapon attack) or hits you with a melee attack from within 5 ft, it takes piercing damage equal to your Proficiency bonus. If your armor has a permanent bonus to its armor class (e.g. the masterwork property), you add this bonus to the damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s420047d17998f64","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serpent's Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet and Blindsight with a range of 10 feet. If you already possess either sense, its range increases by the same amount.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s42260130b26dfb3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nourishing Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your fire spells soothe and restore you. When you expend a spell slot to cast a spell that includes a fire damage roll, you regain hit points equal to the slot's level + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4256aca0455756a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Surge (Level 18)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two allies within 60 feet of you, rather than one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s426a873726f61d4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alleyway Rituals","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following additional Cauldron Rituals:</p><p><strong>Beguiling Performance.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target performs a Perform check, it can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If the Perform check is successful, it treats the result of the roll as 1 step better.</p><p><strong>Drunkard's Luck.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target makes a Carouse check, it adds your spellcasting ability modifier to the result of the d20 roll.</p><p><strong>Eagle Eyes.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target performs a Guard check, it can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If the Guard check results in an encounter, the target cannot be surprised and adds your spellcasting ability modifier to its initiative roll.</p><p><strong>Gutter Remedies.</strong> When you perform an Attend check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If your Attend check is successful, you roll an additional d4 and add it to the result of the die on the result column.</p><p><strong>Magpie's Blessing.</strong> Choose one creature. When the target makes a Pickpocket check, it rolls 2d8 and adds them to the result of the die on the result column if the check was successful. If the check was a failure, it adds your spellcasting ability modifier to any checks made to evade the authorities.</p><p><strong>Twisted Fortune.</strong> Choose one creature. The target rolls 2d8 and adds them to the result of the die on the result column, regardless of whether the Gambling check was successful or not.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4281386c8d82454","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Archetype","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an archetype from the list available that you strive to emulate in your combat styles and techniques. The archetype you choose grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow.webp","_id":"s42945edbe562211","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Piercing Thorns","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your command of primal magic allows you to enhance your attacks with thorns. Once during each of your turns, you can deal an additional 1d6 piercing damage to one creature you hit with a weapon attack. This damage increases to 2d6 when your reach 11th level in this class.</p><p>If your weapon counts as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage, this damage does as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s42b28f02679d912","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Mobility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet. If you have a Climb Speed or Swim Speed, this increase applies to that Speed as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s43d204b3abfdbd0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Power of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a magical benefit based on a totem animal of your choice. You can choose the same animal you selected previously or a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s44086ecf148c8ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed, and magic can't put you to sleep.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s4410bd541039acd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flurry of Healing and Harm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now mete out a flurry of comfort and hurt. When you use Flurry of Blows, you can now replace each of the Unarmed Strikes with a use of your Hand of Healing, without spending ki points for the healing.</p><p>In addition, when you make an Unarmed Strike with Flurry of Blows, you can use Hand of Harm with that strike without spending the ki point for Hand of Harm. You can still use Hand of Harm only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4444bc3990a0547","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strongheart Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with light and medium armor as well as the longsword, battleaxe, longbow, and heavy crossbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/swords-short.webp","_id":"s44e9390e233d74e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Stalker's Ambush.</strong> Any attack with your natural weapons against a creature that is Surprised has Advantage and adds an additional roll of your Natural Weapons die to the damage.</li><li><strong>Swift Climber.</strong> You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and when you take fall damage, you can use your Reaction to decrease that damage by an amount equal to five times your Shifter level.</li><li><strong>Feral Pounce.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and your attack hits, you can force the target to make a Strength Saving Throw if it is no more than one size larger than you. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target is knocked Prone.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s44fea0edf77deec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oceanic Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manifest two water orbs instead of one when you use Wrath of the Sea and all features that affect one water orb, affect both.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4522d7a7d6d056d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visions of the Past","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call up visions of the past that relate to an object you hold or your immediate surroundings. You spend at least 1 minute in meditation and prayer, then receive dreamlike, shadowy glimpses of recent events. You can meditate in this way for a number of minutes equal to your Wisdom score and must maintain Concentration during that time, as if you were casting a spell.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Object Reading.</strong> Holding an object as you meditate, you can see visions of the object's previous owner. After meditating for 1 minute, you learn how the owner acquired and lost the object, as well as the most recent significant event involving the object and that owner. If the object was owned by another creature in the recent past (within a number of days equal to your Wisdom score), you can spend 1 additional minute for each owner to learn the same information about that creature.</p><p><strong>Area Reading.</strong> As you meditate, you see visions of recent events in your immediate vicinity (a room, street, tunnel, clearing, or the like, up to a 50-foot cube), going back a number of days equal to your Wisdom score. For each minute you meditate, you learn about one significant event, beginning with the most recent. Significant events typically involve powerful emotions, such as battles and betrayals, marriages and murders, births and funerals. However, they might also include more mundane events that are nevertheless important in your current situation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s452cf69135b4238","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hydrosophic Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to summon up your water-based defenses at a split-second's notice.</p><p>When you are hit by an attack or subject to an effect that forces you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to create a shield of water around you, granting yourself half-cover until the start of your next turn.</p><p>This cover applies even when against effects that normally ignore cover.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s45b9cff53465ffa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Domain","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one domain related to your deity from the list of available domains. Each domain is detailed in their own feature, and each one provides examples of gods associated with it. Your choice grants you domain spells and other features when you choose it at 3rd level. It also grants you additional ways to use Channel Divinity when you gain that feature at 3rd level, and additional benefits at 6th, 8th, and 17th levels.</p><p><strong>Domain Spells.</strong> Each domain has a list of spells—its domain spells—that you gain at the cleric levels noted in the domain description. Once you gain a domain spell, you always have it prepared, and it doesn't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.</p><p>If you have a domain spell that doesn't appear on the cleric spell list, the spell is nonetheless a cleric spell for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-spirit-blue.webp","_id":"s462d8a4bfe827ec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Guide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to control the weather in your vicinity. You and your companions do not suffer the effects of bad weather. Additionally, your travel speed is doubled if you are using a naval vessel for Overland Travel. Said vessel is likewise protected from bad weather effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s46c4fd3d2dd7e2d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to perceive the auras of other creatures.</p><p>As an Action, select a creature that you can see. That creature makes a Wisdom Saving Throw, though it has no knowledge that you forced it to attempt this Saving Throw. On a failed save, you learn if the creature shares any aspects of its alignment with you, its current hit points, and its current attitude and intentions toward you or one other creature, object, or location of your choice. In addition, for the next 24 hours or until you use this ability again, you can use an Action to determine the creature's distance and direction from you.</p><p>If a creature succeeds on its Saving Throw against this ability, you cannot use this ability against that creature again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s46d683a96946a17","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ki","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your focus and martial training allow you to harness a well of extraordinary energy within yourself. This energy is represented by Ki Points. Your Monk level determines the amount of Ki Points you have, as shown in the Ki Points column of the Monk Features table.</p><p>You can expend these points to enhance or fuel certain Monk features. You start knowing three such features: Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind, each of which is detailed below.</p><p>When you expend Ki Points, it is unavailable until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, at the end of which you regain all your expended Ki Points.</p><p>Some features that use Ki Points require your target to make a Saving Throw. The save DC equals 8 plus your Wisdom modifier and Proficiency Bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.monk.ki-points","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s483ca21a0fdaf13","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Tranquility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Sanctuary spell prepared.</p><p>As a Reaction when you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you is targeted by an attack or other harmful effect, you can cast Sanctuary without expending a spell slot, and you adopt a presence of tranquility for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. During this time, you can cast Sanctuary again as a Reaction without expending a spell slot.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s48915eb6b2f3a48","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Holy Arms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Sanctified Strike cantrip if you do not know it already. Additionally, you can cast Sanctified Strike in place of one attack when you take the attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s48b01c9c93b121f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cauldron Rituals","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn a number of special rituals that you can complete as part of a Short or Long Rest. You may only choose one of these rituals at a time and the effects last until you complete your next Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Bounty of the Earth.</strong> When you forage for food or ingredients, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. If your Foraging check is successful, you roll an additional d4 and add it to the result of the die on the result column.</p><p><strong>Eye of Newt, Wing of Bat.</strong> Select a number of non-masterwork consumables equal to your spellcasting ability modifier that your group crafted on this Adventuring Day using alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit. The selected items receive the masterwork property.</p><p><strong>Nature's Veil.</strong> When your group makes a Prepare Campsite check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. Additionally, you and up to 8 other creatures of your choice regain additional hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch Level when you complete your next Short Rest on this Adventuring Day.</p><p><strong>Snake Stomach.</strong> If your group consumes a meal as part of this rest, the duration of the effect is increased by 1 day. The same meal can only be affected by this ritual once.</p><p><strong>Whispers of the Wild.</strong> When your group makes a Lookout check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9. Additionally, you add your spellcasting ability modifier to your passive Perception and that of up to 8 other creatures of your choice.</p><p><strong>Witch Path.</strong> 3 doesn't slow your group's travel and whenever your group makes a Pathfinding check, you can treat a d20 roll of 8 or lower as a 9.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s48f896c45aff482","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ancient Fortitude","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the endurance of the ancient forests. Your hit point maximum and current hit points increase by 2 per ranger level when you assume your guardian form. This increase lasts until you leave the form; your hit point maximum then returns to normal, but your current hit points remain the same, unless they must decrease to abide by your hit point maximum.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s490034f3d9f94cc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Resurgence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once on each of your turns, if you have no uses of Wild Shape left, you can give yourself one use by expending a spell slot (no action required).</p><p>In addition, you can expend one use of Wild Shape (no action required) to give yourself a level 1 spell slot, but you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/spirit-deer-herd-blue.webp","_id":"s4962ee926bf80b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Wild","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You draw on the strange and ancient horrors of the land for power. While you are Concentrating on a Ranger spell or are under the effect of a Ranger spell that you have cast, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Ancient Armor.</strong> You gain a bonus to your AC equal to your Wisdom modifier. Your body is wreathed in rotten bark or beastly bristles.</li><li><strong>Unnerving Aura.</strong> When an enemy starts its turn within a 10-foot Emanation originating from you, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn. The shadows lengthen around you, insects begin to crawl out of the ground, or carrion birds circle overhead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s498286b31466de0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessing of the Serpent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to Gargan deepens, causing your unarmed attacks to count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>Additionally, you gain Resistance to lightning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s49ddf379e259046","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Snap Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are ever ready to spring into action. If you take the Attack action on your first turn of a combat, you can make one additional ranged weapon attack as part of that action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s49f887d504a2d1c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you regain expended uses of Bardic Inspiration until you have two if you have fewer than that.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/explosion-lava-stone-green.webp","_id":"s49f9c606f0441fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, all attacks granted to your allies through your Concerted Attack that target the same creature are made with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4a1e08e6cc08cd6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spreading Spores","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to seed an area with deadly spores. As a Bonus Action while your Symbiotic Entity feature is active, you can hurl spores up to 30 feet away, where they swirl in a 10-foot cube for 1 minute. The spores disappear early if you dismiss them as a Bonus Action, or if your Symbiotic Entity feature is no longer active.</p><p>Whenever a creature moves into the cube or starts its turn there, that creature takes your Halo of Spores damage, unless the creature succeeds on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. A creature can take this damage no more than once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4a872dc47c7ae6f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fight as One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion gains the Multiattack feature, which allows it to make two bite attacks as part of the same Action. When you use your Action Surge, your companion can make two bite attacks instead of one or use its Breath Weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ab87dbe2b730fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supreme Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12.</p><p>If the healing formula of the spell involves a static number (beside your spellcasting ability modifier), you increase that number by half, rounded down.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s4b0052055954de2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drake's Breath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can exhale a 30-foot cone of damaging breath or cause your drake to exhale it. Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison damage (your choice doesn't have to match your drake's Draconic Essence). Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC, taking 8d6 damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>This damage increases to 10d6 when you reach 15th level in this class.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4b3384dab4d48cb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are a master of navigating the natural world, and you react with swift and decisive action when attacked. This grants you the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You ignore 3.</li><li>You have Advantage on initiative rolls.</li><li>On your first turn during combat, you have Advantage on Attack Rolls against creatures that have not yet acted.</li></ul><p>In addition, you are skilled at navigating the wilderness. You gain the following benefits when traveling for an hour or more:</p><ul><li>Difficult terrain doesn't slow your group's travel.</li><li>Your group can't become lost except by magical means.</li><li>When performing a task during the Travelling Phase of Overland Travel, you may additionally perform the Lookout task or assist with it.</li><li>If you are traveling alone, you can move stealthily at a normal pace.</li><li>When you forage, you find twice as much food as you normally would.</li><li>While tracking other creatures, you also learn their exact number, their sizes, and how long ago they passed through the area.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s4b9c0949cd2f832","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elusive","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No Attack Roll has Advantage against you while you aren't Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-swirling-blue.webp","_id":"s4bbef3b52edb67f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beacon of Leadership","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All allied creatures within 30 feet of you gain the benefits of your Favored Enemy and Greater Favored Enemy features. This feature has no effect while you are Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4bc3df085355eb1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Quivering Palm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to set up lethal vibrations in someone's body. When you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike, you can expend 4 Ki Points to start these imperceptible vibrations, which last for a number of days equal to your Monk level. The vibrations are harmless unless you take an Action to end them. Alternatively, when you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of the attacks to end the vibrations. To end them, you and the target must be on the same plane of existence. When you end them, the target must make a Constitution Saving Throw, taking 10d12 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p>You can have only one creature under the effect of this feature at a time. You can end the vibrations harmlessly (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["10d12","force"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-black-pink.webp","_id":"s4bc7f09c1831b92","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frigid Explorer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Frost Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Cold damage.</li><li><strong>Hunter's Rime.</strong> When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d6 Cold damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn. This extra damage ignores Resistance to Cold damage. When you reach Ranger level 11, this extra damage increases to 2d6.</li><li>A creature that took damage from this feature cannot use the Dash or Disengange Actions until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4bcf1b3584a1a1e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Elegance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make a Charisma (Deception, Intimidation, or Persuasion) check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4be5ff9e32a60ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dagger in the Dark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are in dim light or darkness, you can reduce the cost of any feature that uses your Sneak Attack dice by 1 (to a minimum of 0). You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c448d06dfa10a9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Scourge of the Ancients","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Scourge of the Ancients feature, you can select two of the listed benefits instead of one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c6573480a3c595","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aquatic Affinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, it instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>Additionally the distance you can move your water orb increases to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4c9ed533069ba47","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thieves' Cant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>During your rogue training you learned thieves' cant, a secret mix of dialect, jargon, and code that allows you to hide messages in seemingly normal conversation. Only another creature that knows thieves' cant understands such messages. It takes four times longer to convey such a message than it does to speak the same idea plainly.</p><p>In addition, you understand a set of secret signs and symbols used to convey short, simple messages, such as whether an area is dangerous or the territory of a thieves' guild, whether loot is nearby, or whether the people in an area are easy marks or will provide a safe house for thieves on the run.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"s4ccae39bd92e8c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Thief","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Empower Sneak Attack, you can try to steal the knowledge of how to cast a spell from the caster. The DC equals 8 + your proficiency + your Intelligence. On a failed save, you negate the spell's effect, and you steal the knowledge of the spell. You can cast this spell once without expending a spell slot and without material components during the next 7 days. You can also cast it again by expending a number of uses of your Empower Sneak Attack equal to the spell's level. The original caster can't cast it until the 7 days have passed.</p><p>Once you have stolen a spell with this feature, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ce3608509c47b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bulwark of Force","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can shield yourself and others with telekinetic force. As a Bonus Action, you can choose creatures, which can include you, that you can see within 30 feet of you, up to a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one creature). Each of the chosen creatures is protected by half cover for 1 minute or until you're Incapacitated.</p><p>Once you take this Bonus Action, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to take it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d296455dab9972","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telekinetic Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Telekinesis spell prepared. With this feature, you can cast it without a spell slot or components, and your spellcasting ability for it is Intelligence. On each of your turns while you maintain Concentration on it, including the turn when you cast it, you can make one attack with a weapon as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so in this way again until you finish a Long Rest unless you expend a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d33a897e81f813","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thrill of Victory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally that you can see within 60 ft of you and that can see or hear you, reduces a creature to 0 hitpoints, it can immediately regain a hit die. This feature has no effect if you're incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d8ef7feee6bf63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Formation Fighting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are not incapacitated, allies within 5 ft of you have half-cover against weapon attacks and you add your Leadership ability modifier to the damage roll of the first weapon attack they hit with on a turn. You can extend this benefit to allies that are farther than 5 ft away from you, as long as they are within 5 ft of an ally that already is under the effect of this feature and isn't incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4d97e22f1f96db8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Silver Sisters Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Silver Sisters Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Shield, Zephyr Strike, Magic Weapon, Branding Smite</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Blinding Smite, Spirit Guardians</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fount of Moonlight, Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Moon Cloak, Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4e4918091d33ef4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grim Satisfaction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever a creature fails a Saving Throw against one of your Witch spells or features, you and your bonded familiar gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier + half your Witch level (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4e657320a3d2878","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Explosive Cannon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every Eldritch Cannon you create is now more destructive. You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Detonate.</strong> When your cannon takes damage, you can take a Reaction to command the cannon to detonate if you are within 60 feet of it. Doing so destroys the cannon and forces each creature within 20 feet of it to make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 3d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p><p><strong>Firepower.</strong> The cannon's damage rolls and the number of Temporary Hit Points granted by Protector increase by 1d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":20,"width":null,"units":"ft","type":"sphere"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["3d10","force"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"dex","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/explosion-fireball-large-red-orange.webp","_id":"s4e74287fc3a11af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limited Flight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a Fly Speed of 50 feet, but you must end your movement on a surface you can stand on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-flying-wings-purple.webp","_id":"s4eb0d1ed06b1411","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Smite Evil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage dice of your Divine Smite increase to d10s. Additionally, the bonus damage against fiends and undead now applies against all evil-aligned creatures.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/projectiles-blades-salvo-yellow.webp","_id":"s4ee3b7b5a12a9c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Psionic Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>Whenever you gain a sorcerer level, you can replace one spell you gained from this feature with another spell of the same level. The new spell must be a divination or an enchantment spell from the sorcerer, warlock, or wizard spell list.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Psionic Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Arms of Hadar, Dissonant Whispers, Mind Sliver, Calm Emotions, Detect Thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hunger of Hadar, Sending</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Evard's Black Tentacles, Summon Aberration</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Rary's Telepathic Bond, Telekinesis</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4ef5a4123c5c5ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bladesong","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke a secret elven magic called the Bladesong, provided you aren't wearing medium or heavy armor or using a shield. It graces you with supernatural speed, agility, and focus.</p><p>You can use a Bonus Action to start the Bladesong, which lasts for 1 minute. It ends early if you are Incapacitated, if you don medium or heavy armor or a shield, or if you use two hands to make an attack with a weapon. You can also dismiss Bladesong at any time you choose (no action required).</p><p>While your bladesong is active, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You gain a bonus to your AC equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</li><li>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</li><li>You gain a bonus to any Constitution Saving Throws you make to maintain Concentration on a spell. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4efbb5013bfd963","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lore Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Arcana, Deception, History, Insight, Intimidation, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Performance, Persuasion, Religion, Survival.</p><p>Alternatively, you may replace a chosen skill with one of the following tools: Alchemist's Supplies, Cook's Utensils, Enchanter's Supplies, Herbalist's Kit, Poisoner's Kit, or Tinkerer's Tools.</p><p>If you are already proficient in a chosen skill or tool, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p><p>Additionally, you can use Intelligence for skill checks with a chosen skill or tool if it normally uses a different ability score.</p><p>You can choose two additional skills or tools for this feature when you reach 10th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s4f1fa1e4dbaf792","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Quickened Healing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can spend 2 ki points and roll a Martial Arts die. You regain a number of hit points equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.monk.martial-arts","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-explosion-burst-green.webp","_id":"s4fa3587a6a8a11e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have studied the workings of magic and how to channel it through objects. As a result, you have gained the ability to cast spells. To observers, you don't appear to be casting spells in a conventional way; you look as if you're producing wonders using mundane items or outlandish inventions. The information below details how you use those rules with Artificer spells, which appear on the Artificer spell list.</p><p><strong>Tools Required.</strong> You produce your artificer spell effects through your tools. You must have a spellcasting focus—specifically thieves' tools or some kind of artisan's tool—in hand when you cast any spell with this Spellcasting feature (meaning the spell has an 'M' component when you cast it). You must be proficient with the tool to use it in this way.</p><p>After you gain the Infuse Item feature at 2nd level, you can also use any item bearing one of your infusions as a spellcasting focus.</p><div><strong>The Magic of Artifice</strong><p>As an artificer, you use tools when you cast your spells. When describing your spellcasting, think about how you're using a tool to perform the spell effect. If you cast Cure Wounds using alchemist's supplies, you could be quickly producing a salve. If you cast it using tinker's tools, you might have a miniature mechanical spider that binds wounds. When you cast Poison Spray, you could fling foul chemicals or use a wand that spits venom. The effect of the spell is the same as for a spellcaster of any other class, but your method of spellcasting is special.</p><p>The same principle applies when you prepare your spells. As an artificer, you don't study a spellbook or pray to prepare your spells. Instead, you work with your tools and create the specialized items you'll use to produce your effects. If you replace Cure Wounds with Heat Metal, you might be altering the device you use to heal—perhaps modifying a tool so that it channels heat instead of healing energy.</p><p>Such details don't limit you in any way or provide you with any benefit beyond the spell's effects. You don't have to justify how you're using tools to cast a spell. But describing your spellcasting creatively is a fun way to distinguish yourself from other spellcasters.</p></div<p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two cantrips of your choice from the Artificer spell list. At higher levels, you learn additional artificer cantrips of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Artificer table.</p><p>When you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of the artificer cantrips you know with another cantrip from the artificer spell list.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Artificer Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose four level 1 spells from the Artificer spell list.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Artificer levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Artificer Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells from the Artificer spell list until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 5 Artificer, your list of prepared spells can include six spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.</p><p>If another Artificer feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Artificer spells for you.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you finish a Short Rest, you can replace one of your prepared spells with another Artificer spell for which you have spell slots.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can change your list of prepared spells, replacing any of the spells there with other Artificer spells for which you have spell slots.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for your artificer spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use yoru tools as a Spellcasting Focus for your Artificer spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s4fe1eb50197c4c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nature's Sanctuary","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape and cause spectral trees and vines to appear in a 15-foot Cube on the ground within 120 feet of yourself. They last there for 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition or die. You and your allies have Half Cover while in that area, and your allies gain the current Resistance of your Nature's Ward while there.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move the Cube up to 60 feet to ground within 120 feet of yourself.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/encase-creature-humanoid-hold.webp","_id":"s50084c26b37a2b0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Rest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use soothing music or oration to help revitalize your wounded allies during a Short Rest. If you or any friendly creatures who can hear your performance regain hit points by spending Hit Dice at the end of the Short Rest, each of those creatures can roll extra d6s equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and add them to the total of hit points recovered.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s500bae2ecaed3ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a canine aspect, granting you physical traits such as the piercing eyes, sharp nails, and elongated canines.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>Once per turn when you hit a creature that is no more than 1 size larger than you with your natural weapons, you can force the target to make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failure, the target is knocked Prone. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). If the target creature is already Prone, you grapple the creature instead if it fails the save.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, you count as 1 size larger for the purposes of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s50511b7936ad561","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Phoenix Spark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The fiery energy within you grows restless and vengeful. In the face of defeat, it surges outward to preserve you in a fiery roar.</p><p>If you are reduced to 0 hit points, you can instead be reduced to 1 hit point, and each creature within 10 feet of you takes fire damage equal to half your sorcerer level + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>If you use this feature while under the effects of your Mantle of Flame, this feature instead deals fire damage equal to your sorcerer level + double your Charisma modifier, and your Mantle of Flame immediately ends.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s50e68b13b1d48c5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weaver of Weal and Woe","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Bane and Fortune's Favor spells prepared.</p><p>When you cast Bane, its range increases to 60 feet and you can cast Fortune's Favor without providing the material component. You can cast Fortune's Favor in this manner three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5150c93c48e4f72","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You no longer have to end your flying movement on the ground when you are shifted.</p><p>Additionally, you gain blindsight with a range of 20 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s51778c87dc05abd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Courage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you can't be Frightened while you are conscious.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-beam-impact-silhouette.webp","_id":"s526bae9824a329b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Cleaver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bond with the elemental might of giants and their ilk grows, and you learn to infuse weapons with primordial energy.</p><p>When you enter your rage, you can infuse one weapon of your choice that you are holding with one of the following damage types: acid, cold, fire, thunder, or lightning. While you wield the infused weapon during your rage, the weapon's damage type changes to the chosen type, it deals an extra 1d6 damage of the chosen type when it hits, and it gains the thrown property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If you throw the weapon, it reappears in your hand the instant after it hits or misses a target. The infused weapon's benefits are suppressed while a creature other than you wields it.</p><p>While raging and holding the infused weapon, you can use a Bonus Action to change the infused weapon's current damage type to a different one from the above damage types.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5280fa9af4f554c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elegant Riposte","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are currently in your parrying stance and a creature misses you with a melee weapon attack, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon against that creature, provided it is within your reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s52c0e72c4470c37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Spirit Totem safeguards the beasts and fey that you call forth with your magic. When a beast or fey that you summoned or created with a spell ends its turn in your Spirit Totem aura, that creature regains a number of hit points equal to half your druid level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5335a5328d9ae9d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You embody the power of the wilds. Your Strength and Constitution scores increase by 4. Your maximum for those scores is now 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"s53bcdca96c463bc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inquisitor's Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Cunning Action: Aim, you can choose one creature you can see. You have Advantage on the first Attack Roll against that creature each turn for 1 minute instead. This effect ends early if you can no longer see the target, you are Incapacitated, you perform a hostile action against a different creature (such as an attack or forcing it to make a Saving Throw), or you use Inquisitor's Gaze on a different creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s53eb7aa86c3b27c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Leadership Ability Score","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Some of your features reference your Leadership ability score. It represents how you command the respect and loyalty of those around you, as well as how you lead them in battle. Perhaps you are an experienced veteran, survivor of dozens of military conflicts both large and small, a cunning tactician with an academic background in the study of warfare, or a driven idealist with a larger-than-life personality.</p><p>Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. The chosen ability score becomes your Leadership ability score.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/charge.webp","_id":"s5434a4d7262b9ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Devastating Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you score a critical hit with a weapon attack, you gain a bonus to that weapon's damage roll equal to your level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s544329dd7ad9456","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Faithful Steed","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can call on the aid of an otherworldly steed. You always have the Find Steed spell prepared.</p><p>You can also cast the spell once without expending a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"minute","cost":10,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/creatures/horse-white.webp","_id":"s5454377ca9096dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sylvan Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Words of the First World improve in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Sticky Misfortune.</strong> If the reroll does not turn success into failure or vice versa, the curse instead lasts 1 minute or until it changes the outcome of a roll when you activate it the next time.</li><li><strong>Gloaming Cloak.</strong> The creature affected by your Mantle of Midnight becomes Hidden instead of Invisible, ignoring all the usual restrictions for hiding in plain view.</li><li><strong>Sylvan Farstride.</strong> Tread the Unseen Path's teleport distance increases to 60 feet.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5464fc870f193d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Sacrifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take a Short Rest and use your Arcane Recovery class feature, you can spend a number of hit dice up to equal to your Proficiency modifier.</p><p>The number of hit dice spent in this manner is added to the total level of spell slots that you can recover with Arcane Recovery.</p><p>Additionally, when a creature of at least CR 1/8 afflicted with the Lacerated condition from one of your spells dies within 120 feet of you, you regain one hit die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5475bec6a455fe6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (d12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55574d778df51a2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Omen Seer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Minor Prophecy Witchcraft option. If you already know it, you can choose a different Witchcraft option.</p><p>Additionally, you gain two additional uses for Minor Prophecy and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55702484e0d4e26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undead Thralls","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Animate Dead and Summon Undead spells prepared and they do not count against the number of your prepared spells. When you cast Animate Dead, you can target one additional corpse or pile of bones, creating another zombie or skeleton, as appropriate.</p><p>Any undead creature you control has the following additional benefits:</p><ul><li>The creature's hit point maximum is increased by an amount equal to your wizard level.</li><li>The creature adds your Proficiency bonus to its weapon damage rolls.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5584a9e438cb421","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animal Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills: Animal Handling, Nature, Perception, Stealth, Survival.</p><p>Additionally, you add your Formshift Damage to the chosen skills and to your initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/humanoid-wolf-dog-blue.webp","_id":"s55a05b207c78c46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rage of the Gods","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you activate your Rage, you can assume the form of a divine warrior. This form lasts for 1 minute or until you drop to 0 Hit Points. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>While in this form, you gain the benefits below.</p><ul><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant damage.</li><li><strong>Revivification.</strong> When a creature within 30 feet of you would drop to 0 Hit Points, you can take a Reaction to expend a use of your Rage to instead change the target's Hit Points to a number equal to your Barbarian level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55ae6922c55590b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to unleash special magical effects with some of your shots. When you gain this feature, you learn two Arcane Shot options of your choice (see \"Arcane Shot Options\" below).</p><p>Once per turn, when you make a ranged weapon attack as part of the Attack action, you can apply one of your Arcane Shot options to that attack. If the attack misses, the use is not expended.</p><p>You gain an additional Arcane Shot option of your choice when you reach certain levels in this class: 7th, 10th, 15th, and 18th level.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55cd2e0938a8b43","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shielding Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use your mastery of the storm to protect others. Each creature of your choice has the damage Resistance you gained from the Storm Soul feature while the creature is in your Storm Aura.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s55ee51fd6e9dfe0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pyromancy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Pyromancy Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Faerie Fire, Flaming Sphere, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Melf's Minute Meteors, Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Elemental Bane, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Flame Strike, Immolation</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5627bd87d95c7da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Whispers of the Dead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Echoes of those who have died cling to you. Whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can choose one skill or tool Proficiency that you lack and gain it, as a ghostly presence shares its knowledge with you. You lose this Proficiency when you use this feature to choose a different Proficiency that you lack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5676201d8198f3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Reanimated Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion attacks twice instead of once when you command it to take the Attack action. In addition, you can give it two out of the following benefits. You can change your choice each time you complete a Short or Long Rest.</p><ul><li>Your companion gains Proficiency in Strength or Dexterity Saving Throws (your choice).</li><li>Your companion's Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>Your companion's current and maximum hit points increase by an amount equal to your Artificer level.</li><li>You can cast spells is if you were in your companion's space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s56da437e1206696","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You radiate a soothing, unseeable aura in a 30-foot Emanation that originates from you. The aura is inactive while you have the Incapacitated condition.</p><p>All allied creatures in the aura are Immune to the Frightened condition. If a Frightened ally enters the aura, that condition has no effect on that ally while there.</p><p>Any hostile creature in the aura that targets you or your allies with an attack or other harmful effect takes psychic damage equal to half your cleric level (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s573a1e2298b5b86","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monster Slayer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Monster Slayer Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Monster Slayer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Protection from Evil and Good</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Magic Circle</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Hold Monster</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57790f25906ae2e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avenging Angel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become an avatar of vengeance. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You sprout spectral wings on your back, have a Fly Speed of 60 feet, and can hover.</li><li>If an enemy creature within your Aura of Protection damages you or your allies, it is automatically affected by your Vow of Enmity (no action required). This does not consume a use of your Channel Divinity.</li><li>If an enemy creature starts its turn in your Aura of Protection or enters it for the first time on a turn, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or become Frightened for 1 minute. If the creature is under the effect of your Vow of Enmity, it has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57829a2849ed54e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Split Enchantment","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast an enchantment spell of 1st level or higher that targets only one creature, you can have it target a second creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57b02084573ce61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sea Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once on your turn, you can move up to your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks and teleport your water orb to your position. You can do so before, during, or after this movement.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you can regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s57d60ef17976021","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Timeless Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ki sustains you so that you suffer none of the frailty of old age, and you can't be aged magically. You can still die of old age, however. In addition, you no longer need food or water.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/clock-stopwatch-white-blue.webp","_id":"s582a5359def94d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scourge of the Ancients","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to fully harness the titanic legacy of your companion. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a spell slot of any level to heighten your primeval companion's might, granting it one of the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Hulking Behemoth.</strong> The companion grows one size larger and gains temporary hit points equal to 10 times the level of the spell slot expended. If there isn't enough room for the companion to grow, it attains the maximum possible size in the space available.</li><li><strong>Mauler.</strong> On a hit, the companion's Strike deals additional damage equal to 1d8 plus the level of the spell slot expended.</li><li><strong>Titanic Stride.</strong> The companion's Speed increases by a number of feet equal to 5 times the level of the spell slot expended.</li></ul><p>For the duration, your primeval companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>These benefits last for 1 hour, until the companion vanishes, or until you expend a spell slot for this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5878a63ab452e7c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Smite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one spell slot to deal radiant damage to the target, in addition to the weapon's damage. The extra damage is 2d8 for a 1st-level spell slot, plus 1d8 for each spell level higher than 1st, to a maximum of 6d8. The damage increases by 1d8 if the target is an undead or a fiend, to a maximum of 7d8.</p><p>You can use this feature without expending a spell slot a number of times equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down) and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"floor(@attributes.prof/2)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow-teal.webp","_id":"s589d176e445c6f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the Help action as a Bonus Action. Additionally, when you use the Help action to aid an ally in attacking a creature, the target of that attack can be within 60 feet of you, rather than within 5 feet of you, if the target can see or hear you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s58acb7df5bc9c18","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Veil","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can weave a veil of psychic static to mask yourself. As an Action, you can magically become Invisible, along with anything you are wearing or carrying, for 1 hour or until you dismiss this effect (no action required). This invisibility ends early immediately after you deal damage to a creature or you force a creature to make a Saving Throw.</p><p>If you expend a Psionic Energy Die, you can also affect all creatures of your choice while they are within 20 feet of you. The effect ends early on all affected creatures when any of them deal damage to a creature or force it to make a Saving Throw.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5933560bc979c52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mirror, Mirror","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell of up to 5th level that can only target yourself, you can choose your bonded familiar as a second target if it is within 60 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s594ccb50ac27e38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Striding Giant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of earth allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of the mountain.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>Your size changes the huge and you gain temporary hit points equal to three times your kineticist level.</li><li>You are Immune to the Charmed, Exhausted, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, and Poisoned conditions.</li><li>You ignore all earth-based effects such as the Erupting Earth spell or even a natural earthquake.</li><li>When you move for the first time on your turn, your steps shake the earth. All creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you have to make a Strength Saving Throw against your save DC or be knocked Prone.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s59a8a41a24c8452","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Cunning Action class feature, you can also choose to teleport 30 ft to an unoccupied space that you can see. You can choose to do so immediately after or before applying the effect of Cunning Action. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s59c234b370e824c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alchemical Savant","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell while you have alchemist's supplies on your person, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/mortar-powder-green.webp","_id":"s59da939b544065f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Bane","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have survived the Hunter's Bane—a dangerous, long-guarded ritual that alters your life's blood, forever binding you to the darkness and honing your senses against it. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. The chosen ability score is your Hemocraft ability score, which represents how you make use of your dark gift. You can use this ability score in place of the usual one when you make Arcana, Religion, or Survival checks.</p><p>The Hunter's Bane also empowers your body to control and shape hemocraft magic, using your own blood and life essence to fuel your abilities. Some of your features require your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the feature's effects. The Saving Throw DC is calculated as follows:</p><p><b>Hemocraft save DC</b> = 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Hemocraft modifier (your choice between Intelligence or Wisdom)</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hand-claw-glow-orange.webp","_id":"s59e46b8c9231cca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Health","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The divine magic flowing through you makes you Immune to disease.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/cross-worn-green.webp","_id":"s5a5b76c4d9e1b18","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tempered Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to sword magic gives you extra fortitude. Your hit point maximum increases by 1, and it increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>As an Action, you can gain a base AC of 10 + your Constitution modifier + your Charisma modifier if you aren't wearing armor. This effect lasts until you end it as a Bonus Action or you don armor other than a shield.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5a9942f503d5554","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your animal-like swiftness or thick skin makes it more difficult to land a hit on you.</p><p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice when you get this feature) and your Constitution modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-green.webp","_id":"s5ae0b016e990fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiotic Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are in Symbiosis, you can gain a bonus to your AC and Saving Throws equal to half your Proficiency (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5b0dc25b861b6dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are hit by an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to halve the attack's damage against yourself (round down) and force the attacker to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker takes damage equal to 4d10 plus your Charisma modifier; the damage type is that associated with your genie patron as per your Aura of Elemental Shielding. On a successful save, the attacker takes half as much damage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5b3c04ad4d7c805","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Patient Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Disengage action as a Bonus Action. Alternatively, you can expend 1 Ki Point to take both the Disengage and the Dodge actions as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-glowing-blue.webp","_id":"s5cabc37e591bc42","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Erudite","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your continued studies broaden your areas of expertise. Choose another skill as per your Scholar feature. Alternatively, you can choose to learn a new language.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-purple-glyph.webp","_id":"s5cbaa3817ee1417","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Beauty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become an avatar of unearthly beauty. Your enemies attack with uncertainty, fearful of damaging the wondrous being they behold, while your magic draws upon your presence to augment its power.</p><p>As a Reaction, you can impose a penalty on a creature's attacks against you or on its Saving Throws against your spells and abilities. This benefit lasts until the end of the current turn The penalty equals your Charisma modifier (minimum 1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5cfa15cf41ab116","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Radiant Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your link to the Celestial allows you to serve as a conduit for radiant energy. You have Resistance to radiant damage, and when you cast a spell that deals radiant or fire damage, you can add your Charisma modifier to one radiant or fire damage roll of that spell against one of its targets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d1099e90576f14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rite Revival","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to protect your fading life by reabsorbing the energy you feed to your weapons. If you have one or more crimson rites active and you are reduced to 0 hit points but don't die outright, you can choose to have all your active crimson rites end and immediately regain hit points equal to twice your blood hunter level. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5d586a3a7f7e5a8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serpent's Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Blindsight range increases by 10 feet. No attack from within your Blindsight range has Advantage against you as long as you are not Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5df19d53b568585","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fool's Insight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to gather stories and lore gains a supernatural edge. You can cast detect thoughts up to a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier. You regain any expended uses of this ability after completing a Long Rest.</p><p>If a creature resists your attempt to probe deeper and succeeds at its Saving Throw against your detect thoughts, it immediately suffers an embarrassing social gaffe. It might loudly pass gas, unleash a thunderous burp, trip and fall, or be compelled to tell a tasteless joke.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e52a14d7b87ce1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gather Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your expended elemental energy through focused meditation.</p><p>Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose to regain a number of kinesis points equal to half your kineticist level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you finish a short rest"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"1","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/movement/portal-vortex-orange.webp","_id":"s5e66fb4e04312dc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expert Divination","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Casting divination spells comes so easily to you that it expends only a fraction of your spellcasting efforts. When you cast a divination spell of 2nd level or higher using a spell slot, you regain spell slots with a combined level one lower than the spell cast. The slot you regain can't be higher than 5th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5e80dd760c48a26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insightful Striking","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. Your magic grants you a brief vision of the target's defenses. Until the end of your next turn, you gain one of the following effects of your choice:</p><ul><li>The next time you make an Attack Roll against the target, roll a d6 and add the number rolled to the total.</li><li>The next time the target must make a Saving Throw against a spell you cast, the target must roll a d6 and subtract the number rolled from the Saving Throw.</li></ul><p>You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5f0e3a99289e34a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Druid Circle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose to identify with a circle of druids from the list of available circles. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s5f3846f48285260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Writhing Tide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can condense part of your swarm into a focused mass that lifts you up. As a Bonus Action, you gain a Fly Speed of 10 feet and can hover. This effect lasts for 1 minute or until you are Incapacitated.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5f9575b8d20c89b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unflinching Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all Saving Throws caused by the target of your Inquisitor's Gaze.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s5fe10298682bc8a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are not wearing any armor, your Armor Class equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Constitution modifier. You can use a shield and still gain this benefit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"s604c4d58654b312","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unleash Incarnation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can heighten your echo's fury. Whenever you take the Attack action, you can make one additional melee attack from the echo's position.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60a66c3d233d70e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ferocious Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Formshift Damage to your weapon damage rolls even when not currently shifted. If you are shifted, this damage bonus is doubled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/tail-strike-bone-orange.webp","_id":"s60abd2d7ccf4829","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Signature Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered certain techniques to the point that they have become second nature. Choose two maneuvers that you know. When you use one of these two maneuvers, you can roll a d8 and use it instead of expending a Combat Superiority Die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60c2e4be2f4e77d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Echo Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can temporarily transfer your consciousness to your echo. As an Action, you can see through your echo's eyes and hear through its ears. You can sustain this effect for up to 10 minutes, and you can end it at any time (requires no action). While your echo is being used in this way, it can be up to 1,000 feet away from you without being destroyed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60d1fc5dd7f4b4a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Wings","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to manifest a pair of spectral wings from your back. While the wings are present, you have a Fly Speed of 30 feet. The wings last until you're Incapacitated, you die, or you dismiss them as a Bonus Action.</p><p>The affinity you chose for your Divine Magic feature determines the appearance of the spectral wings: eagle wings for good or law, bat wings for evil or chaos, and dragonfly wings for neutrality.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s60fef5469967f9a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Battle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to the Frightened condition and you gain Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s61b7c8d5acd9f73","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Searing Sunburst","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to create an orb of light that erupts into a devastating explosion. As an Action, you magically create an orb and hurl it at a point you choose within 150 feet, where it erupts into a sphere of radiant light for a brief but deadly instant.</p><p>Each creature in that 20-foot-radius sphere must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take 2d6 radiant damage. A creature doesn't need to make the save if the creature is behind total cover that is opaque.</p><p>You can increase the sphere's damage by spending ki points. Each point you spend, to a maximum of 3, increases the damage by 2d6.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s61b8262b51a6d91","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telepathic Speech","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can form a telepathic connection between your mind and the mind of another. As a Bonus Action, choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. You and the chosen creature can speak telepathically with each other while the two of you are within a number of miles of each other equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). To understand each other, you must both know at least one language.</p><p>The telepathic connection lasts for a number of minutes equal to your sorcerer level. It ends early if you are Incapacitated or die or if you use this ability to form a connection with a different creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s623f1b18103e686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dreadful Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The size of your Dreadful Presence increases to 30 feet. Creatures that fail their Saving Throw against your Unnerving Aura are also Frightened for the duration. When a creature Frightened in this manner is subject to the effect of A Feast for Crows, it deals maximum damage and ignores Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s627c41288aaad77","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visions of the Future","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your knowledge of the future allows you to guide an individual to achieve their greatest possible success. You can cast the Foresight spell once without expending a spell slot. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6287ee31cc84333","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your magical energy by drawning from the essence of the planes. Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your summoner level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 3rd level or higher.</p><p>For example, if you're a 4th-level summoner, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots.</p><p>You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62b945405560121","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Psionics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal psychic or force damage with a wizard spell, you can add your Intelligence modifier to the damage against one of the spell's targets.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62da635f718fba4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Walk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you are in dim light or darkness, as a Bonus Action, you can magically teleport up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s62f22e5da3fe041","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Animal Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You cannot be Surprised unless you are Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/humanoid-wolf-dog-blue.webp","_id":"s62f412ae934d571","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanguine Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Hit Dice to regain hit points, you roll two D12s for each Hit Die and add them together. Any healing you regain through Hit Dice cannot be reduced in any way.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you score a critical hit with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you regain one expended use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-evil-horned-giant.webp","_id":"s63b4d9e5d602574","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nightwalker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to adopt a shadowy form as a Bonus Action for 10 minutes. While in this form, Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you, you gain the Spiderclimb trait, and you double your Speed if you start your turn in an area of dim light or darkness.</p><p>You can use this feature once and must finish a Long Rest before you can use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6422f63fcbf97ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast one of the level 1+ spells that you have prepared from your Circle Spells feature without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a Long Rest before you do so again.</p><p>In addition, when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your Druid level (round up), and none of them can be level 6+. For example, if you're a level 6 Druid, you can recover up to three levels' worth of spell slots. You can recover a level 3 spell slot, a level 2 and a level 1 spell slot, or three level 1 spell slots. Once you recover spell slots with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"s644c14a09adfc1c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Two Minds, One Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma Saving Throws while you are in Symbiosis.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s644dc7f9a8bd619","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"A Feast for Crows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when a creature fails its Saving Throw against your Unnerving Aura or when you damage a creature within its area of effect, you deal 1d10 + your Wisdom modifier necrotic damage to it and regain hit points equal to the damage dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s64771f3a5b2e7fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wind Walker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the wind allows you to move freely through the air. You gain a Fly Speed equal to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s64c8e38997b0ca0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infectious Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you successfully inspire someone, the power of your eloquence can now spread to someone else. When a creature within 60 feet of you adds one of your Bardic Inspiration dice to its Ability Check, Attack Roll, or Saving Throw and the roll succeeds, you can use your Reaction to encourage a different creature (other than yourself) that can hear you within 60 feet of you, giving it a Bardic Inspiration die without expending any of your Bardic Inspiration uses.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). You regain one use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s64ff5afa4067f52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hybrid Transformation Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered your inner predator. You can use your Hybrid Transformation feature an unlimited number of times, and your hybrid form lasts until you revert to your normal form, fall Unconscious, or die.</p><p>You also gain the Blood Curse of the Howl for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s65602915fe6ab74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reclaim Potential","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned to absorb the fleeting magic of your echo. When an echo of yours is destroyed by taking damage, you can gain a number of temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Constitution modifier.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s65bcc8213a2fb1b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of the Sentinel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emit an aura of alertness while you aren't Incapacitated. When you and any creatures of your choice within 10 feet of you roll initiative, you all gain a bonus to initiative equal to your Proficiency bonus.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s65e16be09dd1e37","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are shifted, any hostile creature that starts its turn within 60 feet of you or enters that area for the first time on a turn, must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier) or be Frightened or Charmed by you (your choice) until the end of your next turn. Any affected creature also has Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your breath weapon.</p><p>Once a creature succeeds on this save, it is Immune against this feature for the next 24 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s65f6d9648434c38","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 2 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s66a62c21954e86b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Ascendance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action you transform into an apparition of pure magic for 1 minute, gaining the following benefits. The transformation ends early if you die, you are Incapacitated, or if you end it as a Bonus Action. Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest unless you spend 7 Sorcery Points (no action required) to restore your use of it.</p><ul><li><strong>Arcane Wellspring.</strong> During your turn, you can trade any number of your Hit Dice for the same number of Sorcery Points (no Action required).</li><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You gain a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover.</li><li><strong>Spell Avoidance.</strong> When you're subjected to a spell or magical effect that allows you to make a Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s675aceeb358de89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monastic Tradition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You commit yourself to a monastic tradition, chosen from the list of available traditions. Your tradition grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 11th, and 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/tree-roots-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s6780d225c0d26e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rakish Audacity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your confidence propels you into battle. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Charisma modifier.</p><p>You also gain an additional way to use your Sneak Attack; you don't need Advantage on your Attack Roll to use Sneak Attack against a creature if it is within your melee reach, no other creatures are within 5 feet of you, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s67ae7aaaa072128","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Coven Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Based on your chosen season, you always have the following spells prepared. You can cast each of those spells without expending a spell slot. And you cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Heal, Regenerate.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> Sunbeam, Firestorm.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Chain Lightning, Circle of Death.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> Wall of Ice, Icy Prison.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s67e078c4a24e6f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rat Father's Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can now target other creatures beside your bonded familiar for the purposes of your Mirror, Mirror feature.</p><p>You and any other creature that are currently Invisible through a spell or feature of yours have their speed doubled and can Hide as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s680c9835e570f74","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Sister's Scorn","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 60 feet hits you or your bonded familiar with an attack or forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to curse that creature. The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it is subject to one of the effects of the Bestow Curse spell until the start of its next turn.</p><p>If the target is already under the effect of Bestow Curse, it stacks with this feature as long as you choose a different curse effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6821982c23e41cc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cauterizing Flames","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to turn death into magical flames that can heal or incinerate. When a Small or larger creature dies within 30 feet of you or your wildfire spirit, a harmless spectral flame springs forth in the dead creature's space and flickers there for 1 minute. When a creature you can see enters that space, you can use your Reaction to extinguish the spectral flame there and either heal the creature or deal fire damage to it. The healing or damage equals 2d10 + your Druid level.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68800383c85f600","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 6)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68b2bc75f7af7c3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warcry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When your allies are affected by your Inspiring Surge, you can choose to apply one of the following additional effects per ally:</p><ul><li>The target has Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage until the start of your next turn.</li><li>The target's Speed is doubled until the start of your next turn.</li><li>The target has Advantage on melee weapon Attack Rolls until the start of your next turn, but Attack Rolls against it also have Advantage for the duration.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s68b326d116ec496","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Winter Wanderer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Ranger level specified in the Winter Wanderer Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Winter Wanderer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rime's Binding Ice</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fortify</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Ice Storm</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cone of Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s694759913df72a2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s696381d82ff3075","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Elemental Discipline (Level 11)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn one additional elemental discipline of your choice. You should know 3 elemental disciplines, as well as Elemental Attunement.</p><p>Whenever you learn a new elemental discipline, you can also replace one elemental discipline that you already know with a different discipline.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s69a326c1c157971","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The storm grants you benefits even when your aura isn't active. The benefits are based on the environment you chose for your Storm Aura.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6a5c6d996772292","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bonded familiar can now also use the special actions gained through your Witchcraft. This does not change the number of uses a given feature has or how many times it can affect the same creature.</p><p>Additionally, your bonded familiar now also adds your Proficiency to its AC.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6af1f1ecc488df4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knightly Valor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You cannot be Frightened or Charmed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6afb92f400afd62","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lethality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The critical range for your weapon attacks increases by 1.</p><p>Additionally, you can apply the extra damage from your Assassinate class feature even after the first turn of combat, provided that you are hidden from the target or it is suffering from a condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b1a710f3dc3389","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutal Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you use Reckless Attack, you can forgo any Advantage on one Strength-based Attack Roll of your choice on your turn. The chosen Attack Roll mustn't have Disadvantage. If the chosen Attack Roll hits, the target takes an extra 1d10 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon or Unarmed Strike, and you can cause one Brutal Strike effect of your choice. You have the following effect options.</p><ul><li><strong>Forceful Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a STR Saving Throw or be pushed 15 feet straight away from you. You can then move up to half your Speed straight toward the target without provoking Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Hamstring Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a DEX Saving Throw or have its Speed reduced by 15 feet until the start of your next turn. A target can be affected by only one Hamstring Blow at a time—the most recent one.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"s6b5f040fe2e845b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Shape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of nature allows you to assume the form of an animal. As a Bonus Action, you shape-shift into a Beast form that you have learned for this feature (see \"Known Forms\" below). You stay in that form for a number of hours equal to half your Druid level or until you use Wild Shape again, have the Incapacitated condition, or die. You can also leave the form early as a Bonus Action.</p><ul><li><strong>Number of Uses.</strong> You can use Wild Shape twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li><li>You gain additional uses when you reach certain Druid levels, as shown in the Wild Shape column of the Druid Features table.</li><li><strong>Known Forms.</strong> You know four Beast forms for this feature, chosen from among Beast stat blocks that have a maximum Challenge Rating of 1/4 and that lack a Fly Speed (see appendix B for stat block options). The Rat, Riding Horse, Spider, and Wolf are recommended. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can replace one of your known forms with another eligible form.</li><li>When you reach certain Druid levels, your number of known forms and the maximum Challenge Rating for those forms increases, as shown in the Beast Shapes table. In addition, starting at level 8, you can adopt a form that has a Fly Speed.</li><li>When choosing known forms, you may look in the Monster Manual or elsewhere for eligible Beasts if the Dungeon Master permits you to do so.</li><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Beast Shapes</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Druid Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Known Forms</th><th scope=\"col\">Max. CR</th><th scope=\"col\">Fly Speed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>1/4</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>6</td><td>1/2</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>8</td><td>1</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><li><strong>Rules While Transformed.</strong> While in a form, you retain your personality, memories, and ability to speak, and the following rules apply:</li><ul><li><strong>Temporary Hit Points.</strong> When you assume a Wild Shape form, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to your Druid level.</li><li><strong>Game Statistics.</strong> Your game statistics are replaced by the Beast's stat block, but you retain your creature type; Hit Points; Hit Point Dice; Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; class features; languages; and feats. You also retain your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies and use your Proficiency Bonus for them, in addition to gaining the proficiencies of the creature. If a skill or Saving Throw modifier in the Beast's stat block is higher than yours, use the one in the stat block.</li><li>If you attack in this form, you can use your spell attack bonus instead of the form's attack bonus if it is higher. If the form has a special ability that requires a Saving Throw, you can use your spell save DC in place of the form's DC.</li><li><strong>No Spellcasting.</strong> You can't cast spells, but shape-shifting doesn't break your Concentration or otherwise interfere with a spell you've already cast.</li><li><strong>Objects.</strong> Your ability to handle objects is determined by the form's limbs rather than your own. In addition, you choose whether your equipment falls in your space, merges into your new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it's practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment based on the creature's size and shape. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with the form. Equipment that merges with the form has no effect while you're in that form.</li></ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.druid.wildshape","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/elk-moose-marked-green.webp","_id":"s6b8077cd5422a0f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dampen Elements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature within 30 feet of you takes acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, you can use your Reaction to grant Resistance to the creature against that instance of the damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6b9ecbd4bd0fe39","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose a second option from the Fighting Style class feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-purple.webp","_id":"s6c64c7d66e52e18","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"High Elf Education","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Arcana skill and one more INT-based skill of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-purple-glyph.webp","_id":"s6cdd029a12fb315","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Full of Stars","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While in your Starry Form, you become partially incorporeal, giving you Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d13f9cef35ef03","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Warded Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar have Immunity to the Confused condition and Resistance to psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d5c2e067897840","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Knowledge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in another skill of your choice from the skill list available to Barbarians at level 1.</p><p>In addition, while your Rage is active, you can channel primal power when you attempt certain tasks; whenever you make an Ability Check using one of the following skills, you can make it as a Strength check even if it normally uses a different ability: Acrobatics, Intimidation, Perception, Stealth, or Survival. When you use this ability, your Strength represents primal power coursing through you, honing your agility, bearing, and senses.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/bull-head-horns-glowing.webp","_id":"s6d8f7dd72c06b19","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blazing Revival","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond with your wildfire spirit can save you from death. If the spirit is within 120 feet of you when you are reduced to 0 hit points and thereby fall Unconscious, you can cause the spirit to drop to 0 hit points. You then regain half your hit points and immediately rise to your feet.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6d9164b153fd84d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Insidious Whispers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any spell you cast ignores Immunity to and Advantage on Saving Throws against the Charmed condition unless the target also has Immunity to or Advantage on Saving Throws against the Frightened condition, respectively.</p><p>Additionally, any creature Charmed by a spell cast by you suppresses all memories of the duration. This effect is suspended if the target becomes Immune to the Frightened condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6daf695978b2bad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Affinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to the damage type associated with your draconic ancestry. Additionally, as an Action, you can spend 2 sorcery points to give yourself Immunity to that damage type for 1 hour.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/projectile-icecicles-salvo.webp","_id":"s6ddee5f255064e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ritual Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast any spell as a Ritual if that spell has the Ritual tag and the spell is in your spellbook. You needn't have the spell prepared, but you must read from the book to cast a spell in this way.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/star-yellow.webp","_id":"s6e473ffc9846072","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Favored Enemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You become more adept at fighting your favored foes. Choose a second creature type as favored enemy. Your damage bonus against all your favored enemies increases to +4. Additionally, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against the spells and abilities used by a favored enemy.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp","_id":"s6f3d969b366fe10","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Astral Refuge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step into an astral refuge. As an Action, you disappear from the world for a brief moment and enter the Astral Plane, taking Advantage of its timeless nature. While in your astral refuge, you can take two actions to cast spells that target only you. After using those two actions, you return to the space you occupied and your turn ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6fb88e0692712b2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Storm Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your control of the air streams around you to help you dodge or otherwise ward off certain area effects, like the explosion of a fireball or a dragon's breath.</p><p>When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half damage if you fail.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s6fc5e4cae4da67a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Elemental Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All features of your Elemental Might with an area of effect have their radius increased to 20 feet. Additionally, its element-specific benefits improve in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Air.</strong> Your movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks and you can move through the spaces of other creatures unimpeded.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> Every creature that fails its Saving Throw against your Elemental Might is knocked Prone.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> The critical range of your attacks increases by 1. Your critical hits deal an additional 2d8 fire damage.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> Every creature that fails its Saving Throw against your Elemental Might has its Speed halved until the start your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s706e4af48ab97a8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"True Hide in Plain Sight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You may choose to take the Hide action and may stay hidden even when the conditions normally wouldn't allow you to, such as when you are in direct line of sight of a creature or you are standing in bright light. If you do so, you take a -5 penalty to your Dexterity (Stealth) check to hide. Depending on the circumstances, the DM may impose this penalty multiple times.</p><p>This feature does not allow you to bypass the conditions for hiding against creatures that perceive you with senses other than mundane sight or are able to perceive the true form of a shapechanger.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s70e72a505a2c23c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Join Fates","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through a ritual that lasts 10 minutes, you can touch two other creatures and temporarily tie their fates together. Whenever either creature makes an Ability Check or Saving Throw, the other also rolls and the original creature uses the average of the two rolls to determine the effect (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s71328eb10e00e0e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Physician's Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can administer even greater cures with a touch, and if you feel it's necessary, you can use your knowledge to cause harm.</p><p>When you use Hand of Healing, you can also end one of the following conditions on the creature you heal or remove one disease affecting them: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, or Stunned.</p><p>When you use Hand of Harm on a creature, you can also force that creature to make a Constitution Saving Throw or have the Poisoned condition until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s716b6ecb34a4260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement (Level 13)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature four times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"s723db0e3f058861","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Summoner's Guardian","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your improved connection with your Eidolon allows it to defend you more effectively. You can use your Bonus Action to command your Eidolon to take a guarding stance while it is within 5 feet of you.</p><p>The stance lasts until the start of your next turn. It ends early if your Eidolon is no longer within 5 feet of you or it is Incapacitated.</p><p>While the stance is active, all Attack Rolls that target you have Disadvantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-golem-stone-blue.webp","_id":"s7247809f3c9b162","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Blessing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose two ability scores from Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution. The chosen ability scores and their maximums increase by 2.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"s726dd8063020011","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Manifest Echo","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to magically manifest an echo of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 15 feet of you. This echo is a magical, translucent, gray image of you that lasts until it is destroyed, until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action, until you manifest another echo, or until you're Incapacitated.</p><p>Your echo's AC is equal to yours, has 1 hit point, and Immunity to all conditions. If it has to make a Saving Throw, it uses your Saving Throw bonus for the roll. It is the same size as you, and it occupies its space. On your turn, you can mentally command the echo to move up to 30 feet in any direction (no action required). If your echo is ever more than 30 feet from you at the end of your turn, it is destroyed.</p><p>You can use the echo in the following ways:</p><ul><li>As a Bonus Action, you can teleport, magically swapping places with your echo at a cost of 15 feet of your movement, regardless of the distance between the two of you.</li><li>When you take the Attack action on your turn, any attack you make with that action can originate from your space or the echo's space. You make this choice for each attack.</li><li>When a creature that you can see within 5 feet of your echo moves at least 5 feet away from it, you can use your Reaction to make an Opportunity Attack against that creature as if you were in the echo's space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s726ffef1019336d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Dark Sisters Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Dark Sisters Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Bane, Dissonant Whispers, Arcane Rend, Blindness/Deafness</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dark Orb, Hunger of Hadar</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Doomtide, Greater Malison</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dominate Person, Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s72a29b353ce5dfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn. If you already have this feature from another class, you may choose a Feat instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"s731444e5bfddb3c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Touch of the Long Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your touch can channel the energy of death into a creature. As an Action, you touch one creature within 5 feet of you, and you expend 1 to 10 ki points. The target must make a Constitution Saving Throw, and it takes 2d10 necrotic damage per ki point spent on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that failed this Saving Throw has to repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turn. On a failure, it takes necrotic damage equal to your monk level. Until it succeeds, the creature cannot benefit from healing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7331be108dd96a5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a mind for tactics on and off the battlefield. When you fail an Ability Check, you can expend a use of your Second Wind to push yourself toward success. Rather than regaining Hit Points, you roll 1d10 and add the number rolled to the Ability Check, potentially turning it into a success. If the check still fails, this use of Second Wind isn't expended.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d10","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-spiral.webp","_id":"s733f9dfa90405f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Infusion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Intelligence or Charisma modifier (your choice) to your Eidolon's damage rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/tail-strike-bone-orange.webp","_id":"s7355dde054b5fe5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflecting Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Arcane Deflection, you can spend a spell slot to increase the amount of damage it reduces by 5 x the level of the expended spell slot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s735cd6cbe02f795","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Celestial Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain temporary hit points whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest. These temporary hit points equal your warlock level + your Charisma modifier. Additionally, choose up to five creatures you can see at the end of the rest. Those creatures each gain temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s735ee68d6cf0d06","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ever-Ready Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a use of Arcane Shot.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s738dcc6d79e9f11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt an avian aspect, granting you physical traits such as the piercing eyes of a bird of prey, sharp nails, and wings sprouting from your back.</p><p>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. If you are not shifted, you have to end your flying movement on the ground.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, you no longer need to end your flying movement on the ground while not shifted.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s739881335b6fac8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raging Storm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of the storm you channel grows mightier, lashing out at your foes. The radius of your aura grows to 20 ft and your aura gains an additional effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s73af228f22ef592","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Leading Evasion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and you take only half damage if you fail. If any creatures within 5 feet of you are making the same Dexterity Saving Throw, you can share this benefit with them for that save.</p><p>You can't use this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s73b9a50b5ce4a7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beguiling Twist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of the Feywild guards your mind. You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed or Frightened.</p><p>In addition, whenever you or a creature you can see within 120 feet of you succeeds on a Saving Throw against being Charmed or Frightened, you can use your Reaction to force a different creature you can see within 120 feet of you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC. If the save fails, the target is Charmed or Frightened by you (your choice) for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a successful save.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s73dbae490b082e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inevitable Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Sanctified Mark, you can declare a creature known to you as the target, ignoring all range, sight, and cover restrictions. If the target is on another plane of existence, you learn which one.</p><p>Additionally, you cannot have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against the the target of Sanctified Mark.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s740c3d93c9596ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rend Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can sweep your Psychic Blades directly through a creature's mind. When you use your Psychic Blades to deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature, you can force that target to make an Intelligence Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). If the save fails, the target is Stunned for 1 minute. The Stunned target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend three Psionic Energy dice to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s744e3639b0b8468","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Harness Divine Power","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you touch your holy symbol, utter a prayer, and regain one expended spell slot, the level of which can be no higher than half your Proficiency bonus (rounded up). The number of times you can use this feature is based on the level you've reached in this class: 2nd level, once; 6th level, twice; and 18th level, thrice. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/prayer-hands-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"s74cff080ed57e77","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Telekinetic Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered new ways to use your telekinetic abilities, detailed below.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s74ef0971e4ef1bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Mushroom Circles Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Mushroom Circles Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Faerie Fire, Sleep, Fortune's Favor, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Hypnotic Pattern, Summon Fey</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Charm Monster, Confusion</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mislead, Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75551fc4c2dd638","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Illusory Reality","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned the secret of weaving shadow magic into your illusions to give them a semireality. When you cast an illusion spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose one inanimate, nonmagical object that is part of the illusion and make that object real. You can do this on your turn as a Bonus Action while the spell is ongoing. The object remains real for 1 minute. For example, you can create an illusion of a bridge over a chasm and then make it real long enough for your allies to cross.</p><p>The object can't deal damage or otherwise directly harm anyone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s757d62e68a70684","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hurricane Queen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of air allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of storms.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You ignore all wind-based effects such as the Whirlwind spell or even a natural tornado.</li><li>You gain Immunity to lightning damage.</li><li>You are surrounded by a 60 foot radius aura of stormlike winds of such intensity that they render ranged weapon attacks against you completely impossible. You and any number of creatures of your choice in the area are unaffected.</li><li>Any other creature is Deafened while in this area, must spend 4 feet for every 1 foot of movement while in it, and has to succeed on a Strength Saving Throw against your save DC at the start of its turn or when it enters the area for the first time or be knocked Prone or hurled 20 feet away in a direction that you choose.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75b39b279cd9eca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Phenomenon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your lunar phase magic bursts. As a Bonus Action, you can tap into a special power of the lunar phase you are currently in. Alternatively, as part of the Bonus Action you take to change your lunar phase using your Waxing and Waning feature, you can immediately use the power of the lunar phase you are entering:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon:</strong> You radiate intense moonlight for a moment. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC or be Blinded until the end of its next turn. In addition, one creature of your choice in that area regains 3d8 hit points.</li><li><strong>New Moon:</strong> You momentarily emanate an oppressive gloom. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC or take 3d10 psychic damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. In addition, you become Invisible until the end of your next turn, or until you make an attack or cast a spell.</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon:</strong> You slip through light and darkness. You can magically teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 60 feet of yourself. In addition, you also gain Resistance to all damage until the start of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Once you use a phase's Bonus Action, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75bd981828326f5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Demiurgic Colossus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The primordial power of your rage intensifies. When you rage, your reach now increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Huge, and you can now use your Mighty Impel to move creatures that are Large or smaller.</p><p>In addition, the extra damage dealt by your Elemental Cleaver feature increases to 2d6.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75cd57704d11a79","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Limitless Metamagic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Metamagic, you can combine any of the options you know for the same spell, paying the sorcery point cost for each.</p><p>Additionally, when an ally you can see within 120 feet casts a spell, you can use your Reaction to use your Metamagic on their spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s75dc8b9e06597d4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scout's Swiftness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can roll a Combat Superiority Die without expending it and add it to your initiative.</p><p>Additionally, when initiative is rolled but before the first round of combat, you can expend a Combat Superiority Die to move up to your Speed and make a single weapon attack. If it hits, you add your Combat Superiority Die to the damage roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s76353bd0e7ae664","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Darkness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain strength from darkness. As a Bonus Action, you fade into the shadows. You regain hit points equal to your cleric level and gain Resistance to all damage for one minute. In addition, while this duration lasts you can use a Bonus Action to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is in dim light or darkness. It ends early if you become Incapacitated or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you use this feature you cannot use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s768b44453862906","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Swarm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Gathered Swarm grows mightier in the following ways:</p><ul><li>The damage of Gathered Swarm increases to 2d6.</li><li>If a creature fails its Saving Throw against being moved by Gathered Swarm, you can also cause the swarm to knock the creature Prone.</li><li>When you are moved by Gathered Swarm, it gives you half cover until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s76e90cc9f3a12b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Savage Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you score a critical hit with a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice (and only the weapon's own damage dice) again and add the result to the total.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-purple.webp","_id":"s779dc5e43a82edb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (6th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 6th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p><p>At higher levels, you gain more warlock spells of your choice that can be cast in this way: one 7th-level spell at 13th level, one 8th-level spell at 15th level, and one 9th-level spell at 17th level. You regain all uses of your Mystic Arcanum when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-black-grey.webp","_id":"s77b307447d2e113","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Consuming Flames","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your flames grow extraordinarily intense. You ignore Resistance to fire damage and treat Immunity to fire damage as Resistance instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s77e3e98716c0521","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tinker's Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know the Mending cantrip.</p><p>As a Magic action while holding Tinker's Tools, you can create one item in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of yourself, choosing the item from the following list:</p><ul><li>Ball Bearings</li><li>Basket</li><li>Bedroll</li><li>Bell</li><li>Blanket</li><li>Block and Tackle</li><li>Bottle, Glass</li><li>Bucket</li><li>Caltrops</li><li>Candle</li><li>Crowbar</li><li>Flask</li><li>Grappling Hook</li><li>Hunting Trap</li><li>Jug</li><li>Lamp</li><li>Manacles</li><li>Net</li><li>Oil</li><li>Paper</li><li>Parchment</li><li>Pole</li><li>Pouch</li><li>Rope</li><li>Sack</li><li>Shovel</li><li>Spikes, Iron</li><li>String</li><li>Tinderbox</li><li>Torch</li><li>Vial</li></ul><p>The item lasts until you finish a Long Rest, at which point it vanishes.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"you must be holding Tinker's Tools"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-offering-ritual.webp","_id":"s781bfdfac57f9fe","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Speech Beyond the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to reach beyond death's veil in search of knowledge. Using this feature, you can cast Speak with Dead without material components, and you understand what the target of this casting says. It can understand your questions, even if you don't share a language or it is not intelligent enough to speak.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s785259de19daa87","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Paths of the Dead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of death allows you to tread the paths used by ghosts and other spirits. Using this feature, you can cast Etherealness. Once the spell ends, you can't cast it with this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78726ef369e9ec5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Earthen Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your connection to earth to meld slightly into stone and earthen surfaces, granting you a Climb Speed equal to your Speed when climbing such surfaces.</p><p>Additionally, when you have to make a Strength Saving Throw or check, you can make a Charisma Saving Throw or check instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78ca135edcb69be","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fighting Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your intensity in battle can shield you and help you strike true. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can give yourself Advantage on weapon Attack Rolls until the end of the current turn. When you do so, you also gain temporary hit points equal to your fighter level + Wisdom modifier.</p><p>You can use this feature three times. You regain one use when you finish a Short Rest and all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s78cedf28332ac61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher that deals fire damage or it fails a save against such a spell, you also set it aflame.</p><p>A creature that is aflame takes fire damage equal to twice your Proficiency at the start of each of its turns and sheds bright light in a radius of 10 feet and dim light light in a radius of 10 feet beyond that for 1 minute.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature can make a DEX Saving Throw against your spell save DC to end the effect on itself. Alternatively, it or another creature can spend an Action to put out the flames.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s791bcbd992024ef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Urban Lore","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar become Proficient in three skills out of the following: Deception, Insight, Investigation, Stealth, Persuasion, and Sleight of Hand. Both of you double your Proficiency for one of the chosen skills, this need not be the same skill. Both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for any of the chosen skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s793532dba739641","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 8)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s79832867357169c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Light Steps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You make any stealth check that is contingent on not being heard rather than not being seen with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-sandals-tan.webp","_id":"s79a97d95448c3d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Harbinger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in intimidation. Additionally, the bonus damage of your Divine Smite also applies to good-aligned creatures. Additionally, if a feature or spell allows you to do radiant damage, you can cause it to deal necrotic damage instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s79d18994d7ba8b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Axiom","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mutagenic hemocraft lets your Brand of Castigation reveal a foe's true nature. Any illusion or invisibility in effect on a creature when you brand it ends, and the creature can't benefit from invisibility or illusion effects while branded by you. If a creature branded by you is in an alternative form (by way of the Polymorph spell, the Change Shape action or Shapechanger trait, the Wild Shape feature, and similar effects), it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or revert to its true form and be Stunned until the end of your next turn. Whenever a branded creature attempts to alter its form, it must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or have the attempt fail, and it is Stunned until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a03b43a738030e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twin Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While your spellbook's spectral mind is manifested, it can concentrate for you on any spell you cast through the spellbook or on a scroll that has been placed inside of it. If the spectral mind disappears, that spells ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a0602ea7d697b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rune Carver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a Long Rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Runes Known</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Number of Runes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>10th</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>15th</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The following runes are available to you when you learn a rune. If a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a Saving Throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.</p><h5>Cloud Rune</h5><p>This rune emulates the deceptive magic used by some cloud giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks and Charisma (Deception) checks.</p><p>In addition, when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to invoke the rune and choose a different creature within 30 feet of you, other than the attacker. The chosen creature becomes the target of the attack, using the same roll. This magic can transfer the attack's effects regardless of the attack's range. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Fire Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic channels the masterful craftsmanship of great smiths. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses your Proficiency with a tool.</p><p>In addition, when you hit a creature with an attack using a weapon, you can invoke the rune to summon fiery shackles: the target takes an extra 2d6 fire damage, and it must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw or be Restrained for 1 minute. While Restrained by the shackles, the target takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, banishing the shackles on a success. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Frost Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic evokes the might of those who survive in the wintry wilderness, such as frost giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Animal Handling) checks and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action to increase your sturdiness. For 10 minutes, you gain a +2 bonus to all Ability Checks and Saving Throws that use Strength or Constitution. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Stone Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic channels the judiciousness associated with stone giants. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks, and you have darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.</p><p>In addition, when a creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to invoke the rune and force the creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. Unless the save succeeds, the creature is Charmed by you for 1 minute. While Charmed in this way, the creature has a Speed of 0 and is Incapacitated, descending into a dreamy stupor. The creature repeats the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Hill Rune</h5><p>This rune's magic bestows a resilience reminiscent of a hill giant. While wearing or carrying an object that bears this rune, you have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Poisoned, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action, gaining Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage for 1 minute. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><h5>Storm Rune</h5><p>Using this rune, you can glimpse the future like a storm giant seer. While wearing or carrying an object inscribed with this rune, you have Advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks, and you can't be Surprised as long as you aren't Incapacitated.</p><p>In addition, you can invoke the rune as a Bonus Action to enter a prophetic state for 1 minute or until you're Incapacitated. Until the state ends, when you or another creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to cause the roll to have Advantage or Disadvantage. Once you invoke this rune, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a1890398bd9ddc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of Corrosion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blood curse can infuse a creature's body with terrible toxins. You gain the Blood Curse of Corrosion for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["2 * @attributes.prof","acid"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/dissolve-arm-flesh.webp","_id":"s7a4730bf381d6e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Conjuration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are concentrating on a conjuration spell, your Concentration can't be broken as a result of taking damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7a9953c01ccf8ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Meditation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the power granted by the Hunter's Bane to rapidly heal your wounds. If you spend 10 uninterrupted minutes in meditation, you can spend a number of Hit Dice up to your Proficiency as if you had taken a Rest. You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7aa6336054d9465","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to make your weapon strikes undercut a creature's Resistance to your spells. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, that creature has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes against a spell you cast before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7aa88ab4ff2a72e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through the vagaries of fate, your own study of the supernatural, or other circumstances you have come into contact with a mystical force or great entity whom you are sworn to serve. As a proxy and teacher, you are provided with a constant companion in the form of a bonded familiar.</p><p>This familiar takes the form of a beast, celestial, elemental, fiend, plant, or undead of CR 0, which you choose. It uses the corresponding statblock of the creature, but uses your proficiency bonus and mental ability scores in place of its own. In addition to its own, it also shares your saving throw proficiencies and any of your skill proficiencies that use Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. For each level in this class, it also gains 4 additional hit points. When you finish a Short or Long Rest, your bonded familiar regains all its hit points.</p><p>Your bonded familiar can understand and speak all languages you speak. While it is on the same plane of existence as you, you can communicate with it telepathically.</p><p>Your bonded familiar acts independently of you, but it always obeys your commands. In combat, it rolls its own initiative and acts on its own turn.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can shunt your bonded familiar into a safe pocket dimension. You can recall it to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you in the same manner.</p><p>Should your bonded familiar die, you can resummon it with a special ritual that takes 10 minutes. Alternatively, you can resummon it as an Action by spending a spell slot of 1st level or higher.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7ac2d9ec6141ea7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gnome Cunning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all INT, WIS, and CHA Saving Throws against magic.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"s7ad8dd53d6ad12b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Supreme Sneak","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Stealth checks and you do not lose the benefits of being Hidden as long as you end your turn behind at least three-quarters cover or heavily obscured.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"s7af3e956a3ea718","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Arcana","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Arcana checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7b0182fa2ae3b69","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tools of the Trade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with heavy armor. You also gain Proficiency with armorsmith's tools. If you already have this tool Proficiency, you gain Proficiency with one other type of artisan's tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/smithing/plate-steel-grey.webp","_id":"s7b9bc5e7fc5fae4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If a creature has a Bardic Inspiration die from you and casts a spell that restores hit points or deals damage, the creature can roll that die and choose a target affected by the spell. Add the number rolled as a bonus to the hit points regained or the damage dealt. The Bardic Inspiration die is then lost.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-firefly-hand-yellow.webp","_id":"s7b9c930422454d6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar of the Extraplanar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain expertise in Arcana and two additional languages.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"s7bb72f3282e840e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hollow Warden Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Ranger level specified in the Hollow Warden Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hollow Warden Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Wrathful Smite</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Spike Growth</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Guardian of Nature</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Sanguine Vortex</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7bfc4f78a949a96","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast any level 1+ spell from your Psionic Spells feature, you can cast it by expending a spell slot as normal or by spending a number of Sorcery Points equal to the spell's level. If you cast the spell using Sorcery Points, it requires no Verbal or Somatic components, and it requires no Material components unless they are consumed by the spell or have a cost specified in it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7c40bdd09032a6a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sun Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 4 Ki Points as an Action and become wreathed in a luminous, magical aura for 10 minutes. You shed bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. This light counts as sunlight. You can extinguish or restore the light as a Bonus Action.</p><p>If a creature hits you with a melee attack while this light shines, it takes radiant damage equal to a roll of your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7d23e111af43ef3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artillerist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Artillerist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Artillerist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Shield, Thunderwave</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Scorching Ray, Shatter</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fireball, Wind Wall</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Ice Storm, Wall of Fire</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s7d61251285afb48","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Conversion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can replace the damage of any of your elemental disciplines with that of another elemental discipline you know when you use them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7da68937dda26e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wind Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Immunity to lightning and thunder damage.</p><p>You also gain a magical Fly Speed of 60 feet. As an Action, you can choose a number of creatures within 30 feet of you equal to 3 + your Charisma modifier and grant them a Fly Speed of 60 feet for 1 hour. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or until you spend 5 Sorcery Points to use it again..</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7db9c152765ad32","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to temporarily grow and take on the appearance of a treelike person, covered with leaves and bark. As a Bonus Action, you assume this guardian form, which lasts until you end it as a Bonus Action or until you are Incapacitated.</p><p>You undergo the following changes while in your guardian form:</p><ul><li>Your size becomes Large, unless you were larger.</li><li>Your reach increases by 5 feet.</li><li>You gain a number of temporary hit points at the start of each of your turns. The number equals half your ranger level. When the form ends, you lose any temporary hit points you have from it.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice and you regain all expended uses on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7dca349c9c214ac","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortifying Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your experience surviving harrowing environments allows you to bolster your allies in addition to yourself. When you finish a Short Rest, you can choose a number of creatures you can see equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). A chosen creature regains Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Ranger level and has Advantage on Constitution Saving Throws and Wisdom Saving Throws to avoid or end the Frightened condition for 24 hours.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7e383a82482ed33","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Radiant Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An ally affected by your Channel Divinity: Radiant Defense also has Resistance against the damage of the triggering attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7e6043b1f7e2b0c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hydrokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Shape Water cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7e6368e895de98d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Friendly Face","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/commoner.webp","_id":"s7fa36c0a4884bcc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Fanged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Killing Bite.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can immediately make another attack with them as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Stronger Together.</strong> Allies within 20 feet of you also benefit from your Feral Resilience while you are not Unconscious.</li><li><strong>Feral Defiance.</strong> Your Ferocious Vitality recharges on a Short or a Long Rest and heals for 1x Shifter level additional hit points.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s7fb919a00e82154","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Discoveries","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list or any combination thereof (see a class's section for its spell list). A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table.</p><p>You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s80695084b0a5056","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Menacing","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Intimidation skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/water-elemental-blue-teeth.webp","_id":"s80ca50b21f64fc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature three times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"s810fad0302fd904","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Skirmisher","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are difficult to pin down during a fight. You can move up to half your Speed as a Reaction when an enemy ends its turn within 10 feet of you. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8113a70837cf743","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You ignore Resistance to psychic and force damage, and you treat Immunity to them as Resistance instead. Additionally, you double your Proficiency for Intelligence Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s813ca7d9dd6def7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits while shifted:</p><ul><li>Your can increase your size to Huge and your Natural Weapons die is tripled for calculating your base weapon damage. If you lack the room to become Huge, your size doesn't change.</li><li>You can't be Charmed or Frightened. If you are Charmed or Frightened when you use Formshift, the effect is suspended for the duration of the shift.</li><li>The healing gained from your Ferocious Vitality feature is increased to 5x your Shifter level.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"s816bedfba59ca9b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Twisting Roots.</strong> While shifted, the ground in a 10 feet circle around you is 3 for your enemies. When a creature starts its turn in that area or enters it for the first time on a turn, you can use your Reaction to force it to make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, its Speed is reduced to 0 until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Fey Step.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that you can see. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 2nd Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li><li><strong>Addling Spores.</strong> As an Action, you launch a cloud of befuddling spores at a location within 30 feet of you. Each creature within a 10 feet radius sphere around that point has to make a Constitution a Saving Throw or be Confused until the end of your next turn.</li><li>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 3rd Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s81a91452b1f099e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roguish Archetype","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an archetype that you emulate in the exercise of your rogue abilities from the list of available archetypes. Your archetype choice grants you features at 3rd level and then again at 9th, 13th, and 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-robe-evil-power.webp","_id":"s81ec1acf81c29ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inured to Undeath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to necrotic damage, and your hit point maximum can't be reduced. You have spent so much time dealing with undead and the forces that animate them that you have become inured to some of their worst effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s81f1162fb8eb8b2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to become the centerpiece of a fighting unit and direct others to fight more effectively. Choose an ally within 60 feet that can see or hear you and isn't incapacitated and select one of the options below. You can use any number of the listed options on the same ally or divide them up between multiple allies.</p><ul><li>On your turn, you can use your Bonus Action to give the target an additional Bonus Action on their next turn. Alternatively, the target can use its Reaction to use this Bonus Action immediately.</li><li>You can use your Reaction to give the target an additional Reaction until the start of your next turn. This Reaction cannot be used on the same turn as their normal Reaction.</li><li>On your turn, you can subtract a multiple of 5 from your Speed and add the amount to the target's Speed for its next turn. The amount of Speed the target gains in this manner cannot be higher than its base Speed. This feature has no effect on a target whose Speed is currently 0. You can choose multiple targets. If you do so, you have to divide the amount you subtract among the targets in multiples of 5. Any one of the targets can choose to use their Reaction to move up to the Speed gained in this manner immediately. This movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks. If it does not use up all Speed gained in this manner, it loses the rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/infantry-army.webp","_id":"s8229c310e283d23","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to fight with your Spiritual Weapon like a seamless unit, using it to attack as well as defend.</p><p>When a creature you can see hits you with an Attack Roll while your Spiritual Weapon is within 5 ft of you, you can use your Reaction to gain a +5 bonus to AC against that attack, potentially causing it to miss you.</p><p>If the attack misses, you can make one weapon attack or melee spell attack with your Spiritual Weapon against the attacker as part of this Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8230f09b42a6119","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Henotic Ascendence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the realm of the divine permanently changes you. You gain Resistance to the damage type you chose for the Harm effect of your Channel Divine Energy class feature. For every 10 years that pass, your body only ages 1 year. Additionally, the dice from your pool change to d10s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s834d92d7bc481dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Otherworldly Glamour","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your fey qualities give you a supernatural charm. As a result, whenever you make a Charisma check, you gain a bonus to the check equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p>In addition, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Performance, or Persuasion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s837e79b2f9914d0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frozen Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you cast a Ranger spell using a Spell Slot, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier + half your Ranger level (rounded down). If the spell already gives you temporary hit points, they stack with the ones granted by this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s838a846ad935630","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Elf Spellcasting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>All Dark Elves enjoy the protection of their patron goddess. Excepting the cantrip, you can cast the following spells once per Long Rest without expending material components. Your spellcasting ability for these spells is WIS or CHA (your choice). You can also cast them using spell slots you have of the appropriate level.</p><p>Dancing Lights, Sanctuary, Healing Spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s83a26390cbfaaba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Concentration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your aura of protection fosters mental focus. You and your allies have Advantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain Concentration while in your Aura of Protection.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s83e2e048e52ff44","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blessed Healer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The healing spells you cast on others heal you as well. When you cast a spell of 1st level or higher that restores hit points to a creature other than you, you regain hit points equal to 2 × the spell's level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"s83f3af5ef697811","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your command of sword magic grows stronger, allowing you to harness it for protection.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can grant an aegis to yourself or one allied creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The aegis is a dim, gray aura of earth magic that protects the target. Any bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage the target takes is reduced by half your sorcerer level (rounded down). This effect lasts for 1 minute or until you use it again.</p><p>In addition, when a creature you can see within 60 feet of you hits the protected target (which can be you) with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of the attacker. You can then make one melee weapon attack against the attacker. If that attack hits, it deals an extra 1d10 force damage. This extra damage increases to 2d10 at 11th level and 3d10 at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s83ff9d18e8254bc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of the moon suffuses you, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Improved Lunar Blessing.</strong> Once per turn, you can deal an extra 2d10 Radiant damage to a target you hit with a Wild Shape form's attack.</li><li><strong>Shared Moonlight.</strong> Whenever you use Moonlight Step, you can also teleport one willing creature. That creature must be within 10 feet of you, and you teleport it to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of your destination space.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8406422c6333499","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inner Alchemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can suspend the effect of one potion with a duration of more than 1 minute currently affecting you. You can resume the effect of one potion suspended in this manner at any time as a Bonus Action. Deduct the time of the potion's effect in increments of 1 minute. When you finish a Long Rest, all potion effects still suspended on you end.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8484ac093efedea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expanded Element","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use another element or expand your understanding of your own element. You learn the damage types, cantrip, and elemental defense of that elemental school and you quality for all elemental infusions that have that elemental school as prerequisite.</p><p>This also allows you access to powerful composite kinetic shape, by either combining two different elements or focusing on a single one. You gain another element at 14th level, but you can't choose the same element a third time.</p><p>Using a composite shape requires a great deal of energy and costs 2 kinesis points each time. If you do so, increase the number of dice for that kinetic shape by half (rounded up).</p><p>If your composite shape features two of the same element, you double your Charisma modifier when determining the kinetic shape damage and the cost for using a composite shape is reduced to 1 kinesis point.</p><p>You also gain access to whatever infusion any of the included elements normally would allow, but you do pay their kinesis point cost as normal.</p><p>When you do combine elements with different damage types, half of the total damage is dealt as either damage type. For example, if you use a composite shape of the water and fire elements and roll for a total of 20 damage, 10 damage will be dealt as bludgeoning and 10 as fire.</p><p>If the damage number is uneven, you determine which damage type deals the higher amount.</p><p>You can find a table with the resulting composite elements below:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Composite Elements</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">\\</th><th scope=\"col\">Air</th><th scope=\"col\">Earth</th><th scope=\"col\">Fire</th><th scope=\"col\">Water</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Air</td><td>Storm</td><td>Sand</td><td>Plasma</td><td>Blizzard</td></tr><tr><td>Earth</td><td>Sand</td><td>Metal</td><td>Magma</td><td>Mud</td></tr><tr><td>Fire</td><td>Plasma</td><td>Magma</td><td>Blue Fire</td><td>Steam</td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td>Blizzard</td><td>Mud</td><td>Steam</td><td>Frost</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-smoke-pink.webp","_id":"s84b24e05edb8438","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mob Rule","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use your Cunning Strike feature, you learn the following new way to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Bully (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or all Attack Rolls against it have Advantage until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Cow (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you.</li></ul><p>Additionally, you can reduce the die cost of any of your Cunning Strike options by 1 (to a minimum of 0) while none of your target's allies are within 5 feet of it and at least 1 of your allies is within their melee reach. You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s84e5874e87c8544","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Like a Fish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your attunement to the element of water allows you to move within it just as easily as on land. You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed and you can breathe underwater. If you already have a Swim Speed, that Swim Speed instead increases by 30 feet.</p><p>Additionally, you make any Athletics checks and Saving Throws related to swimming or resisting water-based effects using your Charisma modifier instead of your Strength modifer.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s851feff929a00d0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inky Escape","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call upon your patron to escape from your foes. As a Reaction when you take damage, you can cast Darkness centered on a point within 5 ft. of you. The spell lasts until the end of your next turn, does not require concentration, and has no effect on your vision.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you cannot use it until you complete a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s852a9e8d2b8cb32","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ranger Conclave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose to emulate the ideals and training of a ranger conclave from the list of available conclaves. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 5th, 7th, 11th, and 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8590206aaefdd9b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Retaliation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage from a creature that is within reach of your equipped melee weapon, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/weapons-crossed-swords-yellow.webp","_id":"s859484ae81016ed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Monster Slayer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose three creature types, except humanoids. Whenever you expend superiority dice to add to a damage roll, you can expend up to two dice instead of just one, adding both to the roll. Both dice are expended as normal. If the target of your attack has one of your chosen creature types, you deal maximum damage with all combat superiority dice you expended, instead of rolling them.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s85d8e9157958015","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Fortitude","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can spend any number of sorcery points to roll a d4 for each point expended. You gain a number of temporary hit points equal to the total rolled + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"s85e0152a85b502e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persistent Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can regain all expended uses of Rage. After you regain uses of Rage in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, your Rage is so fierce that it now lasts for 10 minutes without you needing to do anything to extend it from round to round. Your Rage ends early if you have the Unconscious condition (not just the Incapacitated condition) or don Heavy armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"s8620054d6dc6993","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Raven's Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Raven Mother grants you a protective blessing. You gain Advantage on death Saving Throws, Immunity to the Frightened condition, and Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s863bfddeb9a6427","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Champion's Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a second Reaction. Additionally, you make Initiative checks with Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s86552e815838aec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Confounding Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Charm (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to succeed on a Wisddom Saving Throw or become Charmed by you for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns to end the effect.</li><li><strong>Confuse (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target has to succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or become Confused until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s86abfe03ea71528","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hand of Devastation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spells deliver exceptional power. When you roll damage for a spell, you can reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8700dc34a298193","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spider Queen's Chosen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The Spider Queen extends her protection to you while you are in her favored form. You gain Resistance to psychic and poison damage while in your spider form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8753ce782d9b7d0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcery Points","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have 2 sorcery points, and you gain one additional point every time you level up, to a maximum of 20 at level 20. You can never have more sorcery points than shown on the table for your level. You regain all spent sorcery points when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.sorcerer.sorcery-points","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/runes-star-pentagon-orange.webp","_id":"s876f4c97b82810b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase your size to Large when you use your Formshift class feature and your Natural Weapons die is doubled for calculating your base weapon damage while you are shifted. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn't change.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/bull-horns-eyes-glowin-orange.webp","_id":"s8782ccda088efe4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Artificer Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose the type of specialist you are, each of which is detailed at the end of the class's description. Your choice grants you features at 5th level and again at 9th and 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s87fb35cb9b2c1e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Walker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast the Commune with Nature spell, but only as a ritual. When you do so, a spiritual version of one of the animals you chose for Totem Spirit or Aspect of the Beast appears to you to convey the information you seek.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s884994d9d6ecc48","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Roving Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed isn't reduced to 0 by using Cunning Action: Aim.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s88660cd13924112","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Night Flyer.</strong> You gain a darkvision range of 120 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 120 ft to its range.</li><li><strong>Agile Flyer.</strong> Your Speed increases by 10 feet and you do not provoke Opportunity Attacks when you fly out of an enemy's reach.</li><li><strong>Diving Raptor.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce, you can move up to double your Speed if your target is below you. If you moved at least 20 feet in this manner, the attack adds your Natural Weapons die to the damage again once.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s88d27a91555a84e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"s88df4aa92712010","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Defy Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can give yourself vitality when you cheat death or when you help someone else cheat it. You can regain hit points equal to 1d8 + your Warlock level when you succeed on a death Saving Throw or when you stabilize a creature with Spare the Dying.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s88e34406fadf6aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Life Link","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You create magical bond between your lifeforce and that of your Eidolon. When you or your Eidolon take damage that would reduce you to 0 hitpoints, you are reduced 1 hitpoint instead and the other takes the remainder of the damage.</p><p>The link has no effect on features that outright kill you when you are reduced to 0 hitpoints, such as the Disintegrate spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/debuff-energy-hold-green.webp","_id":"s89a3fa081fd1802","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Reinforcements","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The royal courts of the Feywild have blessed you with the assistance of fey beings: you know Summon Fey. It doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know, and you can cast it without a material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require Concentration. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s89a5a7c495b4854","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Shadow Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can draw on your Shadowfell connection to empower your teleportation. When you use your Shadow Step, you can expend 1 Ki Point to remove the requirement that you must start and end in Dim Light or Darkness for that use of the feature. As part of this Bonus Action, you can make an Unarmed Strike immediately after you teleport.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s89e9e6c16b435d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transmuter's Stone","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can spend 8 hours creating a transmuter's stone that stores transmutation magic. You can benefit from the stone yourself or give it to another creature. A creature gains a benefit of your choice as long as the stone is in the creature's possession. When you create the stone, choose the benefit from the following options:</p><ul><li>Darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If the holder already has darkvision, its range increases by 60 feet.</li><li>An increase to Speed of 10 feet while the creature is unencumbered.</li><li>Proficiency in Constitution Saving Throws.</li><li>Resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (your choice whenever you choose this benefit).</li></ul><p>Each time you cast a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher, you can change the effect of your stone if the stone is on your person.</p><p>If you create a new transmuter's stone, the previous one ceases to function.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8a023572bbba941","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Rebuke","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to chastise anyone who dares wield beguilements against you and your wards. Whenever you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you succeeds on an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to deal 2d8 + your Charisma modifier force damage to the creature that forced the Saving Throw.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8adc92495350b82","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flurry of Blows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend 1 Ki Point to make two Unarmed Strikes as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-yellow-red.webp","_id":"s8b1999389a5c40d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expanded Element (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another element, but you can't choose the same element a third time.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-smoke-pink.webp","_id":"s8b610c63f25fb75","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armorer Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Armorer Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Armorer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Magic Missile, Shield</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Mirror Image, Shatter</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Hypnotic Pattern, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Fire Shield, Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Passwall, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"s8b7a1ad31a8b551","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Emissary of Peace","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to diffuse violent situations. Whenever you make a Charisma check to calm violent emotions or to counsel peace, you have Advantage on the roll. You must make this entreaty in good faith; it doesn't apply if Proficiency in the Deception or Intimidation skill applies to your check.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Performance or Persuasion skill (choose one).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8b97074dea60ddf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Casting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You ignore all restrictions on casting or concentrating on spells caused by being shifted. Additionally, when you cast a spell that heals or gives the target temporary hit points, you increase the healing or temporary hit points by an amount equal to your Formshift Damage.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, this bonus doubles.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8bb3f44b3ee5884","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Faithful Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The nature spirits you commune with protect you when you are the most defenseless. If you are reduced to 0 hit points or are Incapacitated against your will, you can immediately gain the benefits of Conjure Animals as if it were cast using a 9th-level spell slot. It summons four beasts of your choice that are challenge rating 2 or lower. The conjured beasts appear within 20 feet of you. If they receive no commands from you, they protect you from harm and attack your foes. The spell lasts for 1 hour, requiring no Concentration, or until you dismiss it (no action required).</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8bbc013461f3971","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Coordination","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take an additional action and Bonus Action on your turn.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short Rest or you spend a spell slot of 4th level or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8c0c96be6cf0367","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fey Wanderer Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Fey Wanderer Spells table. Each spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fey Wanderer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Charm Person</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Dimension Door</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Mislead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>You also possess a preternatural blessing from a fey ally or a place of fey power. Choose your blessing from the Feywild Gifts table or determine it randomly.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Feywild Gifts</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Gift</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Illusory butterflies flutter around you while you take a Short or a Long Rest.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Fresh, seasonal flowers sprout from your hair each dawn.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>You faintly smell of cinnamon, lavender, nutmeg, or another comforting herb or spice.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Your shadow dances while no one is looking directly at it.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Horns or antlers sprout from your head.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Your skin and hair change color to match the season at each dawn.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8c236ff324f215f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Irresistible Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Otto's Irresistible Dance spell prepared. You can cast it without expending a spell slot. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of the feature by expending four uses of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8c4528e4055a607","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Controlled Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you roll on the Wild Magic table, you can roll the die twice and choose which of the two effects to unleash. If you roll the same number on both dice, you can ignore the number and choose any effect on the table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8c7db3b673c05c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiency","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-layered-steel.webp","_id":"s8cc7d7ad0f8631d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stay the Cycle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An a Reaction when you activate the effect of a Lunar Phase, your familiar can prevent you from entering the next one in the cycle if it is within 120 feet of you.</p><p>Your bonded familiar can use this feature twice and it regains all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8cdf098fd54e0e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor Model","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can customize your Arcane Armor. When you do so, choose one of the following armor models: Guardian or Infiltrator. The model you choose gives you special benefits while you wear it.</p><p>Each model includes a special weapon. When you attack with that weapon, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity, to the attack and damage rolls. If your armor has an enhancement bonus, it is added to these attack and damage rolls.</p><p>You can change the armor's model whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, provided you have armorsmith's tools in hand.</p><p><strong>Dreadnought.</strong> You design your armor to become a towering juggernaut in battle. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul><p><strong>Guardian.</strong> You design your armor to be in the front line of conflict. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul><p><strong>Infiltrator.</strong> You customize your armor for subtle undertakings. It has the following features:</p><ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/hand/gauntlet-armored-grey.webp","_id":"s8db9a441d3ce99c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gloom Stalker Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Gloom Stalker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Gloom Stalker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Disguise Self</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rope Trick</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Greater Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8df6717938005ba","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Panache","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You also learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Disarm (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Strength or Dexterity Saving Throw (target's choice) or drop 1 item of your choice that it is holding. The target has Advantage on this Saving Throw if it is holding the item with both hands or is at least 1 size larger than you. This feature has no effect against a creature more than 2 sizes larges than you.</li><li><strong>Goad (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against targets other than you and be unable to make Opportunity Attacks against targets other than you until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Parrying Stance (Cost: 2d6).</strong> Roll 2d6. You gain a bonus to your AC equal to half the number rolled (rounded up) until the start of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e472bef074f41c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wails from the Grave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As you nudge someone closer to the grave, you can channel the power of death to push them over the threshold or harm someone else as well. When you deal your Sneak Attack damage to a creature on your turn, you can cause that creature to take additional damage. Alternatively, you can target a second creature that you can see within 30 feet of the first creature. Roll half the number of Sneak Attack dice for your level (round up), the original target or the second creature takes necrotic damage equal to the roll's total, as wails of the dead sound around them for a moment.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e49c9c39ab0ecc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Eldritch Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional eldritch invocation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e4c6b260d852d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hour of Reaping","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to unsettle or terrify those around you as an Action, for your soul has been touched by the shadow of death. When you take this action, each creature within 30 feet of you that can see you must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or be Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><p>You can also this feature when you gain temporary hit points through Touch of Death (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8e8a574c32c48b8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Naturally Stealthy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attempt to hide even if you are obscured only by a creature that is at least one size larger than you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"s8e9571ef6676829","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thunderbolt Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal lightning or thunder damage to a Large or smaller creature, you can also push it up to 10 feet away from you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f0bd856d9d8afb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Words of Creation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have mastered two of the Words of Creation: the words of life and death. You therefore always have the Power Word Heal and Power Word Kill spells prepared. When you cast either spell, you can target a second creature with it if that creature is within 10 feet of the first target. You can cast either spell once without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to cast these spells this way when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/scream-wail-shout-teal.webp","_id":"s8f2051e810bf9f2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Labyrinthine Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means, unless you allow it. You can present false thoughts by succeeding on a Charisma (Deception) check contested by the mind reader's Wisdom (Insight) check. You are also Immune to the Charmed condition.</p><p>Additionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates you are being truthful if you so choose, and you can't be compelled to tell the truth by magic.</p><p>If you fail a Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to reroll the Saving Throw and add your Intelligence modifier to it, even if it was already added, taking whichever result was higher.</p><p>You can use this feature three times and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f590c4cd8d6479","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primeval Awareness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ranger lore allows you to establish a powerful link to beasts and to the land around you.</p><p>You have an innate ability to communicate with beasts, and they recognize you as a kindred spirit. Through sounds and gestures, you can communicate simple ideas to a beast as an Action, and can read its basic mood and intent. You learn its emotional state, whether it is affected by magic of any sort, its short-term needs (such as food or safety), and actions you can take (if any) to persuade it to not attack.</p><p>You cannot use this ability against a creature that you have attacked within the past 10 minutes.</p><p>Additionally, you can attune your senses to determine if any of your favored enemies lurk nearby. By spending 1 uninterrupted minute in Concentration (as if you were concentrating on a spell), you can sense whether any of your favored enemies are present within 5 miles of you. This feature reveals which of your favored enemies are present, their numbers, and the creatures' general direction and distance (in miles) from you.</p><p>If there are multiple groups of your favored enemies within range, you learn this information for each group.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/eye-slit-pink.webp","_id":"s8f9467b10e64bb4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Riptide","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When one or more creatures have to make a Strength Saving Throw against one of your features or spells, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on that Saving Throw.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency modifier and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8f97da3488ce9c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expansive Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The benefits of your Bonds of Solidarity and Protective Bond features now work when the creatures are within 60 feet of each other. Moreover, when a creature uses Protective Bond to take someone else's damage, the creature has Resistance to that damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s8fc68e1309f5ac6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elf Weapon Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with the elvish sword, greatsword, longbow, and shortbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/bows/shortbow-recurve-yellow.webp","_id":"s8ff977395028af9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Witchcraft","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Through arcane study and the guidance of your bonded familiar, you learn special occult practices and abilities. You gain four witchcraft options of your choice. When you finish a Long Rest you can replace one witchcraft you know with another one.</p><p><strong>Amelioration.</strong> As an Action, you touch a creature that is Blinded, Deafened, Poisoned, or is afflicted with a disease and magically alleviate its affliction. The target does not suffer the effects of your choice of one of these conditions until the start of your next turn. This does not remove the effects from the target and has no effect on them if they are reapplied during this time.</p><p><strong>Cackle.</strong> As an Action, you magically disrupt the ability to recover of one creature that can hear you within 60 feet. Until the start of your next turn, the target makes Saving Throws against ongoing effects on it with Disadvantage.</p><p><strong>Evil Eye.</strong> As an Action, you can curse a creature that you can see within 60 feet. The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it subtracts 1d4 from the result of all D20 Tests it makes until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Familiar Focus.</strong> As an Action, you can perceive through your bonded familiar's senses in addition to your own. You can end this effect again as an Action. Additionally, you can cast any spell or use any witchcraft option from your bonded familiar's space.</p><p><strong>Kettle Chant.</strong> When you make a crafting check using alchemist's supplies, cook's utensils, herbalist's kit, or poisoner's kit, you add half your spellcasting ability modifier (rounded down).</p><p><strong>Mind Fog.</strong> As an Action, you can befuddle the mind of a creature you can see within 60 feet and that is currently concentrating. The target immedidately has to make a Concentration Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 10 + half your Witch level (rounded up) + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Minor Prophecy.</strong> Your gift for divination allows you to foresee minor events. When a creature you can see within 60 feet succeeds on or fails a D20 Test, you can use your Reaction to turn the roll on the D20 into a 9 or 11 (your choice). You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Witch Spittle.</strong> As an Action, you touch a creature and rub spit laced with a minor healing enchantment over its injuries. The target regains hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. If the target is your bonded familiar, it regains additional hit points equal to your Witch level. A creature cannot benefit from this effect again until it has finished a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s901ef0784a2070f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell-Breaking Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you hit a creature with your Spellguard Strike, you can cast Counterspell as part of the same Reaction.</p><p>Additionally, once per turn when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can cast Dispel Magic as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9065a53a65acd9f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drain Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can drain power from ongoing spells to recharge your allies' magic. As a Magic Action, you can touch a willing creature and end one ongoing level 1 or level 2 spell on it; the creature immediately recovers one expended spell slot of level 2 or lower (the target's choice). Alternatively, you regain a number of Empower Sneak Attack uses equal to the spell's level.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s909d15daeba3d14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Firearm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know how to turn a wand, staff, or rod into an arcane firearm, a conduit for your destructive spells. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can use woodcarver's tools to carve special sigils into a wand, staff, or rod and thereby turn it into your arcane firearm. The sigils disappear from the object if you later carve them on a different item. The sigils otherwise last indefinitely.</p><p>You can use your arcane firearm as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells. When you cast an artificer spell through the firearm, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/wands/wand-carved-fire.webp","_id":"s91489e382d6e292","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Bonded Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your familiar learns all Witch cantrips you know and can cast them without material components. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus and spell save DC for these cantrips.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s915b60121130f94","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have dedicated yourself to one of the following sacred roles of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Magician.</strong> You know one extra cantrip from the Druid spell list. In addition, your mystical connection to nature gives you a bonus to your Intelligence (Arcana or Nature) checks. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum bonus of +1).</li><li><strong>Warden.</strong> Trained for battle, you gain Proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Medium armor.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-sproud-hands-dirt-green.webp","_id":"s91b762adbacaca5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Argent Conjunction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At the start of your turn, you can choose to gain the effects of all Lunar Phases at the same time (no action required). If you choose to activate the effect of a Lunar Phase, you likewise trigger the active effects of all Lunar Phases.</p><p>You can use this feature twice and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91bd661d61b023d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Umbral Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Curse (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw or be cursed until the end of your next turn. For the duration of the effect, the target must roll a d4 every time it rolls an Attack Roll or Saving Throw and subtract the result from the total.</li><li><strong>Enfeeble (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or deal half damage with weapon attacks until the end of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Additionally, while you are in darkness, you can reduce the cost of any feature that uses your Sneak Attack dice by 2 instead of 1 (to a minimum of 0). You can do so only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91bfe6dcf43a141","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Whispers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you cloak yourself in dark magic that preys upon the instinctual fears of your foes. When you use this feature, you can designate any number of creatures to be unaffected by it. The effect lasts for 1 hour or until you are Incapacitated or dismiss this effect as a Bonus Action.</p><p>When a creature sees you while you are under this effect, it has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a success, the creature becomes Immune to this feature for the next 24 hours. A creature that is Immune to the Frightened condition is unaffected by this feature.</p><p>On a failure, the creature's enchanted subconscious forces it to ignore you, to the point it denies your existence altogether. You are automatically treated as Hidden from the creature for the duration. All memories of you while affected by this feature are likewise suppressed, even after the effect ends.</p><p>If the creature is in Combat with you, it can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s91f57b0023d3efd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Use Magic Device","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Attunement.</strong> You can attune to up to four magic items at once.</li><li><strong>Charges.</strong> Whenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges.</li><li><strong>Scrolls.</strong> You can use any Spell Scroll, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for the spell. If the spell is a cantrip or a level 1 spell, you can cast it reliably. If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC 10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, you cast the spell from the scroll. On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-chain.webp","_id":"s92b6e41cb799417","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Visage of the Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can summon the visage of your astral self. As a Bonus Action, or as part of the Bonus Action you take to activate Arms of the Astral Self, you can spend 1 ki point to summon this visage for 10 minutes. It vanishes early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>The spectral visage covers your face like a helmet or mask. You determine its appearance.</p><p>While the spectral visage is present, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Astral Sight.</strong> You can see normally in darkness, both magical and nonmagical, to a distance of 120 feet.</p><p><strong>Wisdom of the Spirit.</strong> You have Advantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Charisma (Intimidation) checks.</p><p><strong>Word of the Spirit.</strong> When you speak, you can direct your words to a creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you, making it so only that creature can hear you. Alternatively, you can amplify your voice so that all creatures within 600 feet can hear you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9309e23c63294b6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undying Sentinel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points and not killed outright, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead, and you regain a number of Hit Points equal to three times your Paladin level. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>Additionally, you can't be aged magically, and you cease visibly aging.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s937340e412c634d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Atlas","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Adventurer's Atlas improves, gaining the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Safe Haven.</strong> When a map holder would be reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright, that creature can destroy its map. The creature's Hit Points instead change to a number equal to twice your Artificer level, and the creature is teleported to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you or another map holder of its choice.</p><p><strong>Unerring Path.</strong> If you are one of the map holders for your Adventurer's Atlas, you can cast Find the Path without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without needing spell components. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-eye-brown.webp","_id":"s93a05081912f971","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Phantasmal Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell that deals damage and is not an Illusion spell, you can change its school to Illusion and its damage type to psychic. If the spell requires a Saving Throw, that saving throw becomes a Wisdom saving throw.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93b94d3c31f8808","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Powerful Bloodline","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion grows to Large size and the reach of its bite attack increase to 10 feet, it also no longer suffers from restrictions to its flying capabilities while you are riding it as long it is at least one size larger than you.</p><p>Additionally, your companion's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s93da6c6dea192b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have developed ways to hamper your foes when you use your Sneak Attack. When you deal Sneak Attack damage, you can add one of the following Cunning Strike effects. Each effect has a die cost, which is the number of Sneak Attack damage dice you must forego to add the effect. You remove the die before rolling, and the effect occurs immediately after the attack's damage is dealt. For example, if you add the Lacerate effect, remove 1d6 from the Sneak Attack's damage before rolling.</p><p>If a Cunning Strike effect requires a Saving Throw, the DC equals 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Dexterity or Strength modifier (your choice).</p><ul><li><strong>Distract (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Lacerate (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target is Lacerated for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the Lacerated target can repeat the save, ending the effect on on a success.</li><li><strong>Trip (Cost: 1d6).</strong> If the target is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or be knocked Prone.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-white-orange.webp","_id":"s9402ac383585e63","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dark Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your allies have Resistance to radiant and necrotic damage while within your Aura of Protection.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9426bc0dd00b2ca","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alter Memories","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to make a creature unaware of your magical influence on it. When you cast an enchantment spell to charm one or more creatures, you can alter one creature's understanding so that it remains unaware of being Charmed.</p><p>Additionally, once before the spell expires, you can use your action to try to make the chosen creature forget some of the time it spent Charmed. The creature must succeed on an Intelligence Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC or lose a number of hours of its memories equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1). You can make the creature forget less time, and the amount of time can't exceed the duration of your enchantment spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s946e6a047caa549","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Experimental Elixir","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can magically produce a number of experimental elixirs equal to your Proficiency in empty flasks you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for each elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an Action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an Incapacitated creature.</p><p>Creating an experimental elixir requires you to have alchemist's supplies on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next Long Rest.</p><p>You can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your Action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Experimental Elixir</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Swiftness. The drinker's walking Speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every Attack Roll and Saving Throw they make for the next minute.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Flight. The drinker gains a Fly Speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the Alter Self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/consumables/potions/bottle-bulb-corked-purple.webp","_id":"s947022f7642c528","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Arts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your practice of martial arts gives you mastery of combat styles that use your Unarmed Strike and Monk weapons, which are the following:</p><ul><li>Simple Melee Weapons</li><li>Martial Melee Weapons that have the Light property</li></ul><p>You gain the following benefits while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield.</p><ul><li><strong>Bonus Unarmed Strike.</strong> You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Martial Arts Die.</strong> You can roll 1d6 in place of the normal damage of your Unarmed Strike or Monk weapons. This die changes as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Features table.</li><li><strong>Dexterous Attacks.</strong> You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. In addition, when you use the Grapple or Shove option of your Unarmed Strike, you can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier to determine the save DC.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"s948f8de52a4adc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Enveloping Winds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can surround yourself with a whirling torrent of air or a static field of crackling lightning, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier and all ranged weapon attacks against you are made with Disadvantage. Additionally, any gas, vapor, or fog that can be dispersed by a strong wind has no effect on you.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s94997468fc75f17","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Armor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as shown below.</p><p><strong>Dreadnought.</strong> When you use your Giant Stature, your reach increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Large or Huge (your choice), and you have Advantage on Strength Checks and Strength Saving Throws for the duration.</p><p>When you hit a creature with your Force Demolisher, creatures within 10 ft of it also take 2d6 force damage. Additionally, the original target and every affected creature around it have to make a Strength Saving Throw against your Spell save DC. On a failure, they are knocked Prone. A creature makes this Saving Throw only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Guardian.</strong> When a Huge or smaller creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to magically force it to make a Strength Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you pull the creature up to 25 feet directly to an unoccupied space. If you pull the target to a space within 5 feet of you, you can make a melee weapon attack against it as part of this Reaction.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Infiltrator.</strong> Any creature that takes lightning damage from your Lightning Launcher glimmers with magical light until the start of your next turn. The glimmering creature sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius, and it has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls against you, as the light jolts it if it attacks you. In addition, the next Attack Roll against it has Advantage, and if that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d12 lightning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-gorget-steel-purple.webp","_id":"s94f22d071595c27","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pact Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your arcane research and the magic bestowed on you by your patron have given you facility with spells. The information below details how you use those rules with Warlock spells, which appear on the Warlock spell list.</p><p><strong>Cantrips.</strong> You know two Warlock cantrips of your choice. Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Warlock cantrip of your choice.</p><p>When you reach Warlock levels 4 and 10, you learn another Warlock cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Warlock Features table.</p><p><strong>Spell Slots.</strong> The Warlock Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your warlock spells of levels 1–5. The table also shows the level of those slots, all of which are the same level. You regain all expended Pact Magic spell slots when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>For example, when you're a level 5 Warlock, you have two level 3 spell slots. To cast the level 1 spell Witch Bolt, you must spend one of those slots, and you cast it as a level 3 spell.</p><p><strong>Prepared Spells of Level 1+.</strong> You prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose two level 1 Warlock spells.</p><p>The number of spells on your list increases as you gain Warlock levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Warlock Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Warlock spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the table. The chosen spells must be of a level no higher than what's shown in the table's Slot Level column for your level. When you reach level 6, for example, you learn a new Warlock spell, which can be of levels 1–3.</p><p>If another Warlock feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Warlock spells for you.</p><p><strong>Changing Your Prepared Spells.</strong> Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Warlock spell of an eligible level.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Ability.</strong> Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (your choice) is the spellcasting ability for your Warlock spells.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use an Arcane Focus as a spellcasting focus for your warlock spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/blood-spurt-spray-red.webp","_id":"s94f776149198c90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Ancestry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your draconic ancestry gives you special abilities. Choose a type of dragon from the table below. The type you choose influences your breath weapon and your damage Resistance.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Draconic Ancestry</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Dragon</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td><td>15 ft. cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td><td>15 ft. cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td><td>15 ft. cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td><td>5 by 30 ft. line (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td><td>15 ft. cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-fire-breath-orange.webp","_id":"s950c1dbe8468c61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Invocation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The study of runes has enabled you to wield primordial magic. Your knowledge of these runes is stored in your spellbook, though you determine the runes' cosmetic appearance. You can invoke these runes in the following ways:</p><ul><li><strong>Rune of Renewal.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature regains hit points equal to your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier and you removal all poisons and diseases affecting it.</li><li><strong>Rune of Destruction.</strong> When you cast a spell that deals damage, you can add your Wizard level + your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of that spell and change its damage type to force.</li><li><strong>Rune of Protection.</strong> When a creature you can see within 60 feet has to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to give it a bonus to that roll equal to your Intelligence modifier.</li><li><strong>Rune of Clarity.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can choose one creature you can see within 60 feet. That creature is under the effect of the Detect Magic and Comprehend Languages spells for the next 24 hours.</li></ul><p>You can invoke each rune once. When you finish a Short Rest, you can choose one rune and regain its use. When you finish a Long Rest, you regain the use of all runes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9512a0b371334c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of the Guardian","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can shield others from harm at the cost of your own health. When a creature within 10 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to magically take that damage, instead of that creature taking it. This feature doesn't transfer any other effects that might accompany the damage, and this damage can't be reduced in any way.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s95531bf6aa26c46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter Conclave Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hunter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Hunter's Mark</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Pass without Trace</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Barrage</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s955e366ff6e01e6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ascendant Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The maximum number of Profane Augmentations that can be grafted to your companion increases to three and the maximum for ability scores and AC conferred by the grafted body part increases to 22.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9565d45df966d7e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Transposition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to switch positions with your Eidolon if you can see it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s95920a341f57543","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stout Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against poison, and you have Resistance against poison damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"s95a938a8976779b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cunning Action: Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an additional way to use your Cunning Action: carefully aiming your next attack. As a Bonus Action, you give yourself Advantage on your next Attack Roll on the current turn. You can use this Bonus Action only if you haven't moved during this turn, and after you use the Bonus Action, your Speed is 0 until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/projectile-spiral-gray.webp","_id":"s962ef3d3efeb3aa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unwavering Mark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can menace your foes, foiling their attacks and punishing them for harming others. When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can mark the creature until the end of your next turn. This effect ends early if you are Incapacitated or you die, or if someone else marks the creature.</p><p>While it is within 5 feet of you, a creature marked by you has Disadvantage on any Attack Roll that doesn't target you.</p><p>In addition, if a creature marked by you deals damage to anyone other than you, you can make a special melee weapon attack against the marked creature as a Bonus Action on your next turn. You have Advantage on the Attack Roll, and if it hits, the attack's weapon deals extra damage to the target equal to half your fighter level.</p><p>Regardless of the number of creatures you mark, you can make this special attack a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9631402041fd9bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Plane Charter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s965ed0bfa5d2a90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Frozen Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you magically transform into a creature of living ice. In this form, you have Resistance to piercing, bludgeoning, and slashing damage as well as Immunity to cold damage and poison.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature hits you with a melee attack from within 10 ft or touches you while you are under the effect of your Aegis of Rime feature, it is immediately affected by your Clinging Frost feature. If it was already affected, it instead immediately makes a Constitution Saving Throw as if at the end of its turn, suffering the usual effect on a failure. Succeeding on this Saving Throw does not count towards the three successes needed to clear the effect. </p><p>Finally, creatures affected by your Clinging Frost suffer a -2 penalty to Constitution Saving Throws against your spells that deal cold damage.</p><p>You remain in this form for 1 minute. It ends early if you are incapacitated, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest or you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s967b380e5cd3f21","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bruiser's Arsenal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in martial weapons, medium armor, shields, as well as the Intimidation skill. If you are already proficient in Intimidation, you gain expertise in it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96ab6456ffbdc05","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bolstering Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can harness your wild magic to bolster yourself or a companion. As an Action, you can touch one creature (which can be yourself) and confer one of the following benefits of your choice to that creature:</p><ul><li>For 10 minutes, the creature can roll a d3 whenever making an Attack Roll or an Ability Check and add the number rolled to the d20 roll.</li><li>Roll a d3. The creature regains one expended spell slot, the level of which equals the number rolled or lower (the creature's choice). Once a creature receives this benefit, that creature can't receive it again until after a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>You can take this action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s96f3f340368d297","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (9th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 9th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-face-blue.webp","_id":"s97220a698724c77","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Countercharm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use musical notes or words of power to disrupt mind-influencing effects. If you or a creature within 30 feet of you fails a Saving Throw against an effect that applies the Charmed or Frightened condition, you can take a Reaction to cause the save to be rerolled, and the new roll has Advantage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you or a creature within 30 feet of you fails a Saving Throw against an effect that applies the Charmed or Frightened condition"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/sonic/scream-wail-shout-teal.webp","_id":"s9724a44a097b256","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Command Undead","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use magic to bring undead under your control, even those created by other wizards. As an Action, you can choose one undead that you can see within 60 feet of you. That creature must make a Charisma Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC. If it succeeds, you can't use this feature on it again. If it fails, it becomes friendly to you and obeys your commands until you use this feature again.</p><p>Intelligent undead are harder to control in this way. If the target has an Intelligence of 8 or higher, it has Advantage on the Saving Throw. If it fails the Saving Throw and has an Intelligence of 12 or higher, it can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of every hour until it succeeds and breaks free.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s974d16c7609e7e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keen Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Perception skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/corvid-watchful-glowing-green.webp","_id":"s985d0e46a0b3324","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise (Level 9)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Expertise in two of your Skill Proficiencies of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"s9875556ae604260","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Mysticism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your study of the supernatural gives you a limited ability to use magic. You can cast Detect Magic as a ritual. You can cast Protection from Evil and Good on yourself as a Bonus Action and without expending a Spell Slot, but you cannot cast it again with this feature until you finish a Long Rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells.</p><p>In addition, you gain the ability to speak three of the following languages of your choice: Abyssal, Celestial, Deep Speech, Draconic, Giant, Primordial, Sylvan, or Umbral.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s98d3de4728c7e9c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a draconic aspect, granting you physical traits such as scaled skin, vertical pupils, and sharp nails.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>As an Action, you can exhale destructive energy. All creatues in the area of effect take damage equal to a number of rolls of your Natural Weapons die equal to your Proficiency. The shape, Saving Throw, and damage type of your breath weapon is determined by your draconic form, which you choose when you gain this feature. You can find all available options in the table below. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Constitution modifier. Once you have used your breath weapon, you have to roll a d6 at the start of each of your turns. On a roll of 5 or 6, you regain your use of this feature.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, the size of your breath weapon doubles.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Character Advancement</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Dragon</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon Shape (Saving Throw)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Radiant</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Jabberwock</td><td>Fire</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Night</td><td>Force</td><td>60x5 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td><td>30 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Shadow</td><td>Necrotic</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Radiant</td><td>60x5 ft line (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Sylvan</td><td>Poison</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td><td>30 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s99771c9d83234fb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Back Alley Bruiser","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You don't need Advantage on the Attack Roll to use your Sneak Attack against a creature if its within your melee reach, none of its allies are within 5 feet of it, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.</p><p>Additionally, you can Sneak Attack with any melee weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s997b4e8dc683466","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shifting Form","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to enter a liquid state while moving.</p><p>When you move on your turn, you take only half damage from Opportunity Attacks, and you can move through any enemy's space but can't willingly end your move there.</p><p>On your turn, you can move through any space that is at least 3 inches in diameter and do so without squeezing. When you stop moving, the regular squeezing rules apply if you're in a space one size smaller than you. You can't willingly stop in a space smaller than that, and if you're forced to do so, you immediately flow to the nearest space that can fit you, back along the path of your movement.</p><p>If you start your turn with the Grappled and/or Restrained condition, you can spend half your Speed to immediately end those effects on you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9a3f7f926e524a0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bastion of Law","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can tap into the grand equation of existence to imbue a creature with a shimmering shield of order. As an Action, you can expend 1 to 5 sorcery points to create a magical ward around yourself or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The ward lasts until you finish a Long Rest or until you use this feature again.</p><p>The ward is represented by a number of d8s equal to the number of sorcery points spent to create it. When the warded creature takes damage, it can expend a number of those dice, roll them, and reduce the damage taken by the total rolled on those dice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9b1656a9e278fd5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Universal Speech","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have gained the ability to make your speech intelligible to any creature. As an Action, choose one or more creatures within 60 feet of you, up to a number equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). The chosen creatures can magically understand you, regardless of the language you speak, for 1 hour.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9b3141c003d360b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of Vengeance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The authority with which you speak your Vow of Enmity gives you greater power over your foe. When a creature under the effect of your Vow of Enmity makes an attack, you can use your Reaction to make a melee weapon attack against that creature if it is within range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9b3143a57812368","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Overchannel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase the power of your simpler spells. When you cast a wizard spell that deals damage, you can deal maximum damage with that spell.</p><p>The first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a Long Rest, you take 2d12 necrotic damage for each level of the spell, immediately after you cast it. Each time you use this feature again before finishing a Long Rest, the necrotic damage per spell level increases by 1d12. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/acid/projectile-faceted-glob.webp","_id":"s9b37269de617cd4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Glorious Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can turn defense into a sudden strike. When you or another creature you can see within 10 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to grant a bonus to the target's AC against that attack, potentially causing it to miss. The bonus equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of +1). If the attack misses, you can make one weapon attack against the attacker as part of this Reaction, provided the attacker is within your weapon's range.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain one expended use on a Short Rest and all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9b57a85c6c8fed5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The guardian spirits that aid you can provide supernatural protection to those you defend. If you are raging and another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your Reaction to reduce that damage by 2d6.</p><p>When you reach certain levels in this class, you can reduce the damage by more: by 3d6 at 10th level and by 4d6 at 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you are raging and another creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["20","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-blades-teal.webp","_id":"s9b9ac20623177ee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9bde4688b8245c0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dreadful Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can augment your weapon strikes with mind-scarring magic, drawn from the gloomy hollows of the Feywild. When you hit a creature with a weapon, you can deal an extra 1d4 psychic damage to the target, which can take this extra damage only once per turn.</p><p>The extra damage increases to 2d4 when you reach 11th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9c752b3e81a3539","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Student of War","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Deception, History, Insight, Intimidation, Investigation, Stealth. You can choose to gain Proficiency with an artisan's tools of your choice in place of any of these skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9cda01a2b62d76d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Formshift Damage to all Saving Throws. You do not gain this bonus if you're unconscious.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/spirit-fear-energy-pink.webp","_id":"s9ce2b8fa7f2e352","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Feral Senses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the forces of nature grants you Blindsight with a range of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-shadow-red.webp","_id":"s9d0fb7198ab718d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twilight Dancer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>True Hide in Plain Sight no longer carries penalties. Additionally, you now regain all uses of your Cunning Step and Slippery Escape on a Short Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d27f1dd9db5a6b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Hunter's Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you can take a Reaction to give yourself Resistance to that damage and any other damage of the same type until the end of the current turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/reptiles/serpent-horned-green.webp","_id":"s9d2e4afbd19be4b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Cycle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When Initiative is rolled, you enter one of the below Lunar Phases of your choice, as long as you are not wearing any armor or shield.</p><p>Each Lunar Phase has a passive and an active effect. You can trigger the active effect at the start of your turn (no action required). After you do so, you automatically enter the next Lunar Phase on the start of your next turn.</p><p>The order of Lunar Phases is New Moon -> Crescent Moon -> Full Moon, after which the cycle repeats.</p><p><strong>New Moon.</strong> You gain temporary hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. If you activate this effect, you gain additional temporary hit points equal to twice your Witch level.</p><p><strong>Crescent Moon.</strong> Your Speed increases by 10 feet. If you activate this effect, your speed is doubled and you cannot be targeted by Attacks of Opportunity.</p><p><strong>Full Moon.</strong> Your melee weapon attacks deal additional 1d4 radiant damage. If you activate this effect, the radiant damage increases to 2d4.</p><p>The additional damage increases at 5th level (1d6/2d6), 11th level (1d8/2d8), and 17th level (1d10/2d10) in this class.</p><p>You lose the benefits of any Lunar Phase when you don armor or a shield.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d481988584eec6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Scrivener","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The gold and time you must spend to make a spell scroll are halved if you use your Wizardly Quill.</p><p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can create one or more spell scrolls with a combined spell level of no more than your Proficiency. You do not have to make a skill check or provide any spell slots, gold, or time for these scrolls and the resulting scrolls automatically have the masterwork property. All other rules for creating spell scrolls apply normally.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9d6cf059cf9add6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extraordinary Acrobatics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces on your turn without falling during the move and you can use your Dexterity in place of your Strength to determine the distance of your jumps.</p><p>In addition, once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with an attempt to Climb onto a Bigger Creature, as per the Additional Combat Actions. You can attempt and maintain this special grapple even when you don't have a free hand.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9dad23556887c82","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Shots","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to infuse projectiles with magic. Whenever you make a ranged weapon attack with a nonmagical weapon, you can make it magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>Additionally, whenever you make a ranged weapon attack, you can change the damage type to any other damage type of your choice except bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9dd487d801ef714","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Evolution Feat","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional evolution feat for which you meet the prequisites.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9e342bdb146e0dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Song of Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can direct your magic to absorb damage while your bladesong is active. When you take damage, you can use your Reaction to expend one spell slot and reduce that damage to you by an amount equal to five times the spell's slot level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9e4c65cdd69fa51","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Piercing Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Wisdom modifier to Initiative rolls and to Investigation and Intimidation checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9e76b2e7de821b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Radiant Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are so suffused with righteous might that all your melee weapon strikes carry divine power with them. Whenever you hit a creature with a melee weapon, the creature takes an extra 1d10 radiant damage. The damage increases by 1d10 if the target is an undead or a fiend.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-gold-holy.webp","_id":"s9e971275fbbe263","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant's Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned how to imbue yourself with the might of giants. As a Bonus Action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn't change.</li><li>You have Advantage on strength checks and Strength Saving Throws.</li><li>Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike can deal an extra 1d6 damage to a target on a hit.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9e9874ca1f59172","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tipsy Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move in sudden, swaying ways. You gain the following benefits.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"s9f8610b354766c3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/blade-tip-chipped-blood-red.webp","_id":"sa026b70b8f94b59","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Tethering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The psychic damage from your Brand of Castigation increases to twice your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of 2). Additionally, a branded creature can't take the Dash action, and if it attempts to teleport or to leave its current plane by any means, it takes 4d6 psychic damage and must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the attempt to teleport or leave the plane fails.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/debuff-chains-red.webp","_id":"sa0ac6ad96780a73","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enhanced Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The bond with your wildfire spirit enhances your destructive and restorative spells. Whenever you cast a spell that deals fire damage or restores hit points while your wildfire spirit is summoned, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus equal to the number rolled to one damage or healing roll of the spell.</p><p>In addition, when you cast a spell with a range other than self, the spell can originate from you or your wildfire spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1607ee9f3b8a32","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast Conclave Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Beast Conclave Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Beast Bond</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Animal Messenger</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Catnap</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Charm Monster</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Awaken</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1657c3d21a941a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Protective Canopy.</strong> While you are shifted, your reach increases by 10 feet and allies within 10 feet of you have half-cover.</li><li><strong>Blinding Beauty.</strong> As an Action, you can force every creature of your choice within 30 feet of you that you can see and that can see you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, a target is Blinded for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the target can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success. Once a creature has succeeded on the Saving Throw, it is Immune to this feature for the next 24 hours.</li><li>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Formshift Damage and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a 4th Level Spell Slot to use this feature again.</li><li><strong>Aggressive Effluvia.</strong> Hostile creatures that start their turn within 30 feet of you or enter that space for the first time on a turn, take necrotic damage equal to double your Formshift Damage. Creatures that are Poisoned or have hit points equal to half or less of their maximum, take double damage from this feature. If you are Unconscious or dead, this effect disappears after 1d4 days.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1844470bab0788","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dimensional Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can cast Dimension Door without a verbal component. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1ebb210893f50c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you are in dim light or darkness, as a Bonus Action you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness. You then have Advantage on the first melee attack you make before the end of the turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa1fe50edfff3bc6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Mystic Fighting Style","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack Action or use your Flurry of Blows, you can cast a spell in place of two of your Unarmed Weapon attacks. You can use this feature only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa214f38a9be09f7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grim Psychometry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a supernatural talent for discerning the secrets surrounding mysterious relics or places touched by evil. You can use your hemocraft ability score for History checks and whenever you make a History check to recall information about the sinister or tragic history of an object you are touching or your current location, you have Advantage on the check. At the DM's discretion, a suitably high roll might cause your character to experience brief visions of the past connected to the object or location.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/hand-eye-fire-blue.webp","_id":"sa26554c9efec68d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Violent Attraction","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a gravity-based spell (e.g. Magnify Gravity) that deals force damage, you add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell.</p><p>Additionally, if a creature you can see within 60 feet of you takes damage from a fall, you can use your Reaction to deal additional force damage equal to a number of D10s x your Proficiency to the creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa2696eb06548df4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gnome Tinkerer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency with artisan's tools (tinker's tools). Using those tools, you can spend 1 hour and 10 gp worth of materials to construct a Tiny clockwork device (AC 5, 1 hp).</p><p>The device ceases to function after 24 hours (unless you spend 1 hour repairing it to keep the device functioning), or when you use your action to dismantle it; at that time, you can reclaim the materials used to create it. You can have up to three such devices active at a time. When you create a device, choose one of the following options or suggest an idea of your own to your DM.</p><ul><li><strong>Clockwork Toy.</strong> This toy is a clockwork animal, monster, or person, such as a frog, mouse, bird, dragon, or soldier. When placed on the ground, the toy moves 5 feet across the ground on each of your turns in a random direction. It makes noises as appropriate to the creature it represents.</li><li><strong>Fire Starter.</strong> The device produces a miniature flame, which you can use to light a candle, torch, or campfire. Using the device requires your action.</li><li><strong>Music Box.</strong> When opened, this music box plays a single song at a moderate volume. The box stops playing when it reaches the song's end or when it is closed.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/claw-mechanical.webp","_id":"sa26df4ccae9b2be","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211690,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hungry Darkness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Shield of Ineffable Darkness becomes more powerful. When you use it, you can select up to three additional, hostile creatures you can see within 30 feet of you. They have to make a CON Saving Throw or become Blinded until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa27f7886366f83b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brave","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Frightened.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sa2992bb36b54128","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to cold, fire, lightning, and thunder damage. When you use Elemental Might, you gain Immunity to the damage type of the chosen element.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa304557b5960f61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undeniable Ambition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Also add your Wisdom modifier to the D20 test when you use Reject Failure. If you fail the D20 test, you can choose to use Reject Failure again immediately without a Reaction, rerolling again and taking the highest result. You can only do so once per initial use of Reject Failure.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa316ac14c3fe10a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Invincible Conqueror","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to harness extraordinary martial prowess. As a Bonus Action, you can magically become an avatar of conquest, gaining the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can make one additional attack as part of that action.</li><li>The damage of your Aura of Conquest and Scornful Rebuke is doubled.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3212a4df1b0a0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Projection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spirit can become untethered from your physical form. As an Action, you can project your spirit from your body. The body you leave behind is Unconscious and in a state of suspended animation.</p><p>Your spirit resembles your mortal form in almost every way, replicating your game statistics but not your possessions. Any damage or other effects that apply to your spirit or physical body affects the other. Your spirit can remain outside your body for up to 1 hour or until your Concentration is broken (as if concentrating on a spell). When your projection ends, your spirit returns to your body or your body magically teleports to your spirit's space (your choice).</p><p>While projecting your spirit, you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>Your spirit and body gain Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li><li>When you cast a spell of the conjuration or necromancy school, the spell doesn't require verbal or somatic components or material components that lack a gold cost.</li><li>You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover. You can move through creatures and objects as if they were 3, but you take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.</li><li>While you are using your Form of Dread, once during each of your turns when you deal necrotic damage to a creature, you regain hit points equal to half the amount of necrotic damage dealt.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa33cd7cb54aa543","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bard College","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You delve into the advanced techniques of a bard college of your choice from the list of available colleges. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sa3708d95815e525","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Curving Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to direct an errant projectile toward a new target. When you make an Attack Roll with a magic projectile and miss, you can use a Bonus Action to reroll the Attack Roll against a different target within 60 feet of the original target.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3ae628c2813d25","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hound of Ill Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to call forth a howling creature of darkness to harass your foes. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 3 sorcery points to magically summon a hound of ill omen to target one creature you can see within 120 feet of you. The hound uses the dire wolf's statistics (see the Monster Manual or appendix C in the Player's Handbook), with the following changes:</p><ul><li>The hound is size Medium, not Large, and it counts as a monstrosity, not a beast.</li><li>It appears with a number of temporary hit points equal to half your sorcerer level.</li><li>It can move through other creatures and objects as if they were 3. The hound takes 5 force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.</li><li>At the start of its turn, the hound automatically knows its target's location. If the target was hidden, it is no longer hidden from the hound.</li></ul><p>The hound appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of the target. Roll initiative for the hound. On its turn, it can move only toward its target by the most direct route, and it can use its action only to attack its target. The hound can make Opportunity Attacks, but only against its target. Additionally, while the hound is within 5 feet of the target, the target has Disadvantage on Saving Throws against any spell you cast. The hound disappears if it is reduced to 0 hit points, if its target is reduced to 0 hit points, or after 5 minutes.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa3c080421ca0b71","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tandem Footwork","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration if you don't have the Incapacitated condition. When you do so, roll your Bardic Inspiration die; you and each ally within 30 feet of you who can see or hear you gains a bonus to Initiative equal to the number rolled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa4010420cac2e98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Game of Caps","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Magic Mushrooms are Invisible to anyone other than you and any number of creatures you designate when you initially create them.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can move any circle of mushrooms to a different point you can see within 60 feet of its original position.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa45385bd2a4f7a8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Walker in Dreams","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of the Feywild grants you the ability to travel mentally or physically through dreamlands.</p><p>When you finish a Short Rest, you can cast one of the following spells, without expending a spell slot or requiring material components: Dream (with you as the messenger), Scrying, or Teleportation Circle.</p><p>This use of Teleportation Circle is special. Rather than opening a portal to a permanent Teleportation Circle, it opens a portal to the last location where you finished a Long Rest on your current plane of existence. If you haven't taken a Long Rest on your current plane, the spell fails but isn't wasted.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa498194ea97ea89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Winged Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Death from the Dark.</strong> Once per turn, when you hit a creature you are hidden from with your natural weapons, you deal additional damage equal to two rolls of your Natural Weapons die and the target has to make a Wisdom Saving Throw.</li><li>The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target is Frightened until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Evasive Flight.</strong> When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw, and only half damage if you fail.</li><li>If you succeed on the Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to move up to half your Speed to an unoccupied space that you can see. If you are carrying an ally or otherwise moving them with you, they also automatically succeed on the Saving Throw and take no damage.</li><li>You don't benefit from this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</li><li><strong>Concussive Impact.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and hit the target, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). On a failure, the target suffers an effect based on the distance you travelled as part of Primal Pounce. The listed effects are cumulative.</li><ul><li><strong>20 feet or more:</strong> The target is knocked Prone.</li><li><strong>40 feet or more:</strong> The target is Dazed until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>60 feet or more:</strong> The target is Stunned until the end of your next turn.</li></ul></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa53015986872439","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Purity of Spirit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are always under the effects of a Protection from Evil and Good spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/toxins/poison-bottle-corked-fire-green.webp","_id":"sa53ab3ab3d37914","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Avenger","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your supernatural focus helps you close off a foe's retreat. When you hit a creature with an Opportunity Attacks, you can reduce the creature's Speed to 0 until the end of the current turn. You can then move up to half your Speed as part of the same Reaction. This movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa5756c06fb5113f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Durable Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Any creature that you summon or create with a conjuration spell has temporary hit points equal to twice your Wizard level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa5969d88f2f2849","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor of Faith","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can target yourself with your Inspiring Surge. When you affect a creature with your Inspiring Surge and the target regains hitpoints in excess of its hitpoint maximum, it gains the difference as temporary hitpoints.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa6247b521747bf1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"War Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn when you take the Attack action, you can cast a cantrip in place of one of your weapon attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa646c1c9e447764","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you deal damage to a creature with Planar Warrior, you can choose to impose one of the following effects:</p><ul><li><strong>Planar Pulse.</strong> You deal the damage of Planar Warrior to all creatures of your choice within 10 ft of your target.</li><li><strong>Sealing Strike.</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it cannot teleport move to a different Plane through any means until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Teleporting Strike.</strong> The target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw or be teleported 30 ft horizontally to an unoccupied space your choice that is on a solid surface.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa664b6849fd745c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>By studying the magic of the planes, coming into contact with an extraplanar entity, or other circumstances you have acquired the ability to call forth a magical entity called an Eidolon.</p><p>To summon your Eidolon, you have to spend 10 minutes performing a magical ritual. Upon completion, your Eidolon appears in an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of you.</p><p>When the Eidolon drops to 0 hit points, it disappears, leaving behind no physical form. If your Eidolon is more than 1000 feet away from you or you die, it also disappears. You can also dismiss your Eidolon as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Your Eidolon can understand and speak all languages you speak. While it is on the same plane of existence as you, you can communicate with your Eidolon telepathically.</p><p>Additionally, as an Action, you can see through your Eidolon's eyes and hear what it hears until you end the effect (no action required), gaining the benefits of any special senses that the Eidolon has. During this time, you are deaf and blind with regard to your own senses.</p><p>Your Eidolon acts independently of you, but it always obeys your commands. In combat, it rolls its own initiative and acts on its own turn.</p><p>When you acquire this feature, you choose a template for your Eidolon that determines it's base statistics. Your options are: aquatic, avian, biped, quadruped, serpentine, and tauric. Your Eidolon shares your mental ability scores and all Saving Throw proficiencies.</p><p>Additionally, your Eidolon learns two skills of your choice.</p><p>If you have a bonus to spell save DC, you also apply this bonus to your Eidolon's Attack Rolls, damage rolls, and armor class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":10,"units":"minute"},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-giant-forest-blue.webp","_id":"sa670ed5800f8c1d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legendary Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you fail a Saving Throw, you can succeed instead. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when your Eidolon fails a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":3,"max":3,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/barrier-shield-dome-deflect-teal.webp","_id":"sa682167fbced9e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Overwhelming Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The size of your weapon's damage die increases by 2 steps.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/shield-damaged-broken-orange.webp","_id":"sa6976669c68e353","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Verdant Reprisal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Enemies affected by your Protector's Mark have Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you while they are within 30 feet of you.</p><p>Additionally, if an affected enemy attacks a creature other than you while within that range, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed and make a weapon attack against that enemy. If you are mounted, your mount moves up to its own Speed instead. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1) and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Alternatively, you can spend a spell slot of 2nd level or higher to regain a use of this feature (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa70c832ba3c8e0b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add Symbol to your spellbook and it doesn't count against the number of prepared spells for you. When you cast the spell, you can choose a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier. The chosen creatures are exempt from the spell's effect when it is triggered.</p><p>Additionally, you can cast the spell without a spell slot and without material components. You cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa73cf64d15a4a01","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonded Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you cast a spell on yourself, you can choose to cast the spell on your Eidolon instead if you can see it within 60 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa7527a35be7bc0a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Earth","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the earth allows you to move freely through the ground. You gain a Burrow Speed equal to your Speed and tremorsense in a radius of 60 feet around you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa7c265ad67db845","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Evolution Feats","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>In your study of planar lore, you have unearthed ways to augment your Eidolon, changing its form or otherwise imbuing it with new abilities.</p><p>You gain two evolution feats of your choice. A list of the available options can be found on the Optional Features page. When you gain certain summoner levels, you gain additional evolution feats of your choice, as shown in the Evolution Feats column of the Summoner table.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the evolution feats you know and replace it with another evolution feat that you could learn at that level.</p><p>If an evolution feat has prerequisites, you must meet them to learn it. You can learn the evolution feat at the same time that you meet its prerequisites. A level prerequisite refers to your level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/bat-giant-tattered-purple.webp","_id":"sa7e13ddb7fcca26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Second Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a limited well of physical and mental stamina that you can draw on. As a Bonus Action, you can use it to regain Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Fighter level.</p><p>You can use this feature twice. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>When you reach certain Fighter levels, you gain more uses of this feature, as shown in the Second Wind column of the Fighter Features table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.second-wind","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"heal","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["1d10 + @classes.fighter.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"sa86851d9575db76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 15th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa8b899fd4d09410","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Red Exultation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice) plus your Rogue level (minimum of 1 Temporary Hit Point). You also gain this benefit if someone else reduces an enemy within 10 feet of you to 0 Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa8f3e34cbd0e43f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Weakening Hex","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you apply your Hexblade's Curse to a creature, it also has Disadvantage its next Saving Throw before the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa96e835a885868f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steady Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your aim becomes deadly. As a Bonus Action on your turn, you can take careful aim at a creature you can see that is within range of a ranged weapon you're wielding. Until the end of this turn, your ranged attacks with that weapon gain two benefits against the target:</p><ul><li>The attacks ignore half and three-quarters cover.</li><li>On each hit, the weapon deals additional damage to the target equal to 2 + half your fighter level.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature three times. You regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Additionally, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to regain one use.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa99877868d69524","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You know how to strike subtly and exploit a foe's distraction. Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack if you have Advantage on the Attack Roll. The attack must use a finesse or a ranged weapon.</p><p>You don't need Advantage on the Attack Roll if another enemy of the target is within 5 feet of it, that enemy isn't Incapacitated, and you don't have Disadvantage on the Attack Roll.</p><p>The amount of the extra damage increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Sneak Attack column of the Rogue table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-arcane-pink.webp","_id":"sa9b39cb85f54721","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tireless Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by an additional 10 feet. Additionally, whenever you finish a Short Rest, your Exhaustion level, if any, decreases by 1.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-bladed-boots-fire.webp","_id":"sa9d39945ba0ea1a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Prey","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can focus your ire on one foe, increasing the harm you inflict on it. Once per turn, you can designate one creature you can see as the target of this feature (no action required). The first time each turn that you hit that target with a weapon attack, it takes an extra 1d6 damage from the weapon. This damage increases to 2d6 when your reach 11th level in this class.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sa9e950e00e6834a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Charisma modifier to your strength checks.</p><p>Additionally, your melee weapon attacks deal an additional 1d10 damage of the weapon's type. This extra damage increases to 2d10 at 11th level and 3d10 at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saa591fcad9abe16","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Flesh of Stone","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can harden your body like stone, dampening the impact of most attacks until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Constitution modifier + your Charisma modifier and any bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing you take is reduced by an amount equal to half your kineticist level (rounded down), this reduction applies before any other effect.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saafe030229c9be0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can supernaturally inspire others through words, music, or dance. This inspiration is represented by your Bardic Inspiration die, which is a d6.</p><ul><li><strong>Using Bardic Inspiration.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can inspire another creature within 60 feet of yourself who can see or hear you. That creature gains one of your Bardic Inspiration dice. A creature can have only one Bardic Inspiration die at a time. Once within the next hour when the creature fails a D20 Test, the creature can roll the Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning the failure into a success. A Bardic Inspiration die is expended when it's rolled.</li><li><strong>Number of Uses.</strong> You can confer a Bardic Inspiration die a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). You regain one die when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li><li><strong>At Higher Levels.</strong> Your Bardic Inspiration die changes when you reach certain Bard levels, as shown in the Bardic Die column of the Bard Features table. The die becomes a d8 at level 5, a d10 at level 10, and a d12 at level 15.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"max(1, @abilities.cha.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"@scale.bard.inspiration","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sab3287e49ae0b88","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Watcher at the Threshold","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to necrotic and radiant damage. In addition, while you aren't Incapacitated, any ally within 30 feet of you has Advantage on death Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sab5c39303f12b02","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Theotic Conduit","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to harness divine energy improves further. You regain a number of dice every time you expend a spell slot to cast a spell from the cleric spell list. The number of dice you regain is equal to the level of the expended spell slot. Additionally, the dice from your pool change to d8s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sabfb163c3bd1133","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Body of the Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you have both your astral arms and visage summoned, you can cause the body of your astral self to appear (no action required). This spectral body covers your physical form like a suit of armor, connecting with the arms and visage. You determine its appearance.</p><p>While the spectral body is present, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Improved Deflect Attack.</strong> The damage dealt by your Deflect Attack increases to three rolls of your Martial Arts die and you can change the damage type to force damage.</p><p><strong>Empowered Arms.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a target with the Arms of the Astral Self, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to your Martial Arts die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac0ab8bab3685e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Terror of the Skies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion grows to Huge size and the reach of its bite attack increases to 15 feet, its Strength and Constitution also increase by 2, to a maximum of 22.</p><p>Additionally, the damage of its Breath Weapon increases to 10d6 and the cone size increases to 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac61c5635155e78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Sabotage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Spell Susceptibility (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes against a spell until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Steal Resistance (Cost: 2d6).</strong> Choose one kind of damage. If the target has Resistance to that kind of damage, until the start of your next turn, the target loses that Resistance and you gain Resistance to that damage type.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sac84aa18d2f9204","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Giant Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can magically empower your bonded familiar for 10 minutes if it is within 60 feet of you. It gains the following benefits for the duration:</p><ul><li>Your bonded familiar grows to Huge size. If it lacks the room to become Huge, its size does not change.</li><li>Your bonded familiar's Strength and Constitution score are equal to your spellcasting ability score. If the latter is lower, your bonded familiar's stats do not change. It does not gain any hit points from this increase in Constitution, instead its current and maximum hit points increase by an amount equal to 5 x your Witch level.</li><li>Your bonded familiar has Advantage on Strength and Constitution Saving Throws.</li><li>The damage dice gained through the Battle Familiar feature are tripled.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature you cannot use it against until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saca4d31729c53ec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Zealous Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to channel divine power to inspire zealotry in others. As a Bonus Action, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you that can hear you gain Advantage on Attack Rolls and Saving Throws until the start of your next turn.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. If you've run out of uses of this feature, you can expend one use of your Rage, choosing to activate this feature instead of Rage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sacd664ac9590b2f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Convergent Future","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can peer through possible futures and magically pull one of them into events around you, ensuring a particular outcome. When you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you makes an Attack Roll, an Ability Check, or a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to ignore the die roll and decide whether the number rolled is the minimum needed to succeed or one less than that number (your choice).</p><p>The first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a Long Rest, you take 1d12 necrotic damage for each level (or CR if the creature has no levels) the target creature has. Each time you use this feature again before finishing a Long Rest, the damage increases by 1d12 per level/CR. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sace0fe3423c85c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jotun Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The resilience of giants flows through your body. Your hit point maximum increases by 3, and it increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, when you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 10 + your Strength modifier + your Charisma modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sacef670be1c19d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clockwork Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the Clockwork Spells table. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>Whenever you gain a sorcerer level, you can replace one spell you gained from this feature with another spell of the same level. The new spell must be an abjuration or a transmutation spell from the sorcerer, warlock, or wizard spell list.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Clockwork Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Alarm, Protection from Evil and Good, Aid, Lesser Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dispel Magic, Protection from Energy</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Freedom of Movement, Summon Construct</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Greater Restoration, Wall of Force</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>In addition, consult the Manifestations of Order table and choose or randomly determine a way your connection to order manifests while you are casting any of your sorcerer spells.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Manifestations of Order</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">d6</th><th scope=\"col\">Manifestation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Spectral cogwheels hover behind you.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>The hands of a clock spin in your eyes.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Your skin glows with a brassy sheen.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Floating equations and geometric objects overlay your body.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Your spellcasting focus temporarily takes the form of a Tiny clockwork mechanism.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>The ticking of gears or ringing of a clock can be heard by you and those affected by your magic.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sad2497cecc43773","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Aura","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your guardian form emanates a magical aura that fortifies your injured allies. When any ally starts their turn within 30 feet of your guardian form, that ally regains a number of hit points equal to half your ranger level. This aura has no effect on undead and constructs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sae21ef6b4dedfe8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Arcanum (8th level)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron bestows upon you a magical secret called an arcanum. Choose one 8th-level spell from the warlock spell list as this arcanum.</p><p>You can cast your arcanum spell once without expending a spell slot. You must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-face-black.webp","_id":"sae3e092917d4bdc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Step through the Circle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you create a 10-feet radius circle of mushrooms at a point you can see within 30 feet. You can only have up to three of these circles at the same time. Whenever you create an additional one beyond that number, the oldest one disappears. A circle lasts for 1 year or until you trigger one of the following effects an Action:</p><p><strong>Travel Back.</strong> You and up to 8 other willing creatures of your choice within 10 feet are teleported to the circle's location.</p><p><strong>Travel Forth.</strong> You and up to 8 other willing creatures within the circle are teleported as per the effect of the Plane Shift spell.</p><p>Once you have triggered one of the above effects, you cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sae6b413a28fc434","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll initiative, you regain a number of superiority dice equal to half your maximum (rounded down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sae87ed1dcc42f89","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Draconic Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed when you are shifted, but you have to end your flying movement on the ground.</p><p>Additionally, you gain Resistance to the damage type associated with your Draconic Form.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saeccda586e0023e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Multiattack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/death/skull-trio-badge-purple.webp","_id":"saf06d21d42db29f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Blows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can expend a use of your Second Wind when you hit with a weapon attack. If you do so, the target takes additional damage equal to 1d10 + your fighter level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf096d262932d46","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Veil Wardens Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Veil Wardens Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Detect Evil and Good, Protection from Evil and Good, Darkvision, Mental Barrier</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Intellect Fortress, Magic Circle</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Arcane Storm, Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Circle of Power, Planar Binding</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"saf45c6df43ac728","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Path","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose a path that shapes the nature of your rage from the list of available paths. Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th levels.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/projectile-wave-arrow.webp","_id":"saf691dfa94217f0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Divine Spark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action, you point your Holy Symbol at another creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself and focus divine energy at it. Roll 2d8 and add your Cleric level and your Wisdom modifier. You either restore Hit Points to the creature equal to that total or force the creature to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the creature takes Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice) equal to that total. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage (round down).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"2d8 + @abilities.wid.mod","save":{"ability":"con","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-glow-spiral-yellow.webp","_id":"safb9c3b277eecdb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Horizon Walker Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Horizon Walker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Horizon Walker Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Protection from Evil and Good</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Haste</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Banishment</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Teleportation Circle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"safc5a239e4388ad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Incalculable Sway","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>No Attack Roll can have Advantage against you when you are under the effect of Patient Defense.</p><p>Additionally, whenever an Attack Roll misses you, you can move 10 feet in any direction without provoking Attacks of Opportunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"safc8034cc595ed1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Step of the Wind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action. Alternatively, you can expend 1 Ki Point to take both the Disengage and Dash actions as a Bonus Action, and your jump distance is doubled for the turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/air-wave-gust-blue.webp","_id":"sb07514d85b9fda3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Intimidating Shout","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you force all hostile creatures within 60 feet that can hear you to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, a target deals half damage on its weapon attacks that hit until the start of your next turn.</p><p>This feature has no effect against creatures that are Immune to the Frightened condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb17756877f20bef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wanderer of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Survival skill and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for this skill.</p><p>Additionally, you gain one of the following benefits based on your chosen Wild Domain:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Wild Domain Feature</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>You are acclimatized to extreme heat and your Speed increases by 5 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>You and your bonded familiar cannot be Surprised unless you are Incapacitated.</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>You are acclimatized to extreme cold and you ignore 3 caused by ice and snow, magical or otherwise.</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed. If you already have a Swim Speed, you add 30 feet to it.</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Stealth skill and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for this skill.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb186af72e313eef","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Friendly Fungi","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The radius of your mushroom circles increases to 20 feet and when you activate your Magic Mushrooms, you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your spellcasting ability modifier from the effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb1a220b6c14c1c9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Breath Weapon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to exhale destructive energy. Your draconic ancestry determines size, shape, and damage of the exhalation. Every creature in the area of a effect needs to make a Saving Throw against a DC of 8 + your CON, INT, or CHA modifier (your choice) + your Proficiency. The damage equals 4d6 on a failed save, and have as much on a successful one. The damage increases by 1d6 at levels 6, 11, and 16.</p><p>After you use your breath weapon, you can't use it again until you complete a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["(4+floor(((@details.level)-1)/5))d6",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/beam-jet-stream-trails-orange.webp","_id":"sb1d26b9c9e7e359","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bestial Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The feral power within you increases, causing the natural weapons of your Form of the Beast to count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p>You can also alter your form to help you adapt to your surroundings. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you finish your next Short or a Long Rest:</p><ul><li>You gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you can breathe underwater.</li><li>You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed, and you can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an Ability Check.</li><li>When you jump, you can make a Strength (Athletics) check and extend your jump by a number of feet equal to the check's total. You can make this special check only once per turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb1f766dce3fec16","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Saint of Forge and Fire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your blessed affinity with fire and metal becomes more powerful:</p><ul><li>You gain Immunity to fire damage.</li><li>You can now use your Blessing of the Forge feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb234f90cf8eca14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sanctuary Vessel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter your Genie's Vessel via the Bottled Respite feature, you can now choose up to five willing creatures that you can see within 30 feet of you, and the chosen creatures are drawn into the vessel with you.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can eject any number of creatures from the vessel, and everyone is ejected if you leave or die or if the vessel is destroyed.</p><p>In addition, anyone (including you) who remains within the vessel for at least 10 minutes gains the benefit of finishing a Short Rest, and anyone can add your Proficiency bonus to the number of hit points they regain if they spend any Hit Dice as part of a Short Rest there.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb23efcea2431459","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspired Ferocity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an ally that is currently affected by your Warcry lands a critical hit, it deals additional damage equal to half your warlord level (rounded down) + your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb34039e8a2d69b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Conquest","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You constantly emanate a menacing aura while you're not Incapacitated. The aura extends 10 feet from you in every direction, but not through total cover.</p><p>Any creature of your choice that starts its turn in the aura takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier. If that creature is Frightened, this damage is doubled. Additionally, any creature in the aura that is Frightened, has its Speed reduced to 0.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb37a6981230c6bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Careful Eyes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You excel at picking out hidden enemies and other threats. You can take the Search action as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You also gain Proficiency in the Perception, Investigation, or Survival skill (choose one).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb37b2e1c558b545","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bonus Proficiencies","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: Arcana, History, Insight, Investigation, Nature, or Perception. You can choose to gain Proficiency with thieves' tools in place of one skill choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/academics-investigation-puzzles.webp","_id":"sb38a2d69355ce8f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mark of the Ordning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class. These spells depend on your chosen giant heritage, as shown in the tables below. The spells count as sorcerer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Cloud Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Silent Image, Invisibility, Warding Wind</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Gaseous Form, Major Image</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Greater Invisibility, Hallucinatory Terrain</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Control Winds, Seeming</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Fire Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Burning Hands, Catapult, Enhance Ability, Heat Metal</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Elemental Weapon, Fireball</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fabricate, Fire Shield</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Creation, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Frost Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Frost Fingers, Hold Person, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm, Summon Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Fire Shield, Ice Storm</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Bigby's Hand, Cone of Cold</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Hill Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Longstrider, Earthbind, Protection from Poison</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Create Food and Water, Erupting Earth</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Locate Creature, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Destructive Wave, Tree Stride</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Stone Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Id Insinuation, Sleep, Calm Emotions, Suggestion</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Enemies Abound, Meld into Stone</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Stoneskin, Stone Shape</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Modify Memory, Wall of Stone</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Storm Giant Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Identify, Witch Bolt, Detect Thoughts, Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Clairvoyance, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Divination, Storm Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Scrying, Legend Lore</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb3fd76885eb503e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strength before Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you drop to 0 Hit Points and don't die outright, you can instead drop to 1 Hit Point and immediately move up to your Speed and make a weapon attack.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb4117bbbeedc869","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empress of the Fathoms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of water allows you to infuse your own self with the essence of waves.</p><p>As an Action, you undergo the transformation and gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You ignore all water-based effects such as the Tsunami spell or a natural vortex.</li><li>You gain Immunity to cold damage.</li><li>Water flows from everywhere, including up from the ground and dropping as rain to form a vortex of writhing watery tentacles in a 60 feet radius around you that makes the area 3. You and any number of creatures of your choice in the area unaffected.</li><li>Any other creature that enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your save DC or be Grappled and Restrained. It can make a Strength check as an Action on its turn to no longer be Grappled and Restrained.</li></ul><p>Once you have used this ability, you can't use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb4317b47804b052","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infectious Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you hit a creature with your natural weapons while you are raging, the beast within you can curse your target with rabid fury. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Constitution modifier + your Proficiency bonus) or suffer one of the following effects (your choice):</p><ul><li>The target must use its Reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of your choice that you can see.</li><li>The target takes 2d12 psychic damage.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb4586914f5cdd34","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Siphon Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>One of the things that contributes the most to the reputation Shadowborn have among other races, is their ability to harness residual life energy from the dead. For this reason, Shadowborn are very conscious of when they use this ability.</p><p>As an Action, you can siphon energy from a creature within 5 ft of you that has died within the last 24 hours. If you do so, you can spend hit dice as if you had taken a rest. You cannot use this feature more than once on the same creature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"target has died within the last 24 hours and has not been targeted by this feature before"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":5,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hands-cloud-light-pink.webp","_id":"sb48602422e0c615","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Necrotic Husk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to undeath and necrotic energy now saturates your body. You have Resistance to necrotic damage. If you are transformed using your Form of Dread, you instead become Immune to necrotic damage.</p><p>In addition, when you would be reduced to 0 hit points, you can use your Reaction to drop to 1 hit point instead and cause your body to erupt with deathly energy. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of you takes necrotic damage equal to 2d10 + your warlock level. Once you use this Reaction, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb508eb868bb5a91","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"All-Piercing Shot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can supercharge a shot with arcane energy. As part of this action, you can expend up to 3 uses of your Arcane Shot. The projectile shoots forth in a line 1 foot wide and 150 feet long, before disappearing. The projectile passes harmlessly through objects and magical barriers like Wall of Force, ignoring cover. Each creature in that line must make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Arcane Shot save DC. On a failed save, a creature takes 6d12 force damage + 2d12 additional force damage for every use of Arcane Shot you expended as part of this action.</p><p>You can use this feature once and you cannot use it again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb50ef87d3d8d4fd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clinging Frost","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you hit a creature with a spell of 1st level or higher that deals cold damage or it fails a save against such a spell, the magical cold you command starts clinging to it for 1 minute, reducing its Speed by 10 feet.</p><p>At the end of each of its turns, an affected creature can make a Constitution Saving Throw against your spell save DC. Each time it fails this Saving Throw, it suffers additional effects as per below. If it succeeds three times, the effect of your Clinging Frost ends on it.</p><ul><li><strong>One failed save:</strong> The affected creature cannot take Reactions.</li><li><strong>Two failed save:</strong> The affected creature has Disadvantage on Attack Rolls and Ability Checks.</li><li><strong>Three failed save:</strong> The affected creature is Frozen for 1 minute but does not have Resistance against cold damage caused by your spells and the effect of your Clinging Frost ends on it.</li></ul><p>This feature has no effect on creatures that cannot be Frozen.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb533c6f986abf90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guarded Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The psionic energy flowing through you has bolstered your mind. You have Resistance to psychic damage. Moreover, if you start your turn Charmed or Frightened, you can expend a Psionic Energy die and end every effect on yourself subjecting you to those conditions.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5519ab645cf894","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Skill Versatility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in 3 extra skills of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-unity-alliance.webp","_id":"sb5823659d5727d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silver Sisters Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing no armor and not wielding a shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p>Additionally, You gain Proficiency in martial weapons with the finesse property.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5997a1f0969e6d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rallying Cry","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to inspire your allies to fight on past their injuries.</p><p>When you use your Second Wind feature, you can choose up to three creatures within 60 feet of you that are allied with you. Each one regains hit points equal to your fighter level plus twice your Proficiency, provided that the creature can see or hear you.</p><p>If a creature is healed for more hit points than they are missing, they regain the difference as temporary hit points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb5fd1a5d8e8c686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Undying Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hold your breath indefinitely, and you don't require food, water, or sleep, although you still require rest to reduce Exhaustion and still benefit from finishing short and Long Rests. You are also Immune to diseases and poison.</p><p>In addition, you age at a slower rate. For every 10 years that pass, your body ages only 1 year, and you are Immune to being magically aged.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb6155ad8ad3e2b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unarmored Movement improvement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to move along vertical surfaces and across liquids on your turn without falling during the move.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/wave-water-teal.webp","_id":"sb61d4d6e0255132","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fancy Footwork","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to land a strike and then slip away without reprisal. During your turn, if you make a melee attack against a creature, that creature can't make Opportunity Attacks against you for the rest of your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb63aafad71cd06e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Jack of All Trades","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can add half your Proficiency bonus, rounded down, to any Ability Check you make that doesn't already include your Proficiency bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-steel.webp","_id":"sb64cb4020280dde","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Restore Balance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to the plane of absolute order allows you to equalize chaotic moments. When a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself is about to roll a d20 with Advantage or Disadvantage, you can take a Reaction to prevent the roll from being affected by Advantage and Disadvantage.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb670d2dbc572c5c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211666,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Runes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Carver feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb67eefab4287c5a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Sundering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your strikes expose a fragment of your foe's essence, leaving them vulnerable to your Crimson Rite feature.</p><p>Whenever you hit a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you roll an additional hemocraft die when determining the extra damage from the rite.</p><p>Additionally, if a branded creature has the Incorporeal Movement trait or a similar feature, it can't move through creatures or objects while branded and it cannot benefit from being Invisible.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb6e9b2de0ef74a7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Occult Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can cast the Nondetection spell, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability. When you do so, you can target only yourself, and the duration increases to 7 days.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb6e9c6a490c990e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Action Surge (two uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Action Surge twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sb6f2ec274890a50","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Imbuing Touch","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can touch one nonmagical weapon and spend 2 sorcery points to imbue it with magic for 1 minute. For the duration, the weapon is considered magical for the purpose of overcoming Immunity and Resistance to nonmagical attacks.</p><p>For each additional 2 sorcery points you spend, you can give the weapon a +1 bonus to Attack Rolls and damage rolls (up to +3), stacking with existing bonuses on the weapon, up to a maximum of +5 for the Attack Roll bonus.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"object"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"touch"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orbs-hand-gray.webp","_id":"sb6fc3232fe26134","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Living Bomb","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The damage dealt by your Heart of Fire feature increases to three times your Proficiency.</p><p>When a creature affected by your Heart of Fire feature that you can see is reduced to 0 hit points by fire damage, you can use your Reaction to make it explode violently. Any creature in a 20 feet radius around the target has to make a DEX Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, a creature takes fire damage equal to a number of d6 x your Proficiency and is then set aflame as per your Heart of Fire feature. On a success, it takes half as much damage and isn't set aflame.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb7420efd501057d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Magical Cunning feature, you regain all your expended Pact Magic spell slots and the use of your 6th and 7th level Mystic Arcanum spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/orb-ball-purple.webp","_id":"sb7b9aca50007ead","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Favored Enemy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have significant experience studying, tracking, hunting, and even talking to a certain type of enemy commonly encountered in the wilds.</p><p>Choose a creature type. You gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls with weapon attacks or ranger spells that use a weapon or piece of ammunition as a material component against the chosen type.</p><p>Additionally, you have Advantage on Wisdom and Intelligence checks that pertain to your favored enemies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/dragon-breath-purple.webp","_id":"sb7cdfd6efa61e76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Witchcraft","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your knowledge of your craft deepens. You learn two additional Witchcraft options. Additionally, you can select two Witchcraft options you know, which improve as described below:</p><p><strong>Amelioration.</strong> You can also use this feature on targets with the Confused, Dazed, Exhausted, Incapacitated, Paralyzed, and Stunned conditions.</p><p><strong>Cackle.</strong> You affect all creatures of your choice that can hear you within 60 feet.</p><p><strong>Evil Eye.</strong> You can use this feature as an Action or Bonus Action, but only once per turn.</p><p><strong>Familiar Focus.</strong> As an Action, you can switch positions with your bonded familiar if you can see it.</p><p><strong>Kettle Chant.</strong> The bonus to the listed crafting checks is now equal to your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Mind Fog.</strong> If the target fails the Concentration Saving Throw, it takes psychic damage equal to half your Witch level + your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p><strong>Minor Prophecy.</strong> You gain 1 additional use of this feature. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Witch Spittle.</strong> The healing from this feature is doubled.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb7d8ff11bc29718","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Illusory Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature hits you with an Attack Roll, you can take a Reaction to interpose an illusory duplicate of yourself between the attacker and yourself. The attack automatically misses you, then the illusion dissipates.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 2+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb7e1eae71547238","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kiss of the Spider Queen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the Spider Queen's malevolence into a deadly kiss. As an Action, you touch a creature within your reach. The target takes 12d10 poison or psychic damage (your choice), or half as much on a successful Constitution save. A creature Charmed by you has Disadvantage on its Saving Throw. After you use this ability, you cannot cast it again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb84959312504d5f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Knightly Vigilance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can't be Surprised while you are conscious. Additionally, you add your Wisdom modifier to your Initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb85b757b03679ae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Symbiotic Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws and Initiative rolls.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb8b9f9856fa7e16","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vengeful Ancestors","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ancestral spirits grow powerful enough to retaliate. When you use your Spirit Shield to reduce the damage of an attack, the attacker takes an amount of force damage equal to the damage that your Spirit Shield prevents.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/silhouette-evil-horned-giant.webp","_id":"sb8d01b77433bc10","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elder Champion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can imbue your Aura of Protection with primal power, granting the benefits below for 1 minute or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Diminish Defiance.</strong> Enemies in the aura have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against your spells and Channel Divinity options.</li><li><strong>Regeneration.</strong> At the start of each of your turns, you regain 10 Hit Points.</li><li><strong>Swift Spells.</strong> Whenever you cast a spell that has a casting time of an Action, you can cast it using a Bonus Action instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb8ef313a524a6fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict fire damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sb90bff34baa2caf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vivisectionist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach an Artificer level specified in the Vivisectionist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Vivisectionist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3</td><td>False Life, Shocking Grasp, Witch Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Envenom, Enhance Ability</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Animate Dead, Call Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Blight, Death Ward</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Antilife Shell, Raise Dead</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba2c9843fed780b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grave Touched","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your patron's powers have a profound effect on your body and magic, granting you the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Arcane Necrosis.</strong> Whenever you cast a spell or hit a creature with an attack roll and deal Necrotic damage, the damage dealt ignores Resistance to Necrotic damage.</li><li>Additionally, once per turn when you cast a spell that deals damage while using your Form of Dread, you can change that spell's damage type to Necrotic.</li><li><strong>Undead Endurance.</strong> You don't gain Exhaustion levels from dehydration, malnutrition, or suffocation. In addition, you don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba35cd83cf60756","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Manifest Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can conjure forth the mind of your Awakened Spellbook. As a Bonus Action while the book is on your person, you can cause the mind to manifest as a Tiny spectral object, hovering in an unoccupied space of your choice within 60 feet of you. The spectral mind is intangible and doesn't occupy its space, and it sheds dim light in a 10-foot radius. It looks like a ghostly tome, a cascade of text, or a scholar from the past (your choice).</p><p>While manifested, the spectral mind can hear and see, and it has darkvision with a range of 60 feet. The mind can telepathically share with you what it sees and hears (no action required).</p><p>Whenever you use a spell scroll on your turn, you can cast it as if you were in the spectral mind's space, instead of your own, using its senses. To do so, you must have placed the scroll in your awakened spellbook.</p><p>The spectral mind stops manifesting if it is ever more than 300 feet away from you, if someone casts Dispel Magic on it, if the Awakened Spellbook is destroyed, if you die, or if you dismiss the spectral mind as a Bonus Action.</p><p>Once you conjure the mind, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of any level to conjure it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba757e87574d4d8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ambush Master","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You excel at leading ambushes and acting first in a fight.</p><p>You are proficient in Initiative. In addition, the first creature you hit during the first round of a combat becomes easier for you and others to strike; Attack Rolls against that target have Advantage until the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sba873906466eda8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tenebrous Trinity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Bestow Curse, its range increases to 120 feet and you can choose up to three targets instead of one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbab6387161f0e10","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tongue of the Sun and Moon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to touch the ki of other minds so that you understand all spoken languages. Moreover, any creature that can understand a language can understand what you say.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/day-night-sunset-sunrise.webp","_id":"sbaca8edae4137b7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Pyrokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Control Flames cantrip.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbae9446d7469e26","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The tentacles slam into your foes. Pick up to 5 creatures that you can see within 30 ft. of the portal. Those creatures must make Dexterity Saving Throws against your Warlock spell save DC. Creatures that fail their Saving Throws take 10d6 bludgeoning damage and are Restrained for 1 minute. Creatures that succeed take half the bludgeoning damage and are not Restrained. On its turn, a Restrained creature can use its action to attempt Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your Warlock spell save DC to end its Restrained condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb1e74ad3490dc7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211673,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your scholarly efforts bear fruit. While studying magic, you also specialized in an academic field of study. Choose one of the following skills: Arcana, History, Investigation, Medicine, Nature, or Religion. Your gain Proficiency in the chosen skill. If you are already proficient in the skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/books/book-embossed-spiral-purple-white.webp","_id":"sbb6f987ee930d3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mystic Frenzy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take the Attack action, you can cast one of your cantrips in place of one of the attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb75539a2ecab6c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sword and Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Sword Mage Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Compelled Duel, Wrathful Smite, Branding Smite, Magic Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Blinding Smite, Elemental Weapon</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Staggering Smite, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Banishing Smite, Steel Wind Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbb87b98f2d67beb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Detect Portal","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to magically sense the presence of a planar portal. As an Action, you detect the distance and direction to the closest planar portal within 1 mile of you.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>See the \"Planar Travel\" section in chapter 2 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for examples of planar portals.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbbd3901c1d5cef7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Seasonal Avatar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The radius of your Awakened Season increases to 60 feet. Additionally, you have the following spell prepared based on your chosen season. You can cast this spell once without expending a spell slot. You cannot do so again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Spring.</strong> Power Word Fortify.</p><p><strong>Summer.</strong> Sunburst.</p><p><strong>Autumn.</strong> Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting.</p><p><strong>Winter.</strong> Polar Ray.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbc2def1f2c20213","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you reach a Sorcerer level specified in the Arcane Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Arcane Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Detect Magic, Magic Missile, Misty Step, Nystul's Magic Aura</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Counterspell, Dispel Magic</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Arcane Eye, Spell Turning</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Circle of Power, Spell Mantle</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbcaecc7b7d30512","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell-Storing Item","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch one Simple or Martial weapon or one item that you can use as a Spellcasting Focus, and you store a spell in it, choosing a level 1, 2, or 3 Artificer spell that has a casting time of an action and doesn't require a Material component that is consumed by the spell (you needn't have the spell prepared).</p><p>While holding the object, a creature can take a Magic action to produce the spell's effect from it, using your spellcasting ability modifier. If the spell requires Concentration, the creature must concentrate. Once a creature has used the object to produce the spell's effect, the object can't be used this way again until the start of the creature's next turn.</p><p>The spell stays in the object until it's been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum of twice) or until you use this feature again to store a spell in an object.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/beam-impact-purple.webp","_id":"sbd0bcf4c7837fbd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortified Position","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're a master at forming well-defended emplacements using Eldritch Cannon:</p><ul><li>You and your allies have half cover while within 10 feet of a cannon you create with Eldritch Cannon, as a result of a shimmering field of magical protection that the cannon emits.</li><li>You can now have two cannons at the same time. You can create two with the same action (but not the same spell slot), and you can activate both of them with the same Bonus Action. You determine whether the cannons are identical to each other or different. You can't create a third cannon while you have two.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/artillery/cannon-banded.webp","_id":"sbd447b7bfa88290","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Prodigious Memory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The number of spells you can prepare is increased by half your wizard level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbd4994952140a95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Living Legend","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can empower yourself with the legends—whether true or exaggerated—of your great deeds. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>If your total for a Strength, Dexterity, or Charisma check is less than your Charisma score, you can use that score in place of the total.</li><li>Your weapon attacks deal additional damage equal to half your Paladin level. The damage type is the same as the weapon's.</li><li>When you're not Incapacitated and subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail. You can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbd505465ca05d2f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Brutal Strike (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The extra damage of your Brutal Strike increases to 2d10. In addition, you can use two different Brutal Strike effects whenever you use your Brutal Strike feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"sbd6ba36dc81eb82","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Protection","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you or a friendly creature within 10 feet of you must make a Saving Throw, the creature gains a bonus to the Saving Throw equal to your Charisma modifier (with a minimum bonus of +1). You must be conscious to grant this bonus.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-tornado-wall-blue.webp","_id":"sbd95984cf49c04d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have dedicated yourself to one of the following sacred roles of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Protector.</strong> Trained for battle, you gain Proficiency with Martial weapons and training with Heavy armor.</li><li><strong>Thaumaturge.</strong> You know one extra cantrip from the Cleric spell list. In addition, your mystical connection to the divine gives you a bonus to your Intelligence (Arcana or Religion) checks. The bonus equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1).</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/holy/barrier-shield-winged-cross.webp","_id":"sbdbf292578b65bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infiltration Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can unfailingly create false identities for yourself. You must spend seven days and 25 gp to establish the history, profession, and affiliations for an identity. You can't establish an identity that belongs to someone else. For example, you might acquire appropriate clothing, letters of introduction, and official-looking certification to establish yourself as a member of a trading house from a remote city so you can insinuate yourself into the company of other wealthy merchants.</p><p>Thereafter, if you adopt the new identity as a disguise, other creatures believe you to be that person until given an obvious reason not to.</p><p>You also gain the ability to unerringly mimic another person's speech, writing, and behavior. You must spend at least three hours studying these three components of the person's behavior, listening to speech, examining handwriting, and observing mannerism.</p><p>Your ruse is indiscernible to the casual observer. If a wary creature suspects something is amiss, you have Advantage on any Charisma (Deception) check you make to avoid detection.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbde7aa4cce77bf6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Searing Flesh","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, as a Bonus Action, you can superheat your body to extreme temperatures, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While the effect is active and you aren't wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier and any creature that touches you or hits you with a melee attack from within 10 feet of you takes fire damage equal to your Charisma modifier.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe0559579edb592","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Water Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your being is altered by the power of the sea. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>You no longer need to eat, drink, or sleep.</li><li>A critical hit against you becomes a normal hit.</li><li>You have Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe07442a8b14047","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gale Stride","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use Second Wind and Tactical Shift, you can move up to your full Speed instead. If you choose to not receive healing from Second Wind, you can activate it without a Bonus Action. You can do so only once on your turn.</p><p>Additionally, this movement allows you to move through the spaces of hostile creatures, treating them as 3.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe09305f74a200e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wildfire","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to fire damage and when you cast a spell that deals fire damage, you can choose any creature you can see within 120 ft of you that is currently affected by your Heart of Fire feature as the point of origin. If you do so, the effect of Heart of Fire ends on it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe30978618814d7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Savage Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 3 and increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level in this class.</p><p>Additionally, allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you, take reduced damage from bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage while you are not Incapacitated. The reduction is equal to your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe317935a13a52d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Be like Water","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to embody the evershifting, ungraspable nature of your element.</p><p>When you are Grappled or Restrained on your turn, you can spend 5 feet of movement to no longer be Grappled or Restrained. You also gain blindsight in a 30 feet radius.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe36e622a274ced","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When your bonded familiar hits a creature you can see within 60 feet of you with a weapon attack on its turn, you can use your Reaction to expend a Spell Slot of 1st level or higher. The target creature takes damage of the type gained through your Familiar Bonus Damage equal to 1d8 per level of the spell slot.</p><p>Additionally, it has to make a Constitution Saving Throw or suffer one of the following effects until the end of your bonded familiar's next turn, based on your chosen Wild Domain:</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Familiar Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Wild Domain</th><th scope=\"col\">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dunes</td><td>Target is Blinded.</td></tr><tr><td>Marshes</td><td>Attack Rolls against the target have Advantage and any healing it receives is halved.</td></tr><tr><td>Peaks</td><td>Target is Dazed.</td></tr><tr><td>Tundras</td><td>Target is Restrained.</td></tr><tr><td>Waves</td><td>Target is knocked Prone and moved to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of its original position.</td></tr><tr><td>Wealds</td><td>Attack Rolls against the target have Advantage. You or any of your allies regain hit points equal to your Witch level + your spellcasting ability modifier if they reduce the target to 0 hit points.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe5d05552d01d61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fate's Right Hand","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can channel the Raven Mother's power to curse a creature. You can cast Pale Knight's Portentous Premonition. After you cast the spell with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe6836c7a34559b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fire's Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to direct your inner fire to lash out at attackers. When you are hit by a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to make the attacker take fire damage equal to your kineticist level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbe7ee41698bae45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dread Lord","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can empower yourself with dark forces and exude a corrupting presence. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 10 minutes:</p><ul><li>You emanate an aura of magical gloom within 30 ft. This counts as dim light and sunlight cannot illuminate this area.</li><li>Enemy creatures have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against any of your features and spells, as well as those of undead and fiends while within the gloom.</li><li>When an enemy creature starts its turn in the gloom, it takes 10 necrotic damage. This damage is doubled if the creature is good-aligned. </li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbeb08dc48f37b29","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Water Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict cold or bludgeoning damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbec49d82e33f262","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Holy Nimbus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can imbue your Aura of Protection with holy power, granting the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Holy Ward.</strong> You and allies in the aura have Advantage on any Saving Throw they are forced to make by a Fiend or an Undead.</li><li><strong>Radiant Damage.</strong> Whenever an enemy starts its turn in the aura, that creature takes Radiant damage equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. This damage is doubled against Fiends and Undead.</li><li><strong>Sunlight.</strong> The aura is filled with Bright Light that is sunlight.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-blue-purple.webp","_id":"sbecb9091927bcec","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Right Tool for the Job","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to produce exactly the tool you need: with thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand, you can magically create one set of artisan's tools in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. This creation requires 1 hour of uninterrupted work, which can coincide with a Short or a Long Rest. Though the product of magic, the tools are nonmagical, and they vanish when you use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/trades/construction-carpentry-hammer.webp","_id":"sbee2a6e3c681f52","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stroke of Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have a marvelous knack for succeeding when you need to. If you fail a D20 Test, you can turn the roll into a 20.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"sbef2c4f2fb640ab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use yourself as a Spellcasting Focus and you can ignore verbal components for your wizard spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sbeff51a941caff0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hardened Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against being Charmed and Frightened, and you have a bonus to Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma Saving Throws equal to your Hemocraft modifier (minimum of +1).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"sbf4faf374f00a36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadowdance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to step from one shadow into another. When you use your Cunning Action while in dim light or darkness, you can teleport up to 60 feet to a different unoccupied space you can see that is also in dim light or darkness. You can apply the effects of your Cunning Action before or after you teleport. This does not count as movement for the purpose of Cunning Action: Aim.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc009eda6a45e561","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Blades","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can manifest your psionic power as shimmering blades of psychic energy. Whenever you make a weapon attack, you can manifest a psychic blade from your free hand and make the attack with that blade. This magic blade is a simple melee weapon with the finesse and thrown properties. It has a normal range of 60 feet and no long range, and on a hit, it deals psychic damage equal to your Psionic Energy Die plus the ability modifier you used for the Attack Roll. The blade vanishes immediately after it hits or misses its target, and it leaves no mark on its target if it deals damage.</p><p>After you attack with the blade, you can make a melee or ranged weapon attack with a second psychic blade as a Bonus Action on the same turn, provided your other hand is free to create it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0ade5ffeaaf685","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211658,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Light as Air","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to use your Reaction when you fall to reduce any falling damage you take by an amount equal to five times your kineticist level.</p><p>Additionally, your standing and running jumps use Charisma instead of Strength to determine the distance you cover.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0f94ce605e3243","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Noble Scion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you gain the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required).</p><ul><li><strong>Flight.</strong> You have a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover.</li><li><strong>Greater Aura of Elemental Shielding.</strong> Your Aura of Elemental Shielding now confers Immunity to the chosen element instead of Resistance.</li><li><strong>Minor Wish.</strong> As an Action, you can entreat your genie patron for the effect of one spell that is 5th level or lower and has a casting time of 1 action. The spell can be from any class's spell list, and you don't need to meet the requirements in that spell, including costly components; the spell simply takes effect as part of this Action. Once you have done so, you cannot use this feature again for this use of Noble Scion.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc0fb5726a65ff9e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fortified Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your half your Witch Level + spellcasting ability modifier to Saving Throws to maintain Concentration. This bonus is doubled for your Coven spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc11fc6019f711fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divinity: Divine Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can open your awareness to detect Celestials, Fiends, and Undead. For the next 10 minutes or until you have the Incapacitated condition, you know the location of any creature of those types within 60 feet of yourself, and you know its creature type. Within the same radius, you also detect the presence of any place or object that has been consecrated or desecrated, as with the Hallow spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/eyes/human-single-blue.webp","_id":"sc15b2e29cb546ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Profane Recuperation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you spend a Hit Die to regain hit points, you add your Hemocraft modifier to the roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc17b2c5636a6046","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Siphon Shadows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to necrotic damage. When you are subject to necrotic damage from any source except cantrips, you are instead healed for half the amount of the damage you would have taken.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/hand-claw-glow-orange.webp","_id":"sc1938e54b349dea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Devotion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you can't be Charmed while you are conscious.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"sc197b8fb94ec46a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Instinctive Charm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an Attack Roll against you, you can use your Reaction to divert the attack, provided that another creature is within the attack's range. The attacker must make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your wizard spell save DC. On a failed save, the attacker must target the creature that is closest to it, not including you or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target. On a successful save, you can't use this feature on the attacker again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>You must choose to use this feature before knowing whether the attack hits or misses. Creatures that can't be Charmed are Immune to this effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc1fec2d969be726","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metakinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You further evolve your ability to twist your chosen elements to your needs. You gain access to three of the following Metakinesis options of your choice, all of which modify your kinetic shape.</p><p>You can only use one Metakinesis option with your kinetic shape, unless otherwise noted.</p><h5>Careful Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that forces other creatures to make a Saving Throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the shape's full force. To do so, you spend 1 kinesis point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its Saving Throws against the blast and takes no damage if it would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Distant Kinesis</h5><p>When you use a kinetic shape, you can spend 1 kinesis point to double its range.</p><h5>Empowered Kinesis</h5><p>When you roll damage for your kinetic shape, you can spend 1 kinesis point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p><p>You can use Empowered Kinesis even if you have already used a different Metakinesis option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Extended Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that makes it last more than 1 round, you can spend 1 kinesis point to double its duration, to a maximum duration of 24 hours.</p><h5>Heightened Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that forces a creature to make a Saving Throw to resist its effects, you can spend 2 kinesis points to give one target of the shape Disadvantage on all its Saving Throws made against the effect.</p><h5>Twinned Kinesis</h5><p>When you use your kinetic shape with an infusion that doesn't have a range of self and is incapable of targeting more than one creature, you can spend 3 kinesis points to have it target a second creature within range as well.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-beam-pink.webp","_id":"sc1ff24bde46d74b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Outmaneuver","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>After initiative has been rolled, but before the first turn of combat, you and all allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you can move up to your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks. This feature has no effect if you're incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc219265bba93e54","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Concerted Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your allies form a more effective fighting force. When you use the attack action on your turn, an ally of your choice within 60 feet that can see or hear you can use its Reaction to make a weapon attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-strike-triple-blue.webp","_id":"sc22900edf9d8cbc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mixed Heritage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose the single strongest influence of your parentage from the following:</p><p>Human: You gain Proficiency in one skill</p><p>High Elf: You gain the Cantrip racial trait.</p><p>Wood Elf: You gain the Mask of the Wild racial and Fleet of foot racial traits.</p><p>Dark Elf: Your gain the Dark Elf Spellcasting trait, excluding Healing Spirit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/group.webp","_id":"sc24af6e44516499","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Action Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can push yourself beyond your normal limits for a moment. On your turn, you can take one additional action.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use it again. Starting at 17th level, you can use it twice before a rest, but only once on the same turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.action-surge","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sc290e756fbc497a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Impel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to giant strength now allows you to hurl both allies and enemies on the battlefield. As a Bonus Action while raging, you can choose one Medium or smaller creature within your reach and move it to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Strength Saving Throw (DC equals 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) to avoid the effect.</p><p>If, at the end of this movement, the thrown creature isn't on a surface or liquid that can support it, the creature falls, taking damage as normal and landing Prone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc294de8173f5b81","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brute Force","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You're able to strike with your weapons with especially brutal force. Whenever you hit with a weapon that you're proficient with and deal damage, the weapon's damage increases by an amount based on your level in this class, as shown on the Brute Bonus Damage table. You can also add the same die to the roll if you make a Strength (Athletics) check.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Brute Bonus Damage</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Fighter Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Damage Increase</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>1d4</td></tr><tr><td>10th</td><td>1d6</td></tr><tr><td>16th</td><td>1d8</td></tr><tr><td>20th</td><td>1d10</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc2fd12902e6cc78","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indestructible Life","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You partake some of the true secrets of the Undying. On your turn, you can use a Bonus Action to regain hit points equal to half your maximum hit points. Additionally, if you put a severed body part of yours back in place when you use this feature, the part reattaches.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc333a084a474462","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamystic Arts","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to blend your mastery of body and mind with your mystic arts to modify your spells and Unarmed Attacks; you gain two Metamystic options of your choice from the list below. You use the chosen options to temporarily modify one spell you cast, with additional benefits to your Unarmed Attacks as described. To use an option, you must spend the number of Ki Points that it costs. You can use only one Metamystic option on a spell and subsequent Unarmed Attacks this turn.</p><p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest you can replace one metamystic art you know with another one. </p><h5>Distant Arts</h5><p>When you cast a spell on your turn that has a range of 30 feet or greater, you can spend 1 Ki point to also give that same range to your Unarmed Attacks this turn.</p><h5>Empowered Arts</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend a number of Ki points up to your Wisdom modifier to reroll a number of damage dice equal to the number of Ki points expended. You can then reroll the weapon damage die on a number of Unarmed Attacks you make this turn, up to the number of Ki points expended. You must use the new rolls.</p><h5>Swift Arts</h5><p>When you use your Flurry of Blows, you can spend 2 Ki points to cast one of your Sorcerer cantrips that has a cast time of an Action in place of one of the attacks.</p><h5>Twinned Arts</h5><p>When you cast a spell that targets only one creature and doesn't have a range of self, you can spend a number of Ki points equal to the spell's level to target a second creature in range with the same spell (1 Ki point if the spell is a cantrip). You can spend up to 4 additional Ki points. For each additiona Ki point expended, one of your Unarmed Attacks this turn can target a second creature within their reach, using the original attack and damage roll.</p><p>To be eligible, a spell must be incapable of targeting more than one creature at the spell's current level. For example, Magic Missile and Scorching Ray aren't eligible, but Ray of Frost and Chromatic Orb are.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc36648767c339fa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silvertongued","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Persuasion, Intimidation, and Deception skills.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/mouth-smile-deception-purple.webp","_id":"sc3e2d40cf72043e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fungal Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The fungal spores in your body alter you: you can't be Blinded, Deafened, Frightened, or Poisoned, and any critical hit against you counts as a normal hit instead, unless you're Incapacitated.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc3e3859c0b43950","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Watery Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to Fire and Acid damage.</p><p>You also gain the ability to defend yourself by momentarily assuming a watery form. As a Reaction when you are hit by an attack, you can reduce that damage by an amount equal to your sorcerer level plus your Charisma score, and then you can move up to 30 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks. You cannot use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, or you use 3 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc3e9b082c4566c9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Rapid Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to trade accuracy for swift strikes. If you take the Attack action on your turn and have Advantage on an Attack Roll against one of the targets, you can forgo the Advantage for that roll to make an additional weapon attack against that target, as part of the same action. You can do so no more than once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc40c719273ac2c4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Planar Warrior","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to draw on the energy of the multiverse to augment your attacks.</p><p>Once on your turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, all damage dealt by the attack becomes force damage, and the creature takes an extra 1d8 force damage from the attack. When you reach 11th level in this class, the extra damage increases to 2d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc442070609a7164","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Born to the Saddle","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery as a rider becomes apparent. You have Advantage on Saving Throws made to avoid falling off your mount. If you fall off your mount and descend no more than 10 feet, you can land on your feet if you're not Incapacitated.</p><p>Finally, mounting or dismounting a creature costs you only 5 feet of movement, rather than half your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc48ef4fbd73a144","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blaze of Glory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can delay death for an instant to perform a final heroic act.</p><p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points by an attacker you can see, even if you would be killed outright, you can use your Reaction to move up to your Speed toward the attacker and make one melee weapon attack against it, as long as the movement brings it within your reach. You make this attack with Advantage. If the attack hits, the creature takes an extra 5d10 fire damage and an extra 5d10 damage of the weapon's type. You then fall Unconscious and begin making death Saving Throws as normal, or you die if the damage you took would have killed you outright.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc4a96f7c584fd12","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Tinkering","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to invest a spark of magic into mundane objects. To use this ability, you must have thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand. You then touch a Tiny nonmagical object as an Action and give it one of the following magical properties of your choice:</p><ul><li>The object sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet.</li><li>Whenever tapped by a creature, the object emits a recorded message that can be heard up to 10 feet away. You utter the message when you bestow this property on the object, and the recording can be no more than 6 seconds long.</li><li>The object continuously emits your choice of an odor or a nonverbal sound (wind, waves, chirping, or the like). The chosen phenomenon is perceivable up to 10 feet away.</li><li>A static visual effect appears on one of the object's surfaces. This effect can be a picture, up to 25 words of text, lines and shapes, or a mixture of these elements, as you like.</li></ul><p>The chosen property lasts indefinitely. As an Action, you can touch the object and end the property early.</p><p>You can bestow magic on multiple objects, touching one object each time you use this feature, though a single object can only bear one property at a time. The maximum number of objects you can affect with this feature at one time is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one object). If you try to exceed your maximum, the oldest property immediately ends, and then the new property applies.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":"you must have thieves' tools or artisan's tools in hand"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"object"},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":"touch"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/runes-etched-steel-blade.webp","_id":"sc4ab9d21ff73fed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Inspiring Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your Leadership ability modifier to the number of hitpoints targets regain from your Inspiring Surge.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sc4afdcf80417163","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Cunning Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use up to two Cunning Strike effects when you deal Sneak Attack damage, paying the die cost for each effect.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":"when you deal sneak attack damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-dagger-blood-red.webp","_id":"sc53693eac3becf5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable (two uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Indomitable twice between Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"sc577d957cfc3779","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fast Hands","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you can do one of the following.</p><ul><li><strong>Sleight of Hand.</strong> Make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check to pick a lock or disarm a trap with Thieves' Tools or to pick a pocket.</li><li><strong>Use an Object.</strong> Take the Utilize action, or take the Magic action to use a magic item that requires that action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/theft-pickpocket-bribery-brown.webp","_id":"sc5f72bd02318981","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inspiring Surge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Action Surge feature, you can choose one creature within 60 feet of you that is allied with you. That creature can make one melee or ranged weapon attack with its Reaction, provided that it can see or hear you.</p><p>Starting at 18th level, you can choose two allies within 60 feet of you, rather than one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"sc63374d0b16f5d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Intimidating Presence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter a frenzy, you also adopt a menacing presence that frightens foes around you. Any hostile creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of you while you are in a frenzy or enters that area for the first time on a turn and can see or hear you, must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw (DC equal to 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be Frightened of you until the start of its next turn.</p><p>If a creature's Saving Throw is successful, it is Immune to your Intimidating Presence for the next 24 hours.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-iron-stomping-yellow.webp","_id":"sc696804b2082ddb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Stalker's Prowess","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You add your hemocraft modifier to Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc6f518b3b61cdbc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Uncanny Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your Reaction to halve the attack's damage against you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"sc6f677ce9ce653b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Malevolence","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Creatures that start their turn within 10 feet of you or enter it for the first time on a turn, take psychic damage equal to your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (your choice) and have Disadvantage on Saving Throws against the Frightened and Lacerated conditions while within the aura The aura is inactive while you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc7b3915b4c3ecda","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vanguard","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The number of uses of your Second Wind feature increases by two, and the number of uses for your Indomitable feature increases by one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-aura-energy.webp","_id":"sc7f2fe99a83a94e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Alchemist Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Alchemist Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Artificer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spell</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Healing Word, Ray of Sickness</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Flaming Sphere, Melf's Acid Arrow</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Corrosion, Mass Healing Word</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Death Ward, Vitriolic Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Cloudkill, Mass Cure Wounds</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/cog-shield-white-blue.webp","_id":"sc7f64e6fb24b2fc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Oceanic Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are now even more at home in the depths. You gain Resistance to cold damage. In addition, when you are fully submerged, any creature that is also fully submerged can understand your speech, and you can understand theirs.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc80e8359c75a3e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hex in the City","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Friends and Charm Person spells prepared. When you cast either spell, the target does not know that it was Charmed by you unless it directly observed you casting the spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc867d1e24c199f8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drunkard's Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always seem to get a lucky bounce at the right moment. When you make an Ability Check, an Attack Roll, or a Saving Throw and have Disadvantage on the roll, you can spend 2 ki points to cancel the Disadvantage for that roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8c40b0e68ed56f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aspect of the Wyrm","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of your draconic spirit now radiates from you, warding your allies or inspiring fear in your enemies. As a Bonus Action, you can create an aura of draconic power that radiates 10 feet from you for 1 minute. For the duration, you gain one of the following effects of your choice:</p><ul><li><strong>Frightful Presence.</strong> When you create this aura, and as a Bonus Action on subsequent turns, you can choose a creature within the aura. The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your ki save DC or become Frightened of you for 1 minute. The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a successful save.</li><li><strong>Resistance.</strong> Choose a damage type when you activate this aura: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. You and your allies within the aura have Resistance to that damage.</li></ul><p>Once you create this aura, you can't create it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend 3 ki points to create it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8da86c6dabc913","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Chaos","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell with a spell slot, you can create an effect of your choice from the Wild Magic Surge table, provided the effect casts a spell or restores all your expended Sorcery Points.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish 1d4 Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc8dc9866a501d71","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drakewarden Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the table below. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Drakewarden Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Cause Fear</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Dragon's Breath</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Fear</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Elemental Bane</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Summon Dragon</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Any of these spells can be cast as if you were in the space of your drake companion.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc9187a0353d8e8c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Hunter Order","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You commit to an order of blood hunters whose philosophy will guide you throughout your life: the Order of the Ghostslayer, the Order of the Lycan, the Order of the Mutant, or the Order of the Profane Soul, each of which is detailed at the end of the class description. Your choice grants you features at 7th level and again at 11th, 15th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc928f2354684678","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reliable Talent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you make an Ability Check that uses one of your skill or tool proficiencies, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/target-bullseye-arrow-glowing.webp","_id":"sc933f37d5439894","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Breaker","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you restore hit points to an ally with a spell of 1st level or higher, you can also end one spell of your choice on that creature. The level of the spell you end must be equal to or lower than the level of the spell slot you use to cast the healing spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sc9cc0e93f045028","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211622,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Harfolk Hardiness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take damage, you can choose to use your Reaction to shrug off the blow. Roll a d12 + your CON modifier. And substract the result from the damage taken. You can't use this feature again until you have finished a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you take damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d12 + @abilities.con.mod","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp","_id":"sc9f996923346e1c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Assassinate","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are at your deadliest when you get the drop on your enemies. You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against any creature that hasn't taken a turn in the combat yet. When you use your Sneak Attack against a creature on the first turn of combat that hasn't acted yet or that you are hidden, the number of d6s that you roll as part of your Sneak Attack's damage increases by an amount equal to your Proficiency.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sca073134d23daf9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Flexibility","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can grant your allies attacks as per the Concerted Strike class feature even when you use your action for something other than the attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/gaming/chess-knight-white.webp","_id":"sca08fc78d455291","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aspect of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a magical benefit based on the totem animal of your choice. You can choose the same animal you selected at 3rd level or a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sca34d90d09d62f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empower Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after a creature you can see within 30 feet of you casts a level 1+ spell, you can take a Reaction to absorb magical energy from the spell. When you do so, until the end of your next turn, the next time you hit with your Sneak Attack you deal extra Force damage. To determine the extra damage, roll a number of d6s equal to the spell's level, and add them together.</p><p>You can take this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scaa3ca81daa8043","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Riposte","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an attack miss with the Shield spell, reduce damage to 0 with your Arcane Deflection, or successfully prevent a spell with Counterspell, you can magically retaliate as part of the same Reaction against the originator of the attack or damage if you can see it and it is within 120 feet of you.</p><p>The target has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure it takes force damage equal to a number of D8s times your Proficiency.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also expend a level 2+ spell slot to regain a use of this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scb1549c221a097b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sacred Oath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You swear the oath that binds you as a paladin forever. Up to this time you have been in a preparatory stage, committed to the path but not yet sworn to it. Now you choose from the list of available oaths.</p><p>Your choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 15th, and 20th level. Those features include oath spells and the Channel Divinity feature.</p><p><strong>Oath Spells.</strong> Each oath has a list of associated spells. You gain access to these spells at the levels specified in the oath description. Once you gain access to an oath spell, you always have it prepared. Oath spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.</p><p>If you gain an oath spell that doesn't appear on the paladin spell list, the spell is nonetheless a paladin spell for you.</p><div><strong>Breaking Your Oath</strong><p>A paladin tries to hold to the highest standards of conduct, but even the most virtuous paladin is fallible. Sometimes the right path proves too demanding, sometimes a situation calls for the lesser of two evils, and sometimes the heat of emotion causes a paladin to transgress his or her oath.</p><p>A paladin who has broken a vow typically seeks absolution from a cleric who shares his or her faith or from another paladin of the same order. The paladin might spend an all-night vigil in prayer as a sign of penitence, or undertake a fast or similar act of self-denial. After a rite of confession and forgiveness, the paladin starts fresh.</p><p>If a paladin willfully violates his or her oath and shows no sign of repentance, the consequences can be more serious. At the DM's discretion, an impenitent paladin might be forced to abandon this class and adopt another, or perhaps to take the Oathbreaker paladin option that appears in the Dungeon Master's Guide.</p></div","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp","_id":"scb235d27fa36a14","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d12.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"scb48f3a01a334e9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Edge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of sword magic allows you to enhance your melee attacks. When you make a melee attack, the target takes extra force damage equal to half your sorcerer level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scb5154a8d722412","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Formshift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>By choice or circumstance, you possess the ability to shift into an animal-like form that outfits you with heightened senses, swiftness, and primal ferocity in battle. You shift forms as a Bonus Action. While shifted, you gain the following benefits as long as you aren't wearing armor heavier than light or a shield:</p><ul><li>You have Advantage on Perception checks.</li><li>Your Speed is doubled.</li><li>When you make a melee weapon attack with your natural weapons, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll. This bonus increases as you level.</li></ul><p>If you are able to cast spells, you can't cast them or concentrate on them while shifted.</p><p>Your Formshift lasts for an amount of hours equal to your shifter level. It ends early if you fall Unconscious or you are Incapacitated. You can also end your Formshift as a Bonus Action.</p><p>You can Formshift a number of times shown for your Shifter level in the Formshifts column of the Shifter Features table. You regain one expended use when you finish a Short Rest, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p>You choose whether your equipment falls to the ground in your space, merges into your shifted form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal, but the DM decides whether it is practical for your shifted form to wear a piece of equipment, based on your shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change size or shape to match the new form, and any equipment that your shifted form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge with it. Equipment that merges with your shifted form has no effect until you leave Formshift.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"@scale.shifter.formshifts","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/beast-horned-scaled-glowing-orange.webp","_id":"scba5372efaa0ccf","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"One with the Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You extend your ki into your kensei weapons, granting you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Magic Kensei Weapons.</strong> Your attacks with your kensei weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p><p><strong>Deft Riposte.</strong> When you spend Ki on your Deflect Attack feature, you can attack with a monk weapon you are currently wielding instead of forcing the target to make a Dexterity Saving Throw, provided the target is within your reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scbcc344230c7361","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Uncanny Metabolism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative, you can regain all expended Ki Points. When you do so, roll your Martial Arts die, and regain a number of Hit Points equal to your Monk level plus the number rolled.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you roll initiative"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.monk.martial-arts + @classes.monk.levels","healing"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"scbe9a26550d26e8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fool's Luck","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Jesters seem to have a knack for pulling themselves out of tight situations, transforming what looks like sure failure into an embarrassing but effective success.</p><p>You can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration after you fail an Ability Check, fail a Saving Throw, or miss with an Attack Roll. Roll a Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to your attack, Saving Throw, or Ability Check, using the new result in place of the failed one.</p><p>If using this ability grants you a success on the attack, Saving Throw, or Ability Check, note the number you rolled on the Bardic Inspiration die. The DM can then apply that result as a penalty to an attack or check you make, and you cannot use this ability again until you suffer this drawback. When the DM invokes this penalty, describe an embarrassing gaffe or mistake you make as part of the affected die roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scbf5cac0741719f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Profane Augmentation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can harvest body parts from slain creatures and graft them onto your companion to give it new capabilities. You use your Medicine in place of the usual skill for harvesting each creature type. However, the attempt only succeeds if you meet the DC for a pristine ingredient.</p><p>You can graft or remove body parts to your companion as part of completing a Short or Long Rest. The maximum number of grafted body parts is two and you cannot choose the same creature type more than once. You automatically preserve any body parts that aren't currently grafted, though you need a method of storing and carrying them to bring them with you.</p><p>Your companion gains the ability associated with each grafted body part as per the list below.</p><ul><li><strong>Aberration.</strong> Your companion's Intelligence is replaced with that of the aberration, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, it gains a new ability, which it can use in place of its slam attack: Psychic Rend: 60 ft range, Intelligence Saving Throw: DC equals your spell save DC. Failure: 1d6 + the aberration's proficiency + your companion's Intelligence modifier psychic damage.</li><li><strong>Beast.</strong> Your companion's Strength or Dexterity (your choice) is replaced with that of the beast, up to a maximum of 20, and your companion can use its Dexterity in place of its Strength for melee damage rolls with its slam. Additionally, your companion gains any special movement type of the harvested creature, equal to its own Speed.</li><li><strong>Construct.</strong> Your companion's AC is replaced with that of the harvested creature, up to a maximum of 20.</li><li><strong>Dragon.</strong> Your companion gains a breath weapon which it can use as an Action. The damage type and shape of the breath weapon is the same as that of the dragon. The size of the breath weapon is 30 feet if it is a cone and 5 x 60 feet if it is a line. The damage is equal to that of your companion's death burst feature + the Proficiency of the dragon.</li><li>Once has used its breath weapon, you have to roll a d6 at the start of each of your turns. On a roll of 5 or 6, it regains its use of this feature.</li><li><strong>Elemental.</strong> Your companion gains a damage Resistance based on the elemental's Immunity. If the elemental has multiple Immunities, you choose which one to use. Additionally, your companion deals bonus damage of the same type equal to the elemental's Proficiency when it hits with its slam attack.</li><li><strong>Fey.</strong> Your companion's alignment and its Charisma is replaced with that of the fey, up to a maximum of 20. Your companion also gains its own personality, based on that of the fey, and may act on its own when not currently ordered to do something.</li><li>Additionally, if your companion has to make a Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, it adds half the fey's Proficiency (rounded down). This augmentation is exclusive with those gained from fiends.</li><li><strong>Fiend.</strong> Your companion's alignment and two Ability Scores of your choice are replaced with those of the fiend. Your companion also gains its own personality, based on that of the fiend, and may act on its own when not currently ordered to do something.</li><li>Additionally, your companion regenerates hit points equal to the fiend's Proficiency at the start of each of its turn, unless it has taken radiant damage since its last turn. This augmentation is exclusive with those gained from fey.</li><li><strong>Giant.</strong> Your companion's Strength is replaced with that of the giant, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, your companion's size changes to Large and it has advantage on Strength checks and Strength Saving Throws. When your companion hits with its slam attack, it deals additional damage of the same type equal to the giant's Proficiency.</li><li><strong>Ooze.</strong> Your companion's Constitution is replaced with that of the ooze, up to a maximum of 20. Additionally, its current and maximum hit points increase by four times the ooze's Proficiency and it can spend 5 feet of its movement to remove the Grappled or Restrained condition from itself.</li><li><strong>Plant.</strong> Your companion's current and maximum hit points increase by double the plant's Proficiency. Additionally, the reach of its slam attack increases by 10 feet. Once per turn, a creature hit by your companion's slam attack has to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it is Grappled by your companion. Any creature that starts its turn Grappled in this manner, takes bludgeoning damage equal to the plant's Proficiency.</li><li><strong>Undead.</strong> As part of the Bonus Action used to command it, you can tell your companion to exude an aura of necrotic energy. When you do so, you can exempt a number of creatures equal to your Intelligence modifier from the effect. On subsequent turns, you can deactivate the aura the same way.</li><li>The size of the aura is 10 feet, but increases to 20 feet if the undead's CR was 10 or higher, and to 30 feet if its CR was 20 or higher.</li><li>Any creature that ends its turn in the aura or enters it for the first time on a turn, takes necrotic damage equal to the undead's proficiency.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scc79e398e9410cd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Scholar of the Beyond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Proficiency in the Arcana and Religion skills and both of you can use your spellcasting ability score in place of the usual ability score for these skills.</p><p>Additionally, you can cast Detect Evil and Good without expending a spell slot a number of times equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scca8feb1b2bb5de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Army of One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to summon an ever-increasing number of creatures to your side. When you cast a conjuration or necromancy spell to summon a creature, you can choose to ignore the Concentration limit on that spell. But if you do so, you reduce the spell's duration to 1 minute.</p><p>If you lose Concentration, you lose it on all spells you're concentrating on.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sccb549db636570e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sentinel at Death's Door","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your Reaction to change its hit points to an amount equal to your Cleric level.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you regain all expended uses on a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scd86be4778a1cda","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you fail a Saving Throw, you can add half your Fighter level (rounded down) to it, possibly turning it into a success.</p><p>You can use this feature twice between Long Rests starting at 13th level and three times between Long Rests starting at 17th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you fail a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"@scale.fighter.indomitable","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"floor(@classes.fighter.levels/2)","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"scda9c4e67d71089","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Creative Crescendo","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Performance of Creation feature, you can create more than one item at once. The number of items equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of two items). If you create an item that would exceed that number, you choose which of the previously created items disappears. Only one of these items can be of the maximum size you can create; the rest must be Small or Tiny.</p><p>You are no longer limited by gp value when creating items with Performance of Creation.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scdab811c28e1508","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Slayer's Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following Cunning Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Terrify (Cost: 2d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw, or it has the Frightened condition for 1 minute. The Frightened target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</li><li><strong>Torment (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or it becomes crippled with pain until the start of your next turn. For the duration, its Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on Ability Checks, Attack Rolls, and Constitution Saving Throws to maintain concentration.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce2e073c73cd76e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Far Wanderer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You no longer need to breathe, and you gain Resistance to fire damage and cold damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce3f41332ee6930","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Foreknowledge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you magically expand your mind to the possibilities of the future. For 1 hour, you have Advantage on D20 Tests. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of this feature by expending a level 7+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce52ab7280435bd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirit Ravage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Starting at 14th level, your mastery over blood magic transcends the mere physical. You ignore Immunity to the Lacerated condition and the blood requirement (both for the target creature and for material components) for class features and spells.</p><p>Additionally, any Lacerated condition caused by your spells cannot be removed by healing and heals you for half the damage dealt.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce84ce0b771a12f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Share Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell targeting yourself, you can also affect your Primal Companion beast with the spell if the beast is within 30 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sce9a82acc8539da","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fiendish Resilience","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose one damage type, other than Force, whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You have Resistance to that damage type until you choose a different one with this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/armor-stone-skin.webp","_id":"scf800dfe941666c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Kinetic Blade","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Bonus Action, you form the energy of your element into a weapon-like shape of your choice, which lasts until you are incapacitated or dismiss it as a Bonus Action. You cannot use this shape if you have already used your kinetic blast this turn.</p><p>As an Action, you can make a melee spell attack with this shape against a target of your choice within 5 ft of you, dealing your kinetic shape die + your CHA modifier + your Proficiency modifier damage of your chosen element's type.</p><p>Additionally, your ability to defend yourself with this shape grants you a +1 bonus to your AC while maintaining it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":5,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"msak","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.kineticist.kinetic-shape + @abilities.cha.mod + @attributes.prof",""]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-flanged-lightning.webp","_id":"scf8bd9d1c7b559a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 14)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"scfe462e6aae4955","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brutish Defiance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you drop to 0 Hit Points and don't die outright, you can change your Hit Points to a number equal to double your fighter level. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind (no action required) and add its healing to the total.</p><p>You can't use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd00777affcd11af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cloak of Shadows","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As a Magic action while entirely within Dim Light or Darkness, you can expend 3 Ki Points to shroud yourself with shadows for 1 minute, until you have the Incapacitated condition, or until you end your turn in Bright Light. While shrouded by these shadows, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Invisibility.</strong> You have the Invisible condition.</li><li><strong>Partially Incorporeal.</strong> You can move through occupied spaces as if they were 3. If you end your turn in such a space, you are shunted to the last unoccupied space you were in.</li><li><strong>Shadow Flurry.</strong> You can use your Flurry of Blows without expending any Ki Points. When you use your Improved Shadow Step, you can use Flurry of Blows as part of the same Bonus Action.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd0283b68c43ab6b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strange Metabolism","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your body begins to adapt to toxins and venoms, ignoring their corrupting effects. You gain Resistance to damage from poison and diseases. At the end of each of your turns, you can end one disease or poison affecting you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd05c25351b091f9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vanish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use the Hide action as a Bonus Action on your turn. Also, you can't be tracked by nonmagical means, unless you choose to leave a trail.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/perception/silhouette-stealth-shadow.webp","_id":"sd0b3a52cb0bf6b3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Abeyance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast a spell using a spell slot of 4th level or lower, you can condense the spell's magic into a mote. The spell is frozen in time at the moment of casting and held within a gray bead for 1 hour. This bead is a Tiny object with AC 15 and 1 hit point, and it is Immune to poison and psychic damage. When the duration ends, or if the bead is destroyed, it vanishes in a flash of light, and the spell is lost.</p><p>A creature holding the bead can use its action to release the spell within, whereupon the bead disappears. The spell uses your spell attack bonus and save DC, and the spell treats the creature who released it as the caster for all other purposes.</p><p>Once you create a bead with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd0bc86d643a61d3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Saint of the Currents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to poison and disease and you can walk on water as per the Water Walk spell.</p><p>Additionally, all your water-based spells and your Channel Divinity: Cleaning Current have their area of affect doubled and you can choose to exempt a number of creatures equal to your WIS modifier from their effects.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd10d997fdee9a7c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic-User's Nemesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to thwart someone else's magic. When you see a creature casting a spell or teleporting within 60 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to try to magically foil it. The creature must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC, or its spell or teleport fails and is wasted. If the target is also the quarry of your Slayer's Prey, then you subtract a d6 from its Saving Throw.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest, unless you spend a 3rd-level slot or higher to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd13710fcf40b32e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Inescapable End","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The cleric's ability to channel negative energy becomes more potent. Necrotic damage dealt by the character ignores Resistance to necrotic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd1fa0f3aa79e17d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Grand Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Eidolon becomes an absolutely monstrosity. A true thing of legend and terror. Your Eidolon's Strength or Dexterity (your choice) and Constitution increase by 4. And its maximum for those scores is now 24.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd1fa7f8a0e1a6a4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211669,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sudden Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you attack a creature that you are hidden from, you can make an additional attack as part of your attack action. On the first turn of combat, you can apply your Sneak Attack to both of these attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd20d12c16f7bf12","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Adder's Kiss","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the Blood Curse of the Adder's Kiss for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd22c89b91602910","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Heart of Winter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You master the cold element, to the point that you grow stronger as your foes succumb to the touch of ice and frost:</p><ul><li>You gain Immunity to cold damage.</li><li>At the start of every one of your turns, you gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature within 30 feet of you that is affected by your Winter's Touch class feature or your Bone-Chilling Cold Channel Divinity. If a creature is affected by both, you double the temporary hit points gained for that creature. These temporary hit points last for 1 hour and do not stack with temporary hit points applied in this manner on subsequent rounds.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd24290a89450eed","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Close-Quarters Shooting","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to handle yourself in close combat. Making a ranged Attack Roll while within 5 feet of an enemy doesn't impose Disadvantage on your roll.</p><p>In addition, if you hit a creature within 5 feet of you with a ranged attack on your turn, that creature can't take Reactions until the end of this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd24a15f196e692e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211636,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twilight Shroud","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The twilight that you summon offers a protective embrace: you and your allies have half cover while in the sphere created by your Twilight Sanctuary.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd24b3cb0fdb3d15","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Strongheart Toughness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-red-blue.webp","_id":"sd262d520edac090","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Devotion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your study of psionics begins to unleash your mind's potential. When you gain this feature, choose one of the following cantrips: friends, mage hand, or message. You learn that cantrip if you don't already know it, and it doesn't count against the number of wizard cantrips you know. While your psionic focus is on your person, you can cast the chosen cantrip as a Bonus Action, requiring no components, and with the modification listed below:</p><p><strong>Friends.</strong> When the spell ends, the target doesn't become hostile to you.</p><p><strong>Mage Hand.</strong> You can make the hand Invisible when you cast the spell, and controlling the spell is a Bonus Action for you.</p><p><strong>Message.</strong> You don't need to point toward the target or whisper your message out loud.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd272006aea906ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Seasons Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a season. At each indicated Witch level, add the corresponding listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Spring Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Goodberry, Healing Word, Healing Spirit, Lesser Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Mass Healing Word, Plant Growth</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Aura of Purity, Conjure Woodland Beings</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Greater Restoration, Raise Dead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Summer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Color Spray, Entangle, Heat Metal, Scorching Ray</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Fireball, Haste</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Aura of Life, Death Ward</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dawn, Flame Strike</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Autumn Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Witch Bolt, Death Armor, Warding Wind</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Call Lightning, Thunder Step</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Storm Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Enervation, Jallarzi's Storm of Radiance</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Winter Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Ice Knife, Rime's Binding Ice, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Glacial Spike, Sleet Storm</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Dream</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd2751636ff63bb1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spectral Blade Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can spend 6 ki points to and choose up to seven creatures you can see within 30 ft. Make a melee attack against each target. On a hit, a target takes 5d12 psychic damage and you can use one effect from your Psychic Slash feature against it (no additional ki required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd29d3d96db2b213","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211645,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a feline aspect, granting you physical traits such as the vertical pupils, sharp nails, and elongated canines.</p><p>You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</p><p>Additionally, once per turn when you hit a creature with your natural weapons, you can force the target to make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failure, the target is Lacerated. The DC for this is 8 + your Proficiency + your Strength or Dexterity modifier (your choice). The target can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Creatures who cannot bleed are Immune to this feature.</p><p>Once you reach level 10 in this class, any laceration inflicted with your natural weapons deals damage equal to thrice your Proficiency, rather than twice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd2fe41752b0b00e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enhanced Summons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The weapon attacks of any creature you summon with a conjuration spell count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd319d8e4c8cbb35","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Travel Along the Tree","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you activate your Rage and as a Bonus Action while your Rage is active, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p><p>In addition, once per Rage, you can increase the range of that teleport to 150 feet. When you do so, you can also bring up to six willing creatures who are within 10 feet of you. Each creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice within 10 feet of your destination space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd382b8698774052","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wings Unfurled","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Step of the Wind, you can unfurl spectral draconic wings from your back that vanish at the end of your turn. While the wings exist, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. While you have no uses available, you can spend 3 ki points to use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd3a4ae0b396cede","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Martial Supremacy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use feature type=WM, you may choose from any mastery rather than only the ones available for your weapon.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/maneuver-greatsword-yellow.webp","_id":"sd3a801153ab3497","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Finest Hour","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Leadership can temporarily inspire your companions to transcend their limits. On your turn, choose an ally within 60 feet that can see or hear you and isn't incapacitated. That ally gains an additional turn immediately after your current one.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have completed a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"ally"},"range":{"value":60,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-weapons-orange.webp","_id":"sd4110bda12da744","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Harmonious Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to weave the energies of all your chosen elements together seamlessly.</p><p>Your Elemental Defense subclass features are no longer exclusive and you can choose to activate any number of them with the same Bonus Action (dismissing them still requires no action on your part).</p><p>If your chosen elements grant you access to different formulas to calculate your AC, you must still decide which one to use when you activate your Elemental Defense.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/shield-barrier-flaming-pentagon-teal-purple.webp","_id":"sd413cf9dd341422","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mapping Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Illuminated Cartography.</strong> You can cast Faerie Fire without expending a spell slot, outlining the affected creatures as if in ink. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Portal Jump.</strong> On your turn, you can spend an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down) to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of yourself or within 5 feet of a creature that is within 30 feet of you and holding one of your Adventurer's Atlas maps. You can't use this benefit if your Speed is 0.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"on your turn, spend an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down)"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"sd448decd1f847bb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sneaky","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the stealth skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/humanoid-silhouette-dashing-blue.webp","_id":"sd47f9e3e2722536","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expertise (Level 6)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can choose two more of your proficiencies (in skills or with thieves' tools) to gain the benefit of Expertise.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/tech/cog-bronze.webp","_id":"sd49144ed2592ec0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211654,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death Dealer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Envenom (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or become Poisoned for 1 minute. It can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of every one of its turns, ending the effect on a success. You must have a Poisoner's Kit on your person to use this effect. Alternatively, you can apply a poison that you currently have on your person. If you do so, the save DC of the poison changes to your Cunning Strike save DC if it is normally lower.</li><li><strong>Silence (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or be unable to speak or produce sound with its voice until the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd514ece92f59aa3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Intrigue","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency with the disguise kit, the forgery kit. Additionally, you can use your Intelligence for Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Persuasion checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd51a4ac9fd984b5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Hardened Bark.</strong> When you take bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, that damage is reduced by an amount equal to half your Shifter level. This reduction applies before all other calculations.</li><li><strong>Dryadic Bond.</strong> You gain a darkvision range of 60 feet. If you already possess darkvision, add 60 ft to its range.</li><li>Additionally, you can form a ranged weapon from plant material as a Bonus Action. As part of an attack, you can automatically form ammunition for this weapon if it requires it. The ammunition disappears are hitting or missing. The weapon remains while it is within 100 feet of you and otherwise disappears. This weapon counts as a natural weapon for you and has a range of 90/360 feet.</li><li><strong>Defensive Spores.</strong> When a creature within 10 feet of you hits or misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to force it to make a Constitution Saving Throw against your Spell Save DC. On a failure, the target is Poisoned for 1 minute. At the end of each of its turns, the target can repeat the Saving Throw, ending the effect on a success.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd567309f12e3613","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The might of the elements flows through you. You gain one of the following options of your choice:</p><p><strong>Potent Spellcasting.</strong> You add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any Druid cantrip.</p><p><strong>Primal Strike.</strong> Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an Attack Roll using a weapon or a natural weapon of your Wild Shape, you can cause the target to take an additional 1d8 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-glow-spiral-teal.webp","_id":"sd580de50ffb3738","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Athlete","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in the Athletics skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage-orange.webp","_id":"sd5a791b64faf80a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Apex Predator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your experience and skill allow you to hunt and fight any creature as effectively as your chosen foes, given a little time to prepare. When you finish a Long Rest, you can exchange any of your chosen favorite enemies and replace them with a different one.</p><p>Additionally, your critical range against your favorite enemies increases by 1 and if you land a critical hit with a weapon attack, you add your ranger level to the damage roll.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-beast-eyes-green.webp","_id":"sd63bb241b7b7ff7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Keeper of Souls","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can seize a trace of vitality from a parting soul and use it to heal the living. When an enemy you can see dies within 60 feet of you, you or one creature of your choice that is within 60 feet of you regains hit points equal to three times your Cleric level. You can use this feature only if you aren't Incapacitated. Once you use it, you can't do so again until the start of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6786202376aba0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have learned to regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. Once per Long Rest when you finish a Short Rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.</p><p>For example, if you're a 4th-level wizard, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots.</p><p>You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/earth/explosion-lava-stone-green.webp","_id":"sd678d7e6ab30dc1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Souleater","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to siphon the life energy from your fallen prey. You gain the Blood Curse of the Soul Eater for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd68ff26d038da51","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211621,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Resilient Survivor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a bonus to your Constitution Saving Throws equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd69580eea43195e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While using Wild Shape, you can cast spells in Beast form, except for any spell that has a Material component with a cost specified or that consumes its Material component.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"sd6a25e09b703919","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Channel Divine Energy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to harness divine energy to heal your allies or harm your foes. You have a pool of d6s equal to your wizard level. If you use a feature that uses these dice, the number of dice you expend can be no larger than half your wizard level (rounded down). You regain all expended dice when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Heal.</strong> As an Action, expend a number of d6s from your pool and roll them. Choose creatures within 30 feet of you that you can see. Each target is healed by an amount of equal to the total of the roll.</p><p><strong>Harm.</strong> As an Action, expend a number of d6s from your pool and roll them. Choose creatures within 30 feet of you that you can see. Each target has to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it takes an amount of damage of a type you choose when you gain this feature (cold, fire, lightning, necrotic, or radiant) equal to the total of the roll. On a success, it takes half as much damage. If the target is an undead or a fiend, it has Disadvantage on the Saving Throw, and the feature deals maximum damage to it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6bf697601cd9c2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d10s. They turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6d99ae57040a4b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Gaze","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and your bonded familiar gain Truesight to a distance of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd6dc2b8f65606d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211678,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ecclesitheurgy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two cantrips and two spells from the cleric spell list. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Wizard table. Whenever you gain a wizard level after this one, you can replace one of the wizard spells you add to your spellbook with a spell from the cleric spell list. Any of the spells gained in this manner count as wizard spells for you.</p><p>Additionally, you can copy cleric spells into your spellbook from scrolls or the spellbooks of other theurgists. If you do so, they count as wizard spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd71a8bac5d901d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extensive Study","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell from the wizard spell list. The spell must fulfill all the usual criteria for learning a wizard spell of 1st level or higher. You learn an additional spell in this manner at the following levels in this class: 5th, 9th, 13th, and 17th.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd722404f3de776e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211682,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Avatar of Strength","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You count as one size larger for the purpose of grappling, shoving, and carrying. Additionally, when you make a Strength check, Strength Saving Throw, or Constitution Saving Throw, you add your Wisdom modifier to it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd74bdf5108f29a8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Form of the Phoenix","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You finally master the spark of fire that dances within you. When you activate your Mantle of Flame feature, you can choose to empower its effects:</p><ul><li>You have a Fly Speed of 40 feet and can hover.</li><li>You have Resistance to all damage.</li><li>If you use your Phoenix Spark, that feature deals an extra 20 fire damage to each creature.</li></ul><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you spend 7 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd771987a04cb443","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Sneak Attack","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you spend a Spell Slot to cast a spell of 1st level or higher that requires a spell attack roll, you can use your Sneak Attack on it, adhering to all other conditions as usual. If you do so, the damage die of your Sneak Attack increases to a d8 and its damage type to that of the spell.</p><p>Additionally, the cost of any Cunning Strike you use with such a spell is reduced by a number of dice equal to half the spell's level (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd788f9dab708ad5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Versatile Trickster","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you use your Cunning Strike, you can instead choose a creature other than the original target of your attack that you can see within 5 ft of your mage hand.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd79278ed63c08c8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unerring Accuracy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of weapons grants you extraordinary accuracy. If you miss with an Attack Roll using a monk weapon on your turn, you can reroll it and take the second result. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd7b6bbfd7c3f55e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guardian Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Primeval Guardian Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, and it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Primeval Guardian Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ranger Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Entangle</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Enhance Ability</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Conjure Animals</td></tr><tr><td>13th</td><td>Giant Insect</td></tr><tr><td>17th</td><td>Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd81a1a74fadf95c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211652,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Curse Specialist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Bestow Curse spell prepared and it does not count against your Concentration limit, though the initial instance of the spell ends if you cast it again. If you fail a Concentration Saving Throw and you are currently concentrating on more than one spell, you lose concentration on both spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd81fad7120b8ccb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 12)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd864850e0c3cf4e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflect Energy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Wou can now use your Deflect Attacks feature against attacks that deal any damage type, not just Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/defensive/barrier-shield-dome-deflect-blue.webp","_id":"sd8c6f97491acfc4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master of Nature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells from the Druid spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd8ceba98226ac3b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mage Hand Legerdemain","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Mage Hand, you can cast it as a Bonus Action, and you can make the spectral hand Invisible. You can control the hand as a Bonus Action, and through it, you can make Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd8d1a585c320b24","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ability Score Improvement (Level 19)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.</p><p>If your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feat.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd8d3f00672b6a11","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Defense: Shroud of Water","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you can surround yourself with a shroud of water, ice, or both that protects you from harm, which lasts until you dismiss the effect (no action required).</p><p>While this effect is active and you are not wearing any armor or shield, your AC equals 12 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier.</p><p>This effect is exclusive with Elemental Defense class features from other Elemental Schools.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd8eb66f0f141334","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211639,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Curse of the Exorcist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You hone your hemocraft to tear corruption from the minds and bodies of your allies—and to punish those responsible for it. You gain the Blood Curse of the Exorcist for your Blood Maledict feature. This doesn't count against your number of blood curses known.</p><p>Additionally, you gain an additional use of your Blood Maledict feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":1,"width":null,"units":"","type":"creature"},"range":{"value":30,"long":null,"units":"ft"},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["3d6","psychic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"wis","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/fear-fright-monster-grin-red-orange.webp","_id":"sd908eb96310f716","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable (three uses)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use Indomitable three times between Long Rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"sd91ff0fddc63ac6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Advanced Artifice","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Magic Item Savant.</strong> You can now attune to up to five magic items at once.</p><p><strong>Refreshed Genius.</strong> When you finish a Short Rest, you regain one expended use of your Flash of Genius feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-hands-humanoid-yellow.webp","_id":"sd921a8233d96715","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Litany of Purgation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature is affected by your Inspiring Surge, it can immediately repeat a Saving Throw against one on-going effect on it that normally allows for repeated Saving Throws at the end of its turn. If it spends an additional hit die, it can make this Saving Throw with Advantage. The target does not regain additional hitpoints from spending this additional hit die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sd930e44ec9ae841","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Secrets","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned secrets from various magical traditions. Whenever you reach a Bard level (including this level) and the Prepared Spells number in the Bard Features table increases, you can choose any of your new prepared spells from the Bard, Cleric, Druid, and Wizard spell lists, and the chosen spells count as Bard spells for you (see a class's section for its spell list). In addition, whenever you replace a spell prepared for this class, you can replace it with a spell from those lists.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/documents/document-torn-diagram-tan.webp","_id":"sd9da1e208e5d966","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Green Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You adopt a plantlike aspect, granting you physical traits such as floral skin color, twiglike fingers, and leafs or flowers sprouting from your hair.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda1bbf55bf4ed79","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Moonlight Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can magically transport yourself, reappearing amid a burst of moonlight. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, and you have Advantage on the next Attack Roll you make before the end of this turn.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also regain uses by expending a level 2+ spell slot for each use you want to restore (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sda797d2d3669774","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Toughness","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-red-blue.webp","_id":"sdadd087a3c5ccfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Rune Known (Level 15)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn an additional Rune.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdb200809dd1fbad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Furious Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, as part of a melee weapon attack, you can move up to your Speed in a straight line towards a target of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/people/charge.webp","_id":"sdb339ac76b3c7de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Portent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. You roll three d20s for your Portent feature, rather than two.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdb3d77cd24ca0f0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tactical Shift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can move up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks when you use your Second Wind feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-glowing-yellow.webp","_id":"sdb9a5b7301d495e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Beast's Fury","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your companion can attack twice instead of once whenever it takes the Attack action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdbb3e25a54e0c41","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thief's Reflexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-beam-purple.webp","_id":"sdbb90ab34a91607","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Titanic Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The primeval companion can grow to Large size if you so choose, and when you summon it, you can grant it either a Climb Speed, Swim Speed, Fly Speed or Burrow Speed equal to its Speed.</p><p>In turn, the primeval companion lends you some of its terrifying might. Once per turn while your primeval companion is summoned, when you hit a creature with an attack or deal damage to a creature you can see with a spell you cast, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw against your spell save DC; on a failure, the creature is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdbd7d75de88779b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Runic Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to invoke your rune magic to protect your allies. When another creature you can see within 60 feet of you is hit by an Attack Roll, you can use your Reaction to force the attacker to reroll the d20 and use the new roll.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Additionally, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to regain one use.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdbf1fd7b6f8fbd9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (d10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d10s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdbfa9dd998749f1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Wildkeepers Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a Wild Domain. At each indicated Witch level, add the corresponding listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Dunes Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Earth Tremor, Silent Image, Dust Devil, Mirror Image</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Haste, Wall of Sand</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Blight, Hallucinatory Terrain</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Maelstrom, Mislead</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Marshes Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Grease, Ray of Sickness, Envenom, Ray of Enfeeblement</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Corrosion, Water Walk</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Evard's Black Tentacles, Vitriolic Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Acid Pit, Insect Plague</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Peaks Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Feather Fall, Witch Bolt, Earthbind, Darkvision</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Erupting Earth, Lightning Bolt</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Stoneskin, Wall of Stone</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Blindsense, Transmute Rock</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Tundras Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Fog Cloud, Ice Knife, Blindness/Deafness, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Slow, Glacial Spike</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Freedom of Movement</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Control Winds</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Waves Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Charm Person, Fog Cloud, Enthrall, Water Blast</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Tidal Wave, Water Breathing</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Control Water, Watery Sphere</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dominate Person, Maelstrom</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Wealds Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Animal Friendship, Beast Bond, Barkskin, Pass without Trace</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Conjure Animals, Speak with Plants</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Conjure Nature Spirits, Guardian of Nature</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Tree Stride, Wrath of Nature</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdcabec42cc21e2e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Third Eye","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your action to increase your powers of perception. When you do so, choose one of the following benefits, which lasts until you take a Short or a Long Rest. You can't use the feature again until you finish a rest.</p><p><strong>Darkvision.</strong> You can see normally in darkness, both magical and non-magical, to a distance of 120 feet.</p><p><strong>Greater Comprehension.</strong> You can read any language.</p><p><strong>Truesight.</strong> You gain truesight, to a distance of 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdd378136a93bc93","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose four spells of the necromancy school from any spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sddb0e0c5a3eb984","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battlerager Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action while you are raging.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sddc5274bf0f2f76","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Apotheosis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use one Metamagic option on each of your turns without spending Sorcery Points on it and your Spell Save DC is increased by 2 rather than 1.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sddd15516e2c6daa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Great Stature","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll.</p><p>Moreover, the extra damage you deal with your Giant's Might feature increases to 1d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdde0b0891a9b1f3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211635,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Greater Clawed Aspect","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Stalker's Rake.</strong> You can Hide as a Bonus Action. If you hit a creature with your natural weapons while hidden, it has Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw against your Clawed Aspect. Additionally, creatures Lacerated by you cannot make Opportunity Attacks.</li><li><strong>Big Game Hunter.</strong> When you use Primal Pounce and your attack hits, you can also attempt to Climb onto a Bigger Creature as per the Additional Combat Actions as a Bonus Action.</li><li><strong>Disembowel.</strong> If you hit a Prone creature with your natural weapons, you can force it to make the Saving Throw against your Clawed Aspect again, ignoring the usual per-turn limit. Once per turn, if the Prone creature is already Lacerated, it takes the damage from the condition immediately after the attack if it fails the Saving Throw.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sddfc21f53c88d00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211661,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Superiority Die","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sde09ca29935de5b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
