{"name":"Crafty Negotiator","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the persuasion skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/diplomacy-handshake.webp","_id":"sde609b88129742d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Durable Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The magic you channel helps ward off harm. While you maintain Concentration on a spell, you have a +2 bonus to AC and all Saving Throws.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sde974a39d34c255","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Death's Friend","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your association with death has become so close that you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>When you use your Wails from the Grave, you can deal the necrotic damage to both the first and the second creature.</li><li>When you roll initiative, you regain one soul trinket.</li><li>You also ignore Resistance to necrotic damage from your Wails from the Grave feature and treat Immunity to it as Resistance instead.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdea4143165db2dd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Divine Magic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your link to the divine allows you to learn spells from the cleric class. When your Spellcasting feature lets you learn or replace a sorcerer cantrip or a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher, you can choose the new spell from the cleric spell list or the sorcerer spell list. You must otherwise obey all the restrictions for selecting the spell, and it becomes a sorcerer spell for you.</p><p>In addition, you learn two additional 1st-level spells of your choice from the cleric spell list. These spells count as sorcerer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><p>When you reach 3rd level, 5th, 7th, and 9th level in this class, you also learn two additional spells of 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th level of your choice from the cleric spell, respectively.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sded1fa1a965650a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Royal Envoy","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Persuasion skill. If you are already proficient in it, you gain Proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Insight, Intimidation, or Performance.</p><p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses Persuasion. You receive this benefit regardless of the skill Proficiency you gain from this feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdef76f6d2d9c1c6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Contingency Plans","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As long as you are not incapacitated, you and allies within 60 feet that can see or hear you cannot be Surprised.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdf24d20c67b96d5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Call the Hunt","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The beast within you grows so powerful that you can spread its ferocity to others and gain resilience from them joining your hunt. When you enter your rage, you can choose a number of other willing creatures you can see within 30 feet of you equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of one creature).</p><p>You gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature that accepts this feature. Until the rage ends, the chosen creatures can each use the following benefit once on each of their turns: when the creature hits a target with an Attack Roll and deals damage to it, the creature can roll a d6 and gain a bonus to the damage equal to the number rolled.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdfc65c91ecef664","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mastery of Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You use your familiarity with death to escape its grasp. When you are reduced to 0 hit points and don't die outright, you can expend 1 ki point (no action required) to have 1 hit point instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sdffd467bc473d45","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flyby","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You don't provoke Opportunity Attacks when you fly out of an enemy's reach.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/birds-flock-fly-yellow.webp","_id":"se00a0eb1e7f0864","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spell Resistance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on Saving Throws against spells.</p><p>Furthermore, you have Resistance against the damage of spells.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se015b164172c3e0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict Improvement (Level 17)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use your Blood Maledict feature five times between rests.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"se044f3f1181043e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211620,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental School","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A kineticist chooses one primary element on which to focus. This element determines how she accesses the raw power of the Ethereal Plane, and grants you features at 1st level and again at 6th, 10th, 15th, and 20th level.</p><p>Regardless of your chosen element, you use your Charisma modifier when setting Attack Rolls and determining the Saving Throw DC of your abilities.</p><p><b>Spell save DC</b> = 8 + your Proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier</p><p><b>Spell attack modifier</b> = your Proficiency bonus + your Charisma modifier</p><p><strong>The Elements, intertwined.</strong> Unlike other classes, the kineticist can mix and match her subclass features, provided she has access to multiple different elements through her Expanded Element class feature.</p><p>If so, she can choose from the subclass features available to any of her schools at the appropriate level. For example, if a kineticist picked air as her school at 1st level and then fire at 6th, she can choose her subclass feature at 7th level from either school.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/elements-air-earth-fire-water.webp","_id":"se0bbdb0e181919f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Combat Superiority (Level 18)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your superiority dice turn into d12s.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0d87e3a9399e7f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Charge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see when you use your Action Surge. You can teleport before or after the additional action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se0da13232e04d5d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hunter's Aegis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you cast Protection from Evil and Good through your Hunter's Mysticism Feature, it does not require Concentration and lasts for 7 days.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se12abc7e9253c71","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211634,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magical Ambush","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If you are hidden from a creature when you cast a spell on it, the creature has Disadvantage on any Saving Throw it makes against the spell this turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se15edd18791f921","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211655,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Battering Roots","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Tendrils of the World Tree extend from your melee weapons. While you wield any melee weapon, your reach with that weapon increases by 10 feet.</p><p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack while raging, you can use the Shove action against that same creature. You can count as Huge for the purpose of this Shove.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se1f922ea0e9136f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Controlled Chaos","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain a modicum of control over the surges of your wild magic. Whenever you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table, you can roll twice and use either number.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se1fc86e5a6a459d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211664,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Expert Crafter","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in two tools of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-and-nail.webp","_id":"se25ac26c8cfd686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211689,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mighty Summoner","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Beasts and fey that you conjure are more resilient than normal. Any beast or fey summoned or created by a spell that you cast gains the following benefits:</p><ul><li>The creature appears with more hit points than normal: 2 extra hit points per Hit Die it has.</li><li>The damage from its natural weapons is considered magical for the purpose of overcoming Immunity and Resistance to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se2a0756343eb82e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"The Master's Odem","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you open a small portal and call upon the raw energy of your patron's powerful breath weapon.</p><p>Every creature in the area of effect, which originates from your position, has to make a Saving Throw against your spell save DC. A target takes 15d10 damage on a failed save, and half as much on a successful one. The shape, Saving Throw, and damage type of the breath weapon depends on your draconic patron.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Master's Odem</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Draconic Patron</th><th scope=\"col\">Breath Weapon</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Jabberwock</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Night</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>90 ft cone (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Shadow</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>120x10 ft line (DEX save)</td></tr><tr><td>Sylvan</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>90 ft cone (CON save)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se2c6bec24431fe1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master Duelist","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Immediately after you use your Sneak Attack, you can make another attack against the same target with a melee weapon you are holding, provided the target is within your reach and no other creatures are within 5 feet of you.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se3a59003332439b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211657,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psionic Defenses","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Resistance to psychic damage. When you have to make a Wisdom Saving Throw, you can make an Intelligence Saving Throw instead.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se3a7b52a9044db4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Combat Superiority","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn maneuvers that are fueled by special dice called superiority dice.</p><p><strong>Maneuvers.</strong> You learn three maneuvers of your choice, which are listed under \"Maneuvers\" below. Many maneuvers enhance an attack in some way. You can use only one maneuver per attack.</p><p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice at 7th, 10th, and 15th level. Each time you learn new maneuvers, you can also replace one maneuver you know with a different one.</p><p><strong>Superiority Dice.</strong> You have four superiority dice, which are d8s. A superiority die is expended when you use it. You regain all of your expended superiority dice when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. You can also spend a use of your Second Wind to regain a superiority die (no action required).</p><p>You gain another superiority die at 7th level and one more at 15th level.</p><p><strong>Saving Throws.</strong> Some of your maneuvers require your target to make a Saving Throw to resist the maneuver's effects. The Saving Throw DC is calculated as follows:</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Maneuver save DC</strong> = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier + your Dexterity modifier</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se3b9f8ec8469631","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Focused Aim","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can spend 1 to 3 ki points to increase your Attack Roll by 2 for each of these ki points you spend, potentially turning the miss into a hit.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you hit another creature with a melee weapon attack"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"save","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/crosshair-triple-strike-orange.webp","_id":"se43a7e04afa3dc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Absorb Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you successfully end or disrupt a spell with Dispel Magic or Counterspell, you regain Sorcery Points equal to half the level of the spell slot you used to cast them (rounded up).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se440192049ce81e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Twin Eidolon","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use an Action to assume the shape of your Eidolon, adopting its Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, armor class, and hitpoints, and all its features and evolution feats.</p><p>You also retain all of your skill and Saving Throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the Eidolon.</p><p>You retain the benefit of any features from your class, race, or other source and can use them, provided that your new form is physically capable of doing so. You can't use any special senses you have (for example, darkvision) unless your new form also has that sense.</p><p>When you transform, you choose whether your equipment falls to the ground, merges into the new form, or is worn by it. Worn equipment functions as normal. The DM determines whether it is practical for the new form to wear a piece of equipment, based on the form's shape and size. Your equipment doesn't change shape or size to match the new form, and any equipment that the new form can't wear must either fall to the ground or merge into your new form. Equipment that merges has no effect in that state.</p><p>You can maintain this form up to 1 hour while concentrating (as if concentrating on a spell) and you cannot assume it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/spirit-undead-horned-blue.webp","_id":"se449c6d01688850","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Vigilant Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You respond to danger with extraordinary vigilance. In combat, you get a special Reaction that you can take once on every creature's turn, except your turn. You can use this special Reaction only to make an Opportunity Attack, and you can't use it on the same turn that you take your normal Reaction.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se4666418943521d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animating Performance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can animate one Large or smaller nonmagical item within 30 feet of you that isn't being worn or carried.. The animate item uses the Dancing Item stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB). The item is friendly to you and your companions and obeys your commands. It lives for 1 hour, until it is reduced to 0 hit points, or until you die.</p><p>In combat, the animated item shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the animated item's.</p><p>When you use your Bardic Inspiration feature, you can command the item as part of the same Bonus Action you use for Bardic Inspiration.</p><p>Once you animate an item with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher to use this feature again. You can have only one item animated by this feature at a time; if you use this action and already have a dancing item from this feature, the first one immediately becomes inanimate.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se487e70b6731fc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Blood Maledict","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to channel—or sometimes sacrifice—a part of your vital essence to curse and manipulate creatures through hemocraft magic. You know one blood curse of your choice. A list of the available blood curses can be found on the Optional Features page. You learn one additional blood curse of your choice at 3rd, 6th, 10th, 14th, and 18th level. Each time you learn a new blood curse, you can also choose one of the blood curses you know and replace it with another blood curse.</p><p>Each time you use your Blood Maledict feature, you choose which curse to invoke from the curses you know. While invoking a blood curse, but before it affects the target, you can choose to amplify the curse by taking necrotic damage equal to one roll of your hemocraft die. This damage can't be reduced in any way. An amplified curse gains an additional effect, noted in the curse's description. Creatures that do not have blood are Immune to blood curses unless you have amplified the curse.</p><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all uses on a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":"@scale.bloodhunter.blood-maledict","per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["@scale.bloodhunter.hemocraft","necrotic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-beam-blood-large-red-gray.webp","_id":"se4ec083778d1719","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Consult the Spirits","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to consult with your ancestral spirits. When you do so, you cast the Augury or Clairvoyance spell, without using a spell slot or material components. Rather than creating a spherical sensor, this use of Clairvoyance invisibly summons one of your ancestral spirits to the chosen location. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells.</p><p>After you cast either spell in this way, you can't use this feature again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-shadow-blue.webp","_id":"se5358aec7d67d6e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Remarkable Athlete","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</p><p>You gain Proficiency in either the Athletics or Acrobatics skill. If you are already proficient in the chosen skill, you add double your Proficiency bonus to checks you make with it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-boots-brown.webp","_id":"se585d5191d48689","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Resilience of the Wilds","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Every time you cast a Witch spell of 1st level or higher, your bonded familiar gains temporary hit points equal to four times the spell's level.</p><p>Additionally, you and your bonded familiar gain Resistance to the same damage type gained through the Battle Familiar feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se5ae56331422bad","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Evasion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you're subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity Saving Throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the Saving Throw and only half damage if you fail.</p><p>You don't benefit from this feature if you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/beam-red-orange.webp","_id":"se5c05267751ad98","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Psychic Mastery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to psychic damage and your features ignore Resistance to psychic damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se6057daa17a0cbc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211644,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfect Focus","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you roll Initiative and don't use Uncanny Metabolism, you regain expended Ki Points until you have 4 if you have 3 or fewer.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/orb-shadow-blue.webp","_id":"se612e34e30e5ae4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211641,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Natural Weapons","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Even when not shifted, your form is permanently altered to include fangs, claws, or talons. When you make a melee weapon attack with these natural weapons, you roll a d6 and add your Strength or Dexterity modifier to the attack and damage roll (your choice).</p><p>This die changes as you gain shifter levels, as shown in the Natural Weapons column of the Shifter table.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/claws/claw-talons-yellow-red.webp","_id":"se651f50e241358f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor of Hexes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when a creature hits you with an attack, that creature has to make a Charisma Saving Throw. On a failure, it is subject to the effects of the Bane spell until the start of its next turn (no Concentration required). The effect applies to the triggering attack roll, possibly causing it to miss.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se68a115c6005e88","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Silent Flight","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Proficiency in the Stealth skill.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/birds/raptor-owl-flying-moon.webp","_id":"se6c0dc3e6229ced","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The maneuvers are presented in alphabetical order.</p><h5>Commander's Strike</h5><p>When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can forgo one of your attacks to direct one of your companions to strike. When you do so, choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you and expend one superiority die. That creature can immediately use its Reaction to make one weapon attack, adding the superiority die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Disarming Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to disarm the target, forcing it to drop one item of your choice that it's holding. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, it drops the object you choose. The object lands at its feet.</p><h5>Distracting Strike</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to distract the creature, giving your allies an opening. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll. The next Attack Roll against the target by an attacker other than you has Advantage if the attack is made before the start of your next turn.</p><h5>Evasive Footwork</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die and take the Disengage action. You also roll the die and add the number rolled to your AC until the start of your next turn.</p><h5>Feinting Attack</h5><p>You can expend one superiority die and use a Bonus Action on your turn to feint, choosing one creature within 5 feet of you as your target. You have Advantage on your next Attack Roll against that creature this turn. If that attack hits, add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Goading Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage on all Attack Rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Lunging Attack</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die and take the Dash action. If you move at least 5 feet in a straight line immediately before hitting with a melee attack as part of the Attack action on this turn, you can add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Maneuvering Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to maneuver one of your comrades into a more advantageous position. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and you choose a friendly creature who can see or hear you. That creature can use its Reaction to move up to half its Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks from the target of your attack.</p><h5>Menacing Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to frighten the target. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failed save, it is Frightened of you until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Parry</h5><p>When another creature damages you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction and expend one superiority die to reduce the damage by the number you roll on your superiority die + STR or DEX modifier (your choice) + fighter level.</p><h5>Precision Attack</h5><p>When you miss with an Attack Roll, you can expend one Superiority Die, roll that die, and add it to the Attack Roll, potentially causing the attack to hit.</p><h5>Pushing Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to drive the target back. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, you push the target up to 15 feet away from you.</p><h5>Rally</h5><p>As a Bonus Action, you can expend one Superiority Die to bolster the resolve of a companion. Choose an ally of yours within 30 feet of yourself who can see or hear you. That creature gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the Superiority Die roll plus half your Fighter level (round down).</p><h5>Riposte</h5><p>When a creature misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction and expend one superiority die to make a melee weapon attack against the creature. If you hit, you add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll.</p><h5>Staggering Strike</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock a target off-balance. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is Large or smaller, it must make a Constitution Saving Throw. On a failed save, the target cannot take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the end of your next turn.</p><h5>Sweeping Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to damage another creature with the same attack. Choose another creature within 5 feet of the original target and within your reach. If the original Attack Roll would hit the second creature, it takes damage equal to the number you roll on your superiority die. The damage is of the same type dealt by the original attack.</p><h5>Trip Attack</h5><p>When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to knock the target down. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and if the target is no more than 1 size larger than you, it must make a Strength Saving Throw. On a failed save, you knock the target Prone.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se6c99702b8755f2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fleet of Foot","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your base walking increases to 35 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/movement/feet-winged-sandals-tan.webp","_id":"se71c04198c83af3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Soul of the Forge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of the forge grants you special abilities:</p><ul><li>You gain Resistance to fire damage.</li><li>While wearing heavy armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se7250bbb238d53b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211623,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Instinctive Pounce","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As part of the Bonus Action you take to enter your rage, you can move up to half your Speed.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp","_id":"se7306b67e4cc93d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Hoarfrost Herald","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your mastery of ice grants you special abilities:</p><ul><li>You have Resistance to cold damage.</li><li>You ignore 3 and movement Speed reductions caused by cold, ice, and snow, whether mundane or magical.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se78e0b1325fe759","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cosmic Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can consult your Star Map for omens. When you do so, roll a die. Until you finish your next Long Rest, you gain access to a special Reaction based on whether you rolled an even or an odd number on the die:</p><ul><li><strong>Weal (even).</strong> Whenever a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is about to make an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to roll a d6 and add the number rolled to the total.</li><li><strong>Woe (odd).</strong> Whenever a creature you can see within 30 feet of you is about to make an Attack Roll, a Saving Throw, or an Ability Check, you can use your Reaction to roll a d6 and subtract the number rolled from the total.</li></ul><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se7c3d03ade88d7d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Create Thrall","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to infect a humanoid's mind with the alien magic of your patron. You can use your action to touch an Incapacitated humanoid. That creature is then Charmed by you until a Remove Curse spell is cast on it, the Charmed condition is removed from it, or you use this feature again.</p><p>You can communicate telepathically with the Charmed creature as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"se845ded176031a1","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armor Modifications","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn how to use your artificer infusions to specially modify your Arcane Armor. That armor now counts as separate items for the purposes of your Infuse Items feature: armor (the chest piece), boots, helmet, and the armor's special weapon. Each of those items can bear one of your infusions, and the infusions transfer over if you change your armor's model with the Armor Model feature. In addition, the maximum number of items you can infuse at once increases by 2, but those extra items must be part of your Arcane Armor.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/feet/boots-armored-banded-steel.webp","_id":"se8636038dce2524","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Font of Inspiration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You now regain all your expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p><p>In addition, you can expend a spell slot (no action required) to regain one expended use of Bardic Inspiration.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/sihouette-hold-beam-green.webp","_id":"se8811458f88af80","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowering Reserves","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you make an Ability Check, you can spend 1 sorcery points to gain Advantage on the check.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you make an ability check"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/air/wind-tornado-wall-blue.webp","_id":"se907efcd0d2b1ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wholeness of Body","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to heal yourself. As an Action, you can regain hit points equal to three times your monk level. You must finish a Short or a Long Rest before you can use this feature again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp","_id":"se9ce57b38f4d8e7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Magic Item Adept","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You achieve a profound understanding of how to use and make magic items:</p><ul><li>You can attune to up to four magic items at once.</li><li>If you craft a magic item with a rarity of common or uncommon, it takes you a quarter of the normal time, and it costs you half as much of the usual gold.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/plant-seed-hands-glow-yellow.webp","_id":"se9d79f14c507654","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Awakened Astral Self","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your connection to your astral self is complete, allowing you to unleash its full potential. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 3 ki points to summon the arms, visage, and body of your astral self and awaken it for 10 minutes. Alternatively, you can spend these ki points as part of the same Bonus Action you used for another Monk feature. This awakening ends early if you are Incapacitated or die.</p><p>The cost is reduced by 1 each if you have currently summoned your astral arms and your astral visage.</p><p>While your astral self is awakened, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Armor of the Spirit.</strong> You gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class.</p><p><strong>Astral Barrage.</strong> Whenever you use the Extra Attack feature to attack twice, you can instead attack three times if all the attacks are made with your astral arms.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sea00df4b120b7a6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Pounce","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, as part of an attack with your natural weapons, you can move up to your Speed in a straight line towards a target of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/cougar-pounce-stalk-black.webp","_id":"seabe4cfd0a62972","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Primal Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your natural weapons count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-fist-strike.webp","_id":"seb0e15a2efada02","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211660,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Empowered Channeling","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your ability to channel spirits improves. You gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Power from Beyond.</strong> Once per turn, when you cast a Bard spell that deals damage or restores Hit Points, roll a d6. You gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls or to the total Hit Points the spell restores equal to the number rolled.</li><li><strong>Spiritual Manifestation.</strong> You always have the Spirit Guardians spell prepared. You can cast the spell once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul><p>Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so the spirits also guard against worldly threats. When cast in this way, you and allies within the spell's Emanation have Half Cover. Once you modify the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seb31b1acccc567d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Waxing and Waning","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain greater control over the phases of your lunar magic. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 sorcery point to change your lunar phase for a different one.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seb34cf28b958417","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Momentary Stasis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically force a Large or smaller creature you can see within 60 feet of you to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. Unless the Saving Throw is a success, the creature is encased in a field of magical energy until the end of your next turn or until the creature takes any damage. While encased in this way, the creature is Paralyzed and has a Speed of 0. This feature ignores Immunity to the Paralyzed condition.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seb66e36530de0d9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Anger of a Gentle Soul","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to visit vengeance on someone who fells others. If you see a creature reduce another creature to 0 hit points, you can use your Reaction to grant yourself a bonus to all damage rolls against the aggressor until the end of your next turn. The bonus equals your monk level.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sebe6170a3c3105e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Master's Flourish","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you use a Blade Flourish option, you can roll a d6 and use it instead of expending a Bardic Inspiration die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sec05bfb148f00a2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Reanimated Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Using Tinker's Tools or another type of Artisan's Tools with which you have Proficient, you can take a Magic action to create a Reanimated Companion (see the stat block) through the power of necromancy and science. The companion manifests in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. You determine the companion's appearance; your choices don't affect the companion's game statistics.</p><p>The companion is Friendly to you and your allies and obeys you. It lasts until you finish a Long Rest or until you take a Magic action to dismiss it early, at which point it harmlessly collapses into a pile of viscera. It immediately drops to 0 Hit Points and dies if you die.</p><p>Once you create a companion, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest or expend a spell slot to create one. You can have only one companion at a time and can't create one while your companion is present.</p><ul><li><strong>The Companion in Combat.</strong> The Reanimated Companion shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the companion's.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sec11a43830604c9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Gift","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You begin to take on characteristics of your patron's kind. You now have Resistance to a damage type determined by your patron's kind: bludgeoning (dao), thunder (djinni), fire (efreeti), or cold (marid).</p><p>In addition, as a Bonus Action, you can give yourself a Fly Speed of 30 feet that lasts for 10 minutes, during which you can hover. You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sec258babb561b1e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211672,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eldritch Invocations","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have unearthed Eldritch Invocations, pieces of forbidden knowledge that imbue you with an abiding magical ability or other lessons. You gain one invocation of your choice, such as Pact of the Tome. Invocations are described in the Optional Features page.</p><p><strong>Prerequisites.</strong> If an invocation has a prerequisite, you must meet it to learn that invocation. For example, if an invocation requires you to be a level 5+ Warlock, you can select the invocation once you reach Warlock level 5.</p><p><strong>Replacing and Gaining Invocations.</strong> Whenever you gain a Warlock level, you can replace one of your invocations with another one for which you qualify. You can't replace an invocation if it's a prerequisite for another invocation that you have.</p><p>When you gain certain Warlock levels, you gain more invocations of your choice, as shown in the Invocations column of the Warlock Features table.</p><p>You can't pick the same invocation more than once unless its description says otherwise.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/strike-hand-glow-pink.webp","_id":"sec89d6fe2fecab7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211670,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Danger Sense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain an uncanny sense of when things aren't as they should be, giving you an edge when you dodge perils. You have Advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws unless you have the Incapacitated condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/wounds/injury-face-impact-orange.webp","_id":"sec9988bb86a4b61","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Guided Precision","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, whenever you cast a spell from your Plane Charter Spells list or hit a creature affected by your Faerie Fire with an attack roll, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell or attack.</p><p>In addition, taking damage can't cause you to lose Concentration on Faerie Fire.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"whenever you cast a spell from your Cartographer Spells list or hit a creature affected by your Faerie Fire with an attack roll"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"@abilities.int.mod","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/targeting/target-strike-triple-blue.webp","_id":"secdbd78dc18f4fd","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211612,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Adventurer's Atlas","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest while holding Cartographer's Tools, you can use that tool to create a set of magical maps by touching at least two creatures (one of whom can be yourself), up to a maximum number of creatures equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum of two creatures). Each target receives a magical map, which constantly updates to show the relative position of all the map holders but is illegible to all others. The maps last until you die or until you use this feature again, at which point any existing maps created by this feature immediately vanish.</p><p>While carrying the map, a target gains the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Awareness.</strong> The target adds 1d4 to its Initiative rolls.</p><p><strong>Positioning.</strong> The target knows the location of all other map holders that are on the same plane of existence as itself. When casting a spell or creating another effect that requires being able to see the effect's target, a map holder can target another map holder regardless of sight or cover, so long as the other map holder is still within the effect's range.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d4","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-symbol-circle-white.webp","_id":"sece24ba9639306b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Thought Shield","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means unless you allow it. You also have Resistance to psychic damage, and whenever a creature deals psychic damage to you, that creature takes the same amount of damage that you do.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sed5d0b8d2562087","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Armor","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your metallurgical pursuits have led to you making armor a conduit for your magic. As an Action, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor, provided you have armorsmith's tools in hand.</p><p>You gain the following benefits while wearing this armor:</p><ul><li>If the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the arcane armor lacks this requirement for you.</li><li>You can use the arcane armor as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells.</li><li>The armor attaches to you and can't be removed against your will. It also expands to cover your entire body, although you can retract or deploy the helmet as a Bonus Action. The armor replaces any missing limbs, functioning identically to a limb it replaces.</li><li>You can doff or don the armor as an Action. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/equipment/chest/breastplate-gorget-steel.webp","_id":"see34c77015588e5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable Defense","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain Resistance to two damage types of your choice. Whenever you finish a Short or a Long Rest, you can change the damage types you chose.</p><p>As an Action, you can temporarily give up this Resistance and transfer it to one creature you touch. The creature keeps the Resistance until the end of your next Short or a Long Rest or until you transfer it back to yourself as a Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"see881783f4fa59b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mortal Bulwark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You manifest a spark of divine power in defense of the mortal realms. As a Bonus Action, you gain the following benefits for 1 minute:</p><ul><li>You gain truesight with a range of 120 feet.</li><li>You have Advantage on Attack Rolls against aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, and fiends.</li><li>When you hit a creature with an Attack Roll and deal damage to it, you can also force it to make a Charisma Saving Throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature is magically banished to its native plane of existence if it's currently not there. On a successful save, the creature can't be banished by this feature for 24 hours.</li></ul><p>Once you use this Bonus Action, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a 5th-level spell slot to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"seea61107d343686","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Circle Forms","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While in a Wild Shape form, you gain the following benefits.</p><ul><li><strong>Lunar Blessing.</strong> Your attacks in a Wild Shape form count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</li><li><strong>Increased Toughness.</strong> You can add your Wisdom modifier to your Constitution Saving Throws.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sef25010e187170e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Perfected Bond","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bond to your drake reaches the pinnacle of its power. While your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><strong>Empowered Attack.</strong> The drake's Bite, Elemental Bolt, and Infused Strikes attacks deal an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for its Draconic Essence (for a total of 2d6 extra damage).</li><li><strong>Draconic Might.</strong> The drake grows to Huge size. Its Strength and Constitution are increased by 4 and its Hit Points increase by an additional 2 for each of your levels in this class.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Breath.</strong> The size of your Drake's Breath increases to 60 feet and you regain its use on a Short Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sef7fd34eaaf839b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sef8b3ca09799011","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211630,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Persecutor's Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the following new ways to use your Sneak Attack:</p><ul><li><strong>Brand (Cost: 3d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or lose the ability to cast spells and turn Invisible until the end of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Castigate (Cost: 1d6).</strong> The target must succeed on a Wisdom Saving Throw or subtract 1d6 from its next Saving Throw before the end of your next turn.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sefc215061b35698","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211656,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infuse Item","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to imbue mundane items with certain magical infusions. The magic items you create with this feature are effectively prototypes of permanent items.</p><div><strong>Artificer Infusions</strong><p>Artificers have invented numerous magical infusions, extraordinary processes that rapidly create magic items. To many, artificers seem like wonderworkers, accomplishing in hours what others need weeks to complete.</p><p>The description of each of the following infusions details the type of item that can receive it, along with whether the resulting magic item requires attunement.</p><p>Some infusions specify a minimum artificer level. You can't learn such an infusion until you are at least that level.</p><p>Unless an infusion's description says otherwise, you can't learn an infusion more than once.</p></div<p><strong>Infusing an Item.</strong> Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can touch a nonmagical object and imbue it with one of your artificer infusions, turning it into a magic item. An infusion works on only certain kinds of objects, as specified in the infusion's description. If the item requires attunement, you can attune yourself to it the instant you infuse the item. If you decide to attune to the item later, you must do so using the normal process for attunement.</p><p>Your infusion remains in an item indefinitely, but when you die, the infusion vanishes after a number of days have passed equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 day). The infusion also vanishes if you give up your knowledge of the infusion for another one.</p><p>You can infuse more than one nonmagical object at the end of a Long Rest; the maximum number of objects appears in the Infused Items column of the Artificer table. You must touch each of the objects, and each of your infusions can be in only one object at a time. Moreover, no object can bear more than one of your infusions at a time. If you try to exceed your maximum number of infusions, the oldest infusion immediately ends, and then the new infusion applies.</p><p>If an infusion ends on an item that contains other things, like a bag of holding, its contents harmlessly appear in and around its space.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/swords/sword-runed-glowing.webp","_id":"sefdc576e12839b4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Drake Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>As an Action, you can magically summon the drake that is bound to you. It appears in an unoccupied space of your choice within 30 feet of you.</p><p>The drake is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See its game statistics in the accompanying Drake Companion stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. Whenever you summon the drake, choose a damage type listed in its Draconic Essence trait. You can determine the cosmetic characteristics of the drake, such as its color, its scale texture, or any visible effect of its Draconic Essence; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.</p><p>In combat, the drake obeys your commands as best it can. It rolls for initiative like any other creature, but you determine its actions, decisions, attitudes, and so on. If you are Incapacitated or absent, your companion acts on its own. If you are small enough to ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can any of its actions during your turn or immediately after.</p><p>The drake remains until it is reduced to 0 hit points, until you use this feature to summon the drake again, or until you die. Anything the drake was wearing or carrying is left behind when the drake vanishes.</p><p>Once you summon the drake, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher to summon it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf02ccb1b899c2ee","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211650,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Nature's Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You are Immune to diseases and the Poisoned condition, and you have Resistance to a damage type associated with your current land choice in the Circle Spells feature, as shown in the Nature's Ward table.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Nature's Ward</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Land Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Arid</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Polar</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Temperate</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Tropical</td><td>Poison</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/commodities/flowers/lotus-pink.webp","_id":"sf077858ef890f22","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211627,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sorcerous Origin","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Choose a sorcerous origin, which describes the source of your innate magical power, from the list of available origins.</p><p>Your choice grants you features when you choose it at 3rd level and again at 6th, 14th, and 18th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf0d7cd0bae0bdfb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Infused Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Eidolon's Attacks are treated as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/abilities/stinger-poison-green.webp","_id":"sf1c33dd4f48db95","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211668,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadowy Dodge","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>WWhen a creature makes an Attack Roll against you, you can take a Reaction to impose Disadvantage on that roll. Whether the attack hits or misses, you can then teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf20ed8aba57c6e4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steel Defender","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your tinkering has borne you a faithful companion, a steel defender. It is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See this creature's game statistics in the steel defender stat block, which uses your Proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. You determine the creature's appearance and whether it has two legs or four; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.</p><p>In combat, the defender shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. If you are small enough to ride it, you can direct it to use its movement on your turn (no action required). It otherwise prioritizes following you and defending you from threats and then itself. If you take a Bonus Action on your turn, you can command it to take specific actions. These actions can be one in its stat block or some other action and can be taken during your turn rather than the defender's.</p><p>If the Mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. If it has died within the last hour, you can use your armorsmith's tools as an Action to revive it, provided you are within 5 feet of it and you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. The steel defender returns to life after 1 minute with all its hit points restored.</p><p>At the end of a Long Rest, you can create a new steel defender if you have your armorsmith's tools with you. If you already have a steel defender from this feature, the first one immediately perishes. The defender also perishes if you die.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/magical/construct-golem-stone-blue.webp","_id":"sf20f3e38f1c4396","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211611,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Fateweavers Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Fateweavers Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Heroism, Silvery Barbs, Augury, Zone of Truth</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Clairvoyance, Counterspell</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Divination, Spell Turning</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Dream, Scrying</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2207502e012e00","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Legion of One","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can use a Bonus Action to create two echoes with your Manifest Echo feature, and these echoes can coexist. If you try to create a third echo, the previous two echoes are destroyed. Anything you can do from one echo's position can be done from the other's instead.</p><p>In addition, when you roll initiative and have no uses of your Unleash Incarnation feature left, you regain one use of that feature.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf2ba8ba71303da3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Steps of Night","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can draw on the mystical power of night to rise into the air. As a Bonus Action when you are in dim light or darkness, you can magically give yourself a Fly Speed equal to your Speed for 1 minute. You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf334f32ae31e4ce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211625,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Overflow","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>A kineticist's body surges with energy from her chosen element whenever she spends kinesis points, causing her to glow with a nimbus of fire, weep water from her pores, or experience some other thematic effect.</p><p>When you have less than half your current maximum number of kinesis points, your Charisma bonus to damage on your kinetic shape is doubled. Additionally, you gain Resistance to one damage type corresponding to one of your chosen elements. You can change the chosen resistance to a different one corresponding to one of your chosen elements at the start of each of your turns.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sf34739b438317ff","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Way of the Long Death","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Monks of the Way of the Long Death are obsessed with the meaning and mechanics of dying. They capture creatures and prepare elaborate experiments to capture, record, and understand the moments of their demise. They use this knowledge to guide their understanding of martial arts, yielding a deadly fighting style.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf38eb0c848b9e3d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Defensive Tactics","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain one of the following features of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/nature/leaf-rune-glow-green.webp","_id":"sf397f469aad0d7c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Innate Sorcery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>An event in your past left an indelible mark on you, infusing you with simmering magic. As a Bonus Action, you can unleash that magic for 1 minute, during which you gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li>The spell save DC of your Sorcerer spells increases by 1.</li><li>You have Advantage on the Attack Rolls of Sorcerer spells you cast.</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"bonus","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":2,"max":2,"per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/hand-sparks-smoke-green.webp","_id":"sf3a3f6f76a89207","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Archfamiliar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your occult bond with your familiar is at the height of its power, granting you the following benefits:</p><p><strong>Bonded Magic.</strong> Choose three Witch spells of 1st or 2nd level. You always have the chosen spells prepared. Your bonded familiar also learns these spells. Both of you can cast these spells without spell slots and without material components. It uses your spellcasting attack bonus and spell save DC for these spells.</p><p><strong>Life Ward.</strong> When either you or your bonded familiar drop to 0 hit points but aren't killed out right, you can change the affected target's hit points to a number equal to triple your Witch level. You cannot use this feature again until you have completed a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Longevity.</strong> The mystical powers coursing through you grant you an extended life span. For every nine years that pass, your body ages only one year.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3f231dc189acf0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fungal Infestation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your spores gain the ability to infest a corpse and animate it. If a beast or a humanoid that is Small or Medium dies within 10 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to animate it, causing it to stand up immediately with 1 hit point. The creature uses the zombie stat block in the Monster Manual. It remains animate for 1 hour, after which time it collapses and dies.</p><p>In combat, the zombie's turn comes immediately after yours. It obeys your mental commands, and the only action it can take is the Attack action, making one melee attack.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf3f47cae1322994","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211628,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Deflect Attacks","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When an Attack Roll hits you and its damage includes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage, you can take a Reaction to reduce the attack's total damage against you. The reduction equals 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier and Monk level.</p><p>If you reduce the damage to 0, you can expend 1 Ki Point to redirect some of the attack's force. If you do so, choose a creature you can see within 5 feet of yourself if the attack was a melee attack or a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself that isn't behind Total Cover if the attack was a ranged attack. That creature must succeed on a Dexterity Saving Throw or take damage equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die plus your Dexterity modifier. The damage is the same type dealt by the attack.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when an Attack Roll hits you and its damage includes Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"1d10 + @abilities.dex.mod + @classes.monk.levels","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/ranged/arrow-flying-white-blue.webp","_id":"sf460753e0735e8d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211640,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wild Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to summon a spirit that assumes an animal form: as an Action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape feature to cast the Find Familiar spell, without material components.</p><p>When you cast the spell in this way, the familiar is a fey instead of a beast.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"action","cost":1,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/mammals/rabbit-movement-glowing-green.webp","_id":"sf46ae0da8633644","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211626,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Wrath of the Raging Serpent","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are raging you can call down your god's fury in the form of a powerful lightning bolt when you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack. The target has to make a Dexterity Saving Throw. The DC is equal to 8 + your Proficiency + your STR modifier. On a failure, the creature takes 12d10 lightning damage, and half as much on a successful one. Any creature that you have Grappled has Disadvantage on this Saving Throw.</p><p>You cannot use this feature again until you have finished a Long Rest, unless you spend a use of your rage to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf48f8201b204ec0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211615,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Impeccable Memory","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Advantage on all INT-checks to recall information about something.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/time/arrows-circling-pink.webp","_id":"sf50a9c8c89bff36","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211685,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Arcane Tradition","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You choose an arcane tradition from the list of available traditions, shaping your practice of magic. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/water/orb-ice-glow.webp","_id":"sf51c02ad3e65cc5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aerokinesis","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, you learn the Gust cantrip, which you can cast using only its somatic component.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf530e4113288278","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Icy Glare","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself deals damage to you or forces you to make a Saving Throw, you can use your Reaction to force the creature to make a Wisdom Saving Throw. On a failure, the target takes 4d8 cold damage and its Speed is reduced 0 until the start of your next turn. On a success, it takes half as much damage and its Speed isn't reduced. This damage ignores Resistance.</p><p>You can use this Reaction a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf5ce2020e380517","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211653,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bardic Inspiration (d8)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Bardic Inspiration die changes to a d8.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist.webp","_id":"sf61942f11cd5deb","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211616,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Smite Infidel","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Once per turn, when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can mark that creature until the end of your next turn. The first attack that hits the marked creature deals additional radiant damage equal to half your warlord level (rounded down) + your Leadership ability modifier.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf63a5380c820302","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211675,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Elemental Attunement","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn the Elementalism cantrip and Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it. You only use the somatic component to cast this spell.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/silhouette-hold-change-blue.webp","_id":"sf68c28451364edc","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211637,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Rage","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Rage can keep you fighting despite grievous wounds. If you drop to 0 Hit Points while your Rage is active and don't die outright, you can make a DC 10 Constitution Saving Throw. If you succeed, your Hit Points instead change to a number equal to twice your Barbarian level.</p><p>Each time you use this feature after the first, the DC increases by 5. When you finish a Short or a Long Rest, the DC resets to 10.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/social/intimidation-impressing.webp","_id":"sf68d9c6e9c5d8af","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Armored Hulk","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you enter a rage, you gain the temporary hit points from your armor mastery again, which stack with any existing temporary hit points from that feature. These temporary hit points last until your rage ends.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf699825e06105b9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211614,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Astral Sequestration","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to sequester yourself and your allies on the Astral Plane.</p><p>By performing a special ritual over the course of 5 minutes, you shift yourself and up to ten willing creatures you can see to the Astral Plane. You and those creatures gain the benefits of a Short Rest while sequestered on the Astral Plane. You then return to the spaces you all occupied when you used this ability, with no time having passed in the world.</p><p>During this Short Rest, you and the creatures you sequester can make use of any options available during a rest that affect only you and the creatures you sequester.</p><p>Once you use this ability, you cannot use it again until you complete a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf6b9143c64c9d4f","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211671,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Animal Companion","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to use your magic to create a powerful bond with a creature of the natural world.</p><p>With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 50 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth an animal from the wilderness to serve as your faithful companion. You can select any beast of CR 1/2 or lower as your companion. However, your choices may be restricted depending on the area you currently find yourself in. Your DM determines if any such restrictions apply.</p><p>At the end of the 8 hours, your animal companion appears and gains all the benefits of your Companion's Bond ability. You can have only one animal companion at a time.</p><p>If your animal companion is ever slain, the magical bond you share allows you to return it to life. With 8 hours of work and the expenditure of 25 gp worth of rare herbs and fine food, you call forth your companion's spirit and use your magic to create a new body for it. You can return an animal companion to life in this manner even if you do not possess any part of its body.</p><p>If you use this ability to return a former animal companion to life while you have a current animal companion, your current companion leaves you and is replaced by the restored companion.</p><p>If you are small enough to ride it, your companion's initiative changes to match yours and it can any of its actions during your turn or immediately after.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf6c66626ec41cab","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211649,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Indomitable Might","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>If your total for a Strength check or Strength Saving Throw is less than your Strength score, you can use that score in place of the total.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/unarmed-punch-fist-yellow-red.webp","_id":"sf6d352b2e4c7ed9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Order's Wrath","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Enemies you designate for destruction wilt under the combined efforts of you and your allies. If you deal damage to a creature on your turn, you can curse that creature until the start of your next turn. When one of your allies hits the cursed creature with an attack, the target also takes 2d8 psychic damage. You can curse a creature in this way only once per turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf6e711d8f9cfb90","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211624,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Battle Familiar","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your bonded familiar can attack twice, instead of once, whenever it takes the Attack action on its turn. Moreover, it can use any Witchcraft options or spells it gained through your class features that require an Action in place of one of those attacks.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf6fac02ddf406a4","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211679,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Unearthly Recovery","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You gain the ability to overcome grievous injuries. As a Bonus Action, you can regain a number of hit points equal to half your hit point maximum.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you use 6 sorcery points to use it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf7d6de79cbb8b44","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211665,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Warding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Ancient magic lies so heavily upon you that it forms an eldritch ward. You and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you have Resistance to damage from spells.</p><p>At 18th level, the range of this aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8492bca617b5ea","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211646,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Additional Maneuvers (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional maneuvers of your choice.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf857a4d538600e6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211631,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Ethereal Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn to step through the Ethereal Plane. As a Bonus Action, you can cast the etherealness spell with this feature, without expending a spell slot, but the spell lasts only 1 minute. During that time, you can use a Bonus Action to switch from the Etheral Plane to back to the Plane you are currently on or vice versa.</p><p>You use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier and you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8b0f9197802743","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211651,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Elemental Shielding","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You and any allies within your Aura of Protection have Resistance to the damage type associated with the oath patron you have chosen for your Elemental Smite and make any Saving Throw related to them with Advantage: Cold (Marid), Fire (Efreeti), Lightning (Djinni), Poison (Dao).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8dd7f6038cb544","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211647,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Lunar Empowerment","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The power of a lunar phase saturates your being. Whenever you choose a lunar phase to affect your magic, you also gain the following benefit associated with that phase:</p><ul><li><strong>Full Moon:</strong> You shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. In addition, you and creatures of your choice have Advantage on Saving Throws while within the bright light you shed.</li><li><strong>New Moon:</strong> You have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. In addition, while you are in dim light or darkness, Attack Rolls have Disadvantage against you.</li><li><strong>Crescent Moon:</strong> You have Resistance to necrotic and radiant damage</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8e4f40c748bbe7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Fleet Step","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you take a Bonus Action other than Step of the Wind, you can also use Step of the Wind immediately after that Bonus Action.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf8fda9d4f8bdc07","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211642,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mountain Born","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your are acclimatized to cold regions as per the DMG. You also have Resistance to cold damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-vulcano.webp","_id":"sf919f8ec54a4412","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211686,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Farseer","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>The range of your Minor Prophecy increases to 120 feet and you can turn the roll on the D20 into a 7 or 13 (your choice).</p><p>When you roll Initiative, you regain one use of Minor Prophecy.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf93c4014055af19","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211677,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Spirits of Ill Omen","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>6th-level Sorcerer Shadow Magic feature (replaces Hound of Ill Omen)</p><p>You can cast Summon Undead without a Material component. You can also cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a Long Rest. Whenever you start casting the spell, you can modify it so that it doesn't require Concentration. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting, and the spell ends early if you cast it again.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf961345dea04ffa","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dwarven Combat Training","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have Proficiency in light and medium armor as well as the battleaxe, warhammer, light crossbow, and heavy crossbow.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/weapons/hammers/hammer-double-engraved-green.webp","_id":"sf9bd1595c5e6b5e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211688,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Dervish Dance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>While you are wearing light or no armor and using no shield, you can use a Bonus Action to enter the Dervish Dance for 1 minute, gaining the benefits below. It ends early if you are Incapacitated and if you don medium or heavy armor or a shield. You can also end it early (no action required).</p><ul><li>Your Speed increases by 10 feet.</li><li>On each of your turns, you can give all your melee weapon attacks the benefits of the Flurry or Cleave mastery (your choice). These do not limit your use of other masteries on your attacks, but you cannot use the same mastery twice on the same attack.</li><li>You have advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</li><li>Your AC increases by 1 + half your Proficiency (rounded down).</li></ul><p>You can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a Short or a Long Rest. Additionally, you can expend a use of your Second Wind to use it again (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sf9cb76790443ee5","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Eyes in the Dark","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can hide even when in plain view, as long as you are in an area of dim light or darkness. Additionally, you can see normally in darkness, both magical and non-magical, to a distance of 60 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfa2028b20af307d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211659,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Shadow Martyr","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can make your echo throw itself in front of an attack directed at another creature that you can see. Before the Attack Roll is made, you can use your Reaction to teleport the echo to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the targeted creature. The Attack Roll that triggered the Reaction is instead made against your echo.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest or you spend a use of your Second Wind (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfa4fc85912d8ae0","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211633,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Superior Critical","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-axe-blood-red.webp","_id":"sfa5a7dd23f99d3c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211632,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Air Blast","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you gain access to this element, your kinetic shape gains the ability to inflict bludgeoning or lightning damage (your choice).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfa85575cc2288de","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211638,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Improved Brutal Strike","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You have honed new ways to attack furiously. The following effects are now among your Brutal Strike options.</p><ul><li><strong>Staggering Blow.</strong> The target must succeed on a CON Saving Throw or have Disadvantage on the next Saving Throw it makes, and it can't take Bonus Actions or Reactions until the start of your next turn.</li><li><strong>Sundering Blow.</strong> Before the start of your next turn, the next Attack Roll made by another creature against the target gains a +5 bonus to the roll. If the attack hits, the attacker can maximize up to two of its damage dice. An Attack Roll can gain only one Sundering Blow bonus.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/strike-flail-destructive-yellow.webp","_id":"sfb0522939ceadce","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211613,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Extra Attack (3)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can attack four times whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sfbe1a0dae61d9a3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211629,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Bladesinger Styles","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>From its inception as a martial and magical art, Bladesinging has been tied to the sword, more specifically the longsword. Yet many generations of study gave rise to various styles of Bladesinging based on the melee weapon employed. The techniques of these styles are passed from master to students in small schools, some of which have a building dedicated to instruction. Even the newest styles are hundreds of years old, but are still taught by their original creators due to the long lives of elves. Most schools of Bladesinging are in Evermeet or Evereska. One was started in Myth Drannor, but the city's destruction has scattered those students who survived.</p><p>Styles of Bladesinging are broadly categorized based on the type of weapon employed, and each is associated with a category of animal. Within that style are specializations named after specific animal types, based on the types of spells employed, the techniques of the master, and the particular weapon used. Bladesingers who apprentice to a master typically get a tattoo of their chosen style's animal. Some bladesingers learn multiple styles and bear many tattoos, wearing a warning on their skin of their deadly skills.</p><p><strong>Cat.</strong> Styles that employ a sword belong to this family. The lion style, the eldest, trains practitioners in the use of the longsword and doesn't favor any particular type of spells. Leopard style focuses on the shortsword and spells of illusion and stealth. Red tiger, a style just three centuries old, has its bladesingers using the scimitar in a whirling dance of defense from which they launch into sudden leaps and attacks.</p><p><strong>Bird.</strong> Styles that focus on the use of a hafted weapon, such as an axe or hammer, have been grouped together as bird styles, yet they vary wildly. All relatively new styles, they use weapons not typically favored by elves. Eagle-style bladesingers use small handaxes, and many maneuvers in the style focus on fluid ways to throw the weapon and draw a new one. Raven style uses a war pick, and spells associated with it grant the bladesinger more agility in combat.</p><p><strong>Snake.</strong> Practitioners of these styles use a flail, chain, or whip. Viper style uses a whip, despite its inelegance as a weapon, and has almost as long a history as the lion style. Its masters punctuate their bladesong with a stunningly rapid rhythm of whip cracks, which can keep many foes at bay and allow the bladesinger space to cast the cruel spells of poison and disease favored by the style.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfbe2f856dab020b","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211684,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Sculpt Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can create pockets of relative safety within the effects of your evocations. When you cast an Evocation spell that affects other creatures that you can see, you can choose a number of them equal to 1 plus the spell's level. The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their saving throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-dripping-pseudopods-green.webp","_id":"sfc03de82997474d","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211681,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Mantle of Majesty","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You always have the Command spell prepared.</p><p>As a Bonus Action, you cast Command without expending a spell slot, and you take on an unearthly appearance for 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. During this time, you can cast Command as a Bonus Action without expending a spell slot.</p><p>Any creature Charmed by you automatically fails its Saving Throw against the Command you cast with this feature.</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore your use of it by expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required).</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfc855626583513c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211618,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Restorative Reagents","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:</p><ul><li>Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).</li><li>You can cast Lesser Restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you have alchemist's supplies on your person. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</li></ul>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/laboratory/bowl-herbs-green.webp","_id":"sfca72dde869f6ae","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211610,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Aura of Alacrity","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You emanate an aura that fills you and your companions with supernatural speed, allowing you to race across a battlefield in formation. Your Speed increases by 10 feet. In addition, if you aren't Incapacitated, the Speed of any ally who starts their turn within 10 feet of you increases by 10 feet until the end of that turn.</p><p>When you reach 18th level in this class, the range of the aura increases to 30 feet.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcc79b3c1e38d5c","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211648,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Enchanted Strikes","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Unarmed Strikes count as magical for the purpose of overcoming Resistance and Immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcc8c129b336ee8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211617,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Serene Mind","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You make Wisdom Saving Throws with Advantage and when you use Self-Restoration, you can also remove the Confused condition.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfcccfd8ca72e416","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211643,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamagic","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Because your magic flows from within, you can alter your spells to suit your needs; you gain two Metamagic options of your choice from the list below. You use the chosen options to temporarily modify spells you cast. To use an option, you must spend the number of Sorcery Points that it costs.</p><p>You can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it unless otherwise noted in one of those options.</p><p>When you finish a Short or a Long Rest you can replace one metamagic you know with another one. You gain two more options at Sorcerer level 10 and two more at Sorcerer level 17.</p><h5>Careful Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that forces other creatures to make a Saving Throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the spell's full force. To do so, you spend 1 sorcery point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their Saving Throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Distant Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a range of 5 feet or greater, you can spend 1 sorcery point to double the range of the spell.</p><p>When you cast a spell that has a range of touch, you can spend 1 sorcery point to make the range of the spell 30 feet.</p><h5>Empowered Spell</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll a number of the damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You must use the new rolls.</p><p>You can use Empowered Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Extended Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a duration of 1 minute or longer, you can spend 1 sorcery point to double its duration, to a maximum duration of 24 hours.</p><p>If the affected spell requires Concentration, you have Advantage on any Saving Throw you make to maintain that Concentration.</p><h5>Heightened Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that forces a creature to make a Saving Throw to resist its effects, you can spend 2 sorcery points to give one target of the spell Disadvantage on all its Saving Throws made against the spell.</p><h5>Maximized Spell</h5><p>When you roll damage for a spell, you can spend 2 sorcery points and choose a number damage dice up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). You maximize the rolled result for the chosen dice.</p><p>You can use Maximized Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Quickened Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that has a casting time of an Action, you can spend 2 Sorcery Points to change the casting time to a Bonus Action for this casting. You can't modify a spell in this way if you've already cast a level 1+ spell on the current turn, nor can you cast a level 1+ spell on this turn after modifying a spell in this way.</p><h5>Seeking Spell</h5><p>If you make an Attack Roll for a spell and miss, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll the d20, and you must use the new roll.</p><p>You can use Seeking Spell even if you have already used a different Metamagic option during the casting of the spell.</p><h5>Subtle Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell, you can spend 1 sorcery point to cast it without any somatic, verbal and material components, unless that material component has a cost or is consumed by the spell.</p><h5>Twinned Spell</h5><p>When you cast a spell that targets only one creature and doesn't have a range of self, you can spend a number of sorcery points equal to the spell's level to target a second creature in range with the same spell (1 sorcery point if the spell is a cantrip).</p><p>To be eligible, a spell must be incapable of targeting more than one creature at the spell's current level. For example, Magic Missile and Scorching Ray aren't eligible, but Ray of Frost and Chromatic Orb are.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-colllecting-energy-green.webp","_id":"sfcd507fc5acccb2","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211662,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Projected Ward","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When a creature that you can see within 30 feet of yourself takes damage, you can take a Reaction to cause your Arcane Ward to absorb that damage. If this damage reduces the ward to 0 Hit Points, the warded creature takes any remaining damage. If that creature has any Resistances or Vulnerabilities, apply them before reducing the ward's Hit Points.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfd5978fda2c6d3a","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211680,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Coven of Alleyways Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>At each indicated Witch level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Coven of Alleyways Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Witch Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Disguise Self, Expeditious Retreat, Detect Thoughts, Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Meld into Stone, Tongues</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Greater Invisibility, Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Mislead, Passwall</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfde93fae78bfc97","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211676,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Veteran Field Commander","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you give your Bonus Action or Reaction to an ally, you can target two allies instead of one. You can do so only once per turn. </p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/skills/melee/spear-tips-triple-orange.webp","_id":"sfdf5e33fe897c2e","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211674,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Gravity Well","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You've learned how to manipulate gravity around a living being: whenever you cast a spell on a creature, you can move the target up to 10 feet to an unoccupied space of your choice if the target is willing to move, the spell hits it with an attack, or it fails a Saving Throw against the spell.</p><p>Upon reaching 10th level in this class, the maximum distance you can move a creature in this manner increases to 20 ft.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sfe546abcde57f25","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211683,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Flash of Genius","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails an ability check or a saving throw, you can take a Reaction to add a bonus to the roll, potentially causing it to succeed. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).</p><p>You can take this Reaction a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"reaction","cost":1,"condition":"when you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails an Ability Check or a Saving Throw"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","per":"lr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"max(1, @abilities.int.mod)","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/light/explosion-star-glow-silhouette.webp","_id":"sfeb057e0d1f9fb6","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Tool Expertise","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>Your Proficiency bonus is doubled for any Ability Check you make that uses your Proficiency with a tool.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/tools/hand/hammer-backing-steel.webp","_id":"sff5ca00338b4cd3","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211609,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Brand of Castigation","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite, you can channel hemocraft magic to sear an arcane brand into that creature (no action required). You always know the direction to the branded creature as long as it's on the same plane as you. Further, each time a branded creature deals damage to you or forces you to make a Saving Throw, it takes psychic damage equal to your Hemocraft modifier.</p><p>Your brand lasts until you dismiss it or until you use this feature to apply a brand to another creature. Your brand can be dispelled with Dispel Magic, and is treated as a spell with a level equal to half your blood hunter level (maximum 9th level).</p><p>Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a Short or a Long Rest - or until you spend a use of your Blood Maledict to regain it.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"special","cost":null,"condition":"when you damage a creature with a weapon for which you have an active crimson rite"},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":1,"max":1,"per":"sr","recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":1},"ability":null,"actionType":"util","attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[["max(1, @abilities.int.mod, @abilities.wis.mod)","psychic"]],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/symbols/rune-sigil-hook-white-red.webp","_id":"sff8f0c1d1c097c7","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211619,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Relentless Endurance","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>When you are reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 hit point instead. You can't use this feature again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/control/control-influence-rally-purple.webp","_id":"sffc88598de85c43","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211687,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Cryomancer Spells","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn additional spells when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown on the table below. Each of these spells counts as a sorcerer spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of sorcerer spells you know.</p><div style=\"width: 100%;\"><table style=\"width: 100%;\"><caption>Cryomancer Spells</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Sorcerer Level</th><th scope=\"col\">Spells</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Armor of Agathys, Ice Knife, Rime's Binding Ice, Snilloc's Snowball Swarm</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Sleet Storm, Water Walk</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Ice Storm, Stoneskin</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Cone of Cold, Conjure Elemental</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","_id":"sffd6df1fa2a33f9","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211667,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
{"name":"Metamagic (Level 10)","type":"feat","system":{"description":{"value":"<p>You learn two additional metamagic options.</p>","chat":"","unidentified":""},"source":"","activation":{"type":"","cost":null,"condition":""},"duration":{"value":"","units":""},"cover":null,"crewed":false,"target":{"value":null,"width":null,"units":"","type":""},"range":{"value":null,"long":null,"units":""},"uses":{"value":null,"max":"","per":null,"recovery":""},"consume":{"type":"","target":null,"amount":null},"ability":null,"actionType":null,"attackBonus":"","chatFlavor":"","critical":{"threshold":null,"damage":""},"damage":{"parts":[],"versatile":""},"formula":"","save":{"ability":"","dc":null,"scaling":"spell"},"type":{"value":"","subtype":""},"requirements":"","recharge":{"value":null,"charged":null}},"img":"icons/magic/unholy/orb-colllecting-energy-green.webp","_id":"sffe38df84d8ffa8","_stats":{"systemId":"dnd5e","systemVersion":"2.4.9","coreVersion":"10.303","createdTime":1777072572464,"modifiedTime":1777110211663,"lastModifiedBy":"dnd5ebuilder0000"},"flags":{},"sort":0}
